wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "quote": "## The kit vehicle this model is built from: the author's", "problem": "Vocabulary: CONTEXT.md lists 'vehicle' under Unit's Avoid terms. The new docs use it for the author's kit models: kit_unit_model.gd line 3 'one of the author's concept-kit vehicles', line 46 (this quote); kit_merge.gd line 3-4 'one of the author's concept-kit vehicles' (low; the assets/art/vehicles path itself is the author's and stays).", "fix": "Write 'concept-kit model' / 'kit model' in prose in both files and keep the res://assets/art/vehicles/... path literal as it is."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/canister/water_canister.gd", "quote": "## zone. It", "problem": "Ragged doc wrap left by the edit: the class doc's first paragraph now ends one line early with a one-word line ('a touch' / '## zone. It' / '## holds where it is ...'). Nit.", "fix": "Re-wrap lines 3-7 as one paragraph of at most 100 columns, '...a small water tank in its owner's colour and a touch zone. It holds where it is (at home, carried, dropped) and the Unit carrying it, and nothing else.'"}], "measurements": [{"ac": "FROZEN", "what": "the 9 frozen files, shasum -a 256 -c frozen.sha256 (same as dev07.py frozen)", "value": "9 of 9 OK", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "base.tscn, greybox_field.tscn, terrain_stand_ins.tscn, greybox_fuel_cans.tscn, player_1_body_material.tres, player_2_body_material.tres, project.godot, assets/ unchanged", "value": "git status empty for all of them", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "STD", "what": "lint007.py all: ## lines over 100 columns; declarations without a ## above", "value": "0 and 0", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "STD", "what": "lint007.py: functions over 40 lines or cc 10 (3 reported), confirmed by reading", "value": "0 confirmed: kit_merge._commit is 16 lines (the lint's window runs through the inner classes, comment words inflate cc); base._rea