nister.gd/.tscn, fuel_can.gd/.tscn, split_screen.gd/.tscn, greybox_field.gd, unit.gd (look touched none of it: _swap_model and _paint_team_colour unchanged), player_hud.gd, unit_choice.gd/.tscn, the UI edge and Team material files, all 16 map materials and 2 of the 9 textures (the 9 diffed byte-identical against the preflight recipes), compound_base.tscn, map_01_dressing.tscn, the runner's diff, and map_fps.gd, map_legibility.gd, map_showcase.gd. Provenance of the look's own edits came from file mtimes against the design-look time and the scratch pre-look snapshot of map_kit.gd, which showed the only look edit outside the DESIGN's list (map_kit.gd); design/rules.md and the story file predate the look. The runner's TD-009 key re-assertion, watchdog constant and greybox composition are the layout design's (it names TD-009); the look's share is the registrations, GREYBOX_MODELS and the Player body materials, all named. Lint counts were each confirmed by reading (see measurements). Not covered: no Godot run, so parse, regress, the five map scenarios, windowed frames and draw calls are NOT_VERIFIED here; map_01_terrain, water, cliffs, cover and depot scenes (layout files) were only spot-checked for the look's restyle (depot uses steel, rust and dark steel materials, never red; map_01.tscn instances the dressing). A /tech-debt skill block with no subcommand accompanied the task; it was not run and nothing was written to docs/tech-debt-register.md."}
