{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DEFECT", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "quote": "lead = (origin - _last_origin) / delta * rise_lead_seconds", "problem": "The rise looks ahead only along the Unit's straight-line motion of the last tick (lines 126-131 and 145-147: hull footprint stretched by that lead). It cannot see rock the hull reaches from a standstill or by turning, so the model's lowest point is INSIDE the rock for some ticks, against the design's 'early enough that no part of the model is ever inside rock'. Measured on the real Map 01 (Gyrocopter on a probe copy driven by set_drive_input, headless --fixed-fps 60; hull footprint sampled against the CSG polygons AND a physics slab query at the model's lowest plane, both agree): STANDING START straight at the canyon-south face z=-20 from rest, gap hull-to-face 0.00/0.10/0.25/0.50 m -> 12/6/4/2 ticks inside rock, lowest point up to 1.12/0.52/0.32/0.12 m below the rock top; gap 1.0 m -> 0 inside (clearance 0.18); gap >=1.5 m -> clean. TURN INTO A FACE at top speed 16.4 m/s flying along the same face with lateral clearance 0.3/0.8/1.5 m then full steer into it -> 8/4/1 ticks inside rock, up to 0.72/0.32/0.02 m below the top; 3.0 m clean; turning away never rises (control). Straight crossings are clean: canyon road along z=-26 across all bends, canyon S-to-N, ridge at x=-70/0/70, oblique canyon, lateral entries from a channel at 4.8 m gap: min clearance exactly 0.250 m, 0 inside ticks, rise 1.470 m already on the first rock tick, camera ray clear of layer 32 on every rock tick, back to hover (model y 0.800) on sand, collider shape/offset/layer/mask unchanged, Unit y max 0.001. Windowed captures at the first violating tick (scratch rise-frames/chase.png, side_from_outside.png, oblique.png) show a short, small clip of the lower body against the rock face (4-12 ticks, 0.07-0.2 s), so the visual cost is low; the design sentence is still not met.", "fix": "Pad the query box horizontally on every side, not only along the motion: in _rise_target() widen low/high by a margin before sizing _rise_box (new export rise_margin, e.g. 2.0 m, set on gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn only; the model still rises as a visual offset only). Then rerun the scratch probes: godot --headless --fixed-fps 60 --path <repo> -s <scratch>/look/lens-runtime/probe_stand.gd and probe_turn.gd: every RUN must show inside_rock_ticks(sample)=0 and slab_ticks=0 for every gap and lateral distance, and probe_rise.gd must still end at rise 0.000 / model y 0.800 over open sand and over both channels."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn", "quote": "model_scale = 0.735", "problem": "The hull of two kit models is not inside its collider footprint, measured from the built meshes (KitMerge.Built.hull x model_scale + position, Unit frame) against the UnitStats collider: Truck hull z[-2.330..2.073] against collider z[-2.200..2.200] -> the nose stands 0.130 m beyond the collider front (the 4.40 m length fits, the centring does not, and the scene has no offset); Motorbike hull z[-1.242..1.360] against z[-1.300..1.300] -> tail 0.060 m beyond (the design's own accepted figure, the 1.36 tail tip); Buggy overshoot 0.001 m; Gyrocopter hull overshoot 0.005 m (its rotor, above the 2.0 m hull line, spans x +-2.22 m by design). The Truck's nose therefore pokes 0.13 m into a wall or cover its collider stops against.", "fix": "Centre the Truck's hull on its collider the way the design does for the Gyrocopter: truck_kit_model.tscn offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.129) (hull then z[-2.20..2.20]); optionally motorbike_kit_model.tscn offset = Vector3(0, 0, -0.059) (hull z[-1.30..1.30]; this also only improves the Flag's tail clearance). Re-measure with the scratch probe_models.gd FOOT_HULL lines: overshoot z must read 0.000."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "lens 5 / regression", "what": "dev07.py regress (24 baselines on the greybox composition)", "value": "ALL_OK=True: the strict twenty byte