ver sand; over both channels 2295 ticks at rise 0.000; collider box, offset, layer 16, mask 1 unchanged; Unit y max 0.0010", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "lens 3 / AC-13 design sentence", "what": "Gyrocopter rise from a standstill or a turn near a face", "value": "standing start gap 0.0-0.5 m: 2-12 ticks inside rock, up to 1.12 m below the top; turn into a face at 16.4 m/s with 0.3-1.5 m lateral clearance: 1-8 ticks, up to 0.72 m below the top (issue 1)", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "lens 4", "what": "first textured frame of a windowed run (real main scene added before the first frame, root viewport captured at the first frame_post_draw, 12 frames, frames 0 and 11 read)", "value": "nine NoiseTexture2D files have an image at the first drawn frame (9/9); 0 magenta, 0 near-black of 230400 sampled pixels in every frame; frame 0 and frame 11 look identical, textured sand, rust garage floor, scrap and dark walls, Team-coloured towers, HUD and choice panels with Orange and Teal edges", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14 (side measure)", "what": "draw calls of a windowed main-scene frame, both views together, before the Round (Units benched)", "value": "299 in the first frames, 267-270 with a Unit spawned; budget 1,000", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "windowed frame rate of a driven run", "value": "not measured by this lens (map_fps belongs to the orchestrator)", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "lens 4", "what": "first frames of a real project launch with --write-movie, and two more windowed respawn-timing samples", "value": "the run was refused by the permission system and not retried; the -s probe frames stand for it (same scene added before the first frame)", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Read-only runtime review of Story 007's look on Godot 4.7.2 (Metal, macOS), all Godot runs one at a time with timeouts, nothing written to the repo (git status line count unchanged at 60; probes, frames and logs under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-runtime/: probe_models.gd, probe_rise.gd, probe_stand.gd, probe_stand2.gd, probe_turn.gd, probe_cap.gd, probe_main.gd, probe_warm.gd, probe_first.gd, probe_kits.gd, run_probe.py, main-frames/, rise-frames/). Covered: (1) windowed build times and cache, first spawn and ten respawns of each type, leak counts, warm-up order and silence; (2) all four kit models headless, painting through the real Unit.spawn() with both Team materials, surfaces, scales, hovers, hull vs collider footprint, the kit palettes against the Team colours; (3) the Gyrocopter rise on the real Map 01 (about 30 runs: straight crossings at top speed over every canyon bend, wall and ridge, channel runs, lateral entries, standing starts at 0.0-4.0 m, turns into a face at 0.3-3.0 m lateral clearance, a turn-away control), with polygon-sampled and physics-slab inside-rock tests, a chase-camera ray, the collider before and after, and windowed images of the clip read; (4) the first textured frame windowed (9/9 textures ready, 0 magenta, frames read); (5) dev07 regress ALL_OK, the five map scenarios, launch, frozen, assets. Two issues: the rise's look-ahead misses a standstill or a turn near a face (DEFECT, low visual cost), and the Truck/Motorbike hulls overshoot their colliders (DESIGN, low). Not verified: real-launch --write-movie frames, repeat respawn samples (command refused), and the windowed frame rate (AC-14 fps) and AC-15, which are not this lens's.\""}
