{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "AC_UNMET", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/textures/sea.tres", "quote": "legibility_channel_gyrocopters_f68.png(295, 200, 345, 240) teal n= 68 obj_med=(26, 103, 110) bg_med=(51, 74, 103) dE76 med=23.7 p90=47.0", "problem": "AC-13 asks for the Gyrocopter of either Team colour over salt water. At 38 m (cam1_to_p2=38.0), P2's Teal Gyrocopter over the channel differs from the water by a median dE76 of only 23.7, which is under the ~25 bar. The design's 'Teal over it measured dE 44 to 46' holds only for the lit side (p90 here is 47). A chase camera that faces the Sun sees the Team accent's shaded side, sRGB (26,103,110), and that is close to the channel's navy (51,74,103). PNG: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/legibility_channel_gyrocopters_f68.png (left view, the far Gyrocopter at about x 320, y 222).", "fix": "Darken the shared water ramp in sea.tres (channel.tres uses the same one by design) so the channel renders at about L* 20 or below, e.g. about (0.04, 0.12, 0.24) instead of (0.07, 0.20, 0.35). Then re-measure with map_legibility. This departs from DESIGN 2's named navy recipe, so the orchestrator decides. The alternative is to record 23.7 (shaded) and 47 (lit p90) in the evidence doc as a known marginal pair for the author's AC-15 judgement."}, {"kind": "DEFECT", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd", "quote": "print(\"SPLIT %s t=%.3f frame=%d phase=%s %s %s round=%s\" % [_harness.scenario, _harness.time(), Engine.get_process_frames(),", "problem": "On every moment= line, frame=N names the first PNG of the NEXT staging, not the moment itself. The md5 of frames N-2 and N-1 match (that is the hold) and frame N differs. Showcase: garage_spawn 124 (9ad4dc 9ad4dc then 70eff6), under_towers 190, gates 256, depot 652, fords 718. map_legibility.gd line 180 has the same print: there, frame N for sand (362), salt_flat (422) and canyon_road (482) is md5-identical to the next moment's hold. Its doc line 14 ('frame= (in a --write-movie run the number of the next PNG)') points at that wrong frame. Visual proof, in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/: showcase_garage_spawn_f123.png shows the Units in the Garage, but showcase_garage_spawn_f124.png (the PNG that 'garage_spawn frame=124' names) already shows them under the water towers. Likewise, frame=652 'depot' names showcase_frame_eq_652_shows_fords_staging_not_depot.png. An orchestrator that retains the PNG frame= names gets the wrong staging for every moment.", "fix": "On moment= lines, print the hold's last PNG, Engine.get_process_frames() - 1, or print the moment line on the tick before the next staging moves the Units. Do this in map_showcase.gd line 260 and map_legibility.gd line 180, and change both class docs to say 'the number of the PNG that shows the moment'. Until then, the retained set must use frame-1. The lens-visual showcase_*_f(N-1).png and legibility_*_f(N-1).png files are those frames."}, {"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_legibility.gd", "quote": "SPLIT map_legibility t=1.100 frame=69 phase=channel_gyrocopters moment=channel_gyrocopters cam1_to_p2=38.0 cam1_to_can=24.0 cam2_to_p1=38.0 ... p1_x=-40.00 p1_z=20.50 ... p2_x=-40.00 p2_z=44.83", "problem": "AC-13 asks for the Gyrocopter of EITHER Team colour over salt water, but only Teal is shown over it at 40 m. P1's Orange Gyrocopter at z 20.50 sits at the ford/channel junction. cam2 looks north at it from 38 m and sees it against the bright ford (background (165,232,249), dE 91), not the channel. PNG: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/legibility_channel_gyrocopters_f68.png (right view). Computed from colours measured in other frames, Orange vs the channel would be dE 82 lit and 69 shaded, so it should pass, but no frame shows it.", "fix": "Re-stage the channel_gyrocopters moment so that, in cam2's line of sight, the ground about 8 m behind P1's Gyrocopter is channel water. For example, put P1 deeper in the channel (z about 28 or more) and move P2 so that cam2_to_p1 stays about 40 m. Until then, record the Orange-over-salt-water pair in the evidence doc as computed, not observed."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/canister/water_canister.tscn", "quote": "a Team-coloured cylindrical body (the body_mesh apply_color() paints) of radius at most 0.30 m (so at the Motorbike's unchanged carry_offset (0, 0.5, 1.7) its near edge, z 1.40, clears the kit Motorbike's tail tip", "problem": "When a Motorbike carries the enemy Flag, the ~1 m Flag at carry_offset z +1.7 sits between the chase camera and the Motorbike. The carrier's own Team-colour pixels in its chase box fall from at least 221 (frames 63-123) to 14 (frame 1887). There are 130 Team pixels in total, almost all of them the other Team's Flag. So from its own camera, the Orange Motorbike reads as a Teal barrel with a cream dot. The cream cue stays visible: 60 px on every frame from 1878 to 1939, the same as uncarried, so AC-12 holds. AC-13's 'no rock, wall, tank or roof comes between a camera and its Unit' names the bends, the towers and the Garages, not carrying. PNGs: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/showcase_flag_carried_own_colour_hidden_f1887.png and showcase_flags_taken_f1938.png.", "fix": "No change in this story: the design fixes carry_offset and the Flag's ~1 m height. Record this in the evidence doc for the author's AC-15 judgement, so the author can decide later on a shorter body or a different carry_offset."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-10", "what": "First frame textured (main scene, the Round's start, both views)", "value": "f0: sand, salt, rock, Garage floor, Team towers and HUD all textured or coloured; lens-visual/showcase_first_f0.png", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Magenta (missing-resource) pixels, every 6th pixel of every frame", "value": "0 in all 1940 map_showcase frames and 543 map_legibility frames", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Top-down (--width=330) beside design/source/map01_colored.png", "value": "Island, north canyon with the road, cracked salt flat, light-cyan fords, navy channels (open question 16), darker ridge, Bases with Team corner towers, dashed rectangle, rust Garage, olive containers, tyre stacks, depot (3 grey tanks, pale ring, 6 dark posts, 5 red Cans) and boulders all follow the drawing; lens-visual/topdown_map01_w330.png, topdown_baseA.png, topdown_depot.png", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Z-fighting or visible repetition in the frames read (about 35 frames); flicker in static holds", "value": "None seen; static holds are md5-identical frame to frame (e.g. 122=123, 188=189, 650=651)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Shimmer under camera motion", "value": "Not measurable from stills; nothing seen in the road and gyro frames", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Each Unit in one Team colour (units_team_cam0/2 beside vehicle-design.png)", "value": "8 models, each one Team colour with neutral darks; opposite-colour pixels in a box only where a neighbouring model, Flag or Can overlaps it; Buggy pennant is the owner's colour", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Bases and UI wear their Team colour; walls dark, Garage rust", "value": "Base A: Orange corner towers, dashed rectangle and tank; Base B: Teal. HUD band and choice-panel edges: Orange on the left view, Teal on the right. Fuel amber vs Orange edge: dE76 36", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Neutral things vs Team colours and the Fuel Can red", "value": "Lit canyon rock vs Orange: dE 27 (shaded Orange: 14). Base B Garage floor vs Orange: 32 (17). Cover is rust, posts dark steel, tanks grey. Red appears only on Cans; the red above the Truck in f880 is the road's Fuel Can 6 m ahead", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Cream heading cue pixels at 13 m, with and without a carried Flag", "value": "60 px uncarried (f123); 60 px carried on every frame 1878-1939 in both views", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12/AC-13", "what": "Water tower in view, not hidden, from the salt flat's four corners and its centre, both views", "value": "Visible in f321 (NW), f387 (SW), f453 (NE), f519 (SE) and f585 (centre); lens-visual/showcase_towers_*.png", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over sand (dE76: object median vs local background)", "value": "Teal 54-57, Orange 36-40, Can red 57-61; Orange-Red 26-37, Teal-Red 81-97, Teal-Orange 71-92", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over the salt flat", "value": "Teal 43-55, Orange 40-67, Red 61-85", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over the canyon road", "value": "Orange Unit at 40 m 28.4 (p90 32.1), Teal 57.5, Red 43.7-54.2; at 13 m: Orange 28-33 (marginal)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over a ford", "value": "Teal 27-40, Orange 81-89, Red 93-94", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Teal Gyrocopter over salt water (channel) at 38 m", "value": "median dE76 23.7, p90 47 (shaded Teal (26,103,110) vs channel (51,74,103))", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Orange Gyrocopter over salt water at 40 m", "value": "Not staged: seen over the ford (dE 91). Over the channel at 13 m: 60. Computed vs channel: 69-82", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Gyrocopter visible on every frame crossing the canyon wall and ridge (Team pixels per frame, frames 1462-1708)", "value": "Min 155/143 (wide box) and 86/77 (chase box); never 0. Over rock: Orange dE 27.7-42.9, Teal 43.7-44.2", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Unit not hidden from its own camera on the canyon road's bends (frames 760-1395)", "value": "Own-colour pixels min 661 (P1) / 240 (P2); 0 frames below 25", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Unit not hidden appearing in a Garage and under a water tower", "value": "Garage (frames 63-123): min 221/492 px. Under tower (frames 124-189): min 109/109 px", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "map_fps windowed 1280x720, run 1 (first second left out)", "value": "fps_min_steady=120.0, fps_avg_steady=120.0, draw_calls_max=257, primitives_max=173084 (both views, RENDER_TOTAL_DRAW_CALLS_IN_FRAME); legs flat_and_road:ok, into_bases:ok", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "map_fps windowed 1280x720, run 2 back to back", "value": "fps_min_steady=120.0, draw_calls_max=258, primitives_max=176168 (refresh 120 Hz)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1..AC-9", "what": "regress, new (5 map scenarios), frozen, assets", "value": "Outside this lens; not run by me", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "This was the windowed visual and cost lens, retry run.\n\nI reused the previous attempt's windowed runs, which are still valid for this tree: no file under src/, tools/, assets/ or project.godot changed after 00:13, and the runs were made 01:06-01:13 with Godot 4.7.2 on Metal at 1280x720. They are map_showcase and map_legibility with --write-movie (1940 and 543 frames), map_fps twice back to back, the top-down snapshot at --width=330 plus the two Bases and the depot, and the four Units in both Team colours.\n\nI read about 35 frames: f0, garage f123/f124, under_towers, gates, the four corner tower views and the centre one, depot, fords, two road bends, both gyro-over-rock frames, gyro_end, flags_taken f1887/f1938, the legibility frames for the canyon road and the channel, the top-down, the Base A and depot top-downs, and the units renders. I compared them with design/source/map01_colored.png and assets/art/vehicles/vehicle-design.png.\n\nMeasurements:\n- dE76, computed with a pure-python PNG sampler (px.py, legib.py, de_far.py, mix.py in lens-visual/).\n- Per-frame Team, cream and magenta pixel counts over every movie frame, from a headless Godot in a scratch project (lens-visual/gdproj, never --path to the repo; my own child processes only, with timeouts, none left running, no window opened in this retry).\n- md5 of frames around each frame= value.\n\nNew PNGs are saved in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/ as showcase_towers_south_west_f387.png, showcase_towers_north_east_f453.png, showcase_towers_south_east_f519.png, showcase_flag_carried_own_colour_hidden_f1887.png and showcase_frame_eq_652_shows_fords_staging_not_depot.png. The full movies are in movie_showcase/ and movie_legibility/.\n\nFindings:\n- One marginal AC-13 legibility pair: the Teal Gyrocopter over a channel at 38 m is dE 23.7.\n- One scenario defect: frame= on moment= lines names the next staging's PNG; use frame-1.\n- One evidence gap: the Orange Gyrocopter is never shown over salt water at 40 m.\n- One design observation for the author: a carried Flag hides the carrier's own colour from its camera, while the cream cue stays visible.\n\nEverything else I checked holds:\n- AC-10: textured first frame, no magenta, follows the drawing.\n- AC-11: one Team colour per model and Base, UI edges, amber told apart from Orange.\n- AC-12: the Flag, the cream cue while carrying, the towers as landmarks from all five salt-flat positions.\n- AC-13: no Unit hidden on the bends, in the Garage, under the towers or crossing rock.\n- AC-14: fps_min_steady 120, at most 258 draw calls for both views, against a budget of 1000.\n\nNot covered by this lens: regress, new map scenarios, frozen, assets, lint, code standards, shimmer under motion, and per-scene MeshInstance3D counts (not needed, since the draw-call budget is far from its limit)."}
