{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_legibility.gd", "quote": "## over that surface the other Team's Unit, the Flag it carries (the viewer's own) and a Fuel Can.", "problem": "AC-13 asks that a Flag, a Fuel Can and a Unit of either Team colour are told apart at 40 m over sand, salt flat, canyon road and ford. The frames this scenario stages cannot show that. In all four surface moments (lens-visual/movie_legibility/f00000361.png sand, f00000420.png salt flat, f00000480.png canyon road, f00000542.png ford; log: flag1=CARRIED flag2=CARRIED), the only Flag at 40 m rides on the only Unit at 40 m. So the far figure is a roughly 10 px mix of the Unit's colour and the viewer's own Flag colour. No frame shows a Flag standing on the ground, or an unladen Unit of either colour, at 40 m from a chase camera over sand, road or ford. The only unladen Units on record are on the salt flat, in lens-visual/units_team_cam0-2.png, which were not taken from a chase camera. The near carrier does not help either: seen from 13 m behind, the Flag hides almost all of the Motorbike (k4/frames/cue_flag_crop.png), so it reads as the enemy's colour.", "fix": "In map_legibility.gd, hold each SURFACES moment with the Flags off the Units. Stand the viewer's Flag on the ground beside its Can, either moved as a staging step the way CAN_PATHS moves the Cans (and put back on its seat at the end), or dropped by its carrier's Self-destruct key if the Flag rules leave it where its carrier was destroyed. Leave the other Team's Unit unladen. Each view then shows a Flag, a Fuel Can and a Unit as three separate objects about 40 m away. Re-run the scenario and read the four surface PNGs."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"CylinderMesh\" id=\"CylinderMesh_tank\"] ... top_radius = 4.0 / bottom_radius = 4.0 / height = 5.0 (no radial_segments; water_canister.tscn CylinderMesh_body / _band / _stand and SphereMesh_lid likewise)", "problem": "Polish, not blocking. The water tower's tank, platform, band and roof, and the Flag's body, bands, stand and lid, all use the CylinderMesh/SphereMesh defaults: 64 radial segments, smooth. So the two most important Team-coloured objects render as smooth, perfectly round cylinders (lens-visual/movie_showcase/f00000189.png, f00000324.png; k4/frames/cue_flag_crop.png). Everything around them is faceted: the kit Units, the 12-sided depot posts and the 7-sided boulders in map_01_dressing.tscn. This is the one place the Map leaves AC-10's 'flat-shaded low-poly' language, and the author will see it next to the concept sheet.", "fix": "Set radial_segments = 12, matching the depot posts, with few rings (cylinders rings = 0; the lid and roof spheres about rings = 3). Apply it to CylinderMesh_tank, CylinderMesh_platform, CylinderMesh_band and SphereMesh_roof in compound_base.tscn, and to CylinderMesh_body, CylinderMesh_band, CylinderMesh_stand and SphereMesh_lid in water_canister.tscn. Do the same for the depot's fuel-tank cylinders in map_01_depot.tscn if they are at the default. 12 is a multiple of 4, so the outermost vertices stay on the axes: the meshes' bounds and the Flag's 0.30 m near edge do not change. Then re-run regress and the five map scenarios."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Palette against design/source/map01_colored.png (ground, rock, ridge, salt flat, water, Bases, cover, depot, dressing) and assets/art/vehicles/vehicle-design.png (Units); built-in meshes and code textures", "value": "Follows the drawing. Sand and road warm; canyon rock rust with the ridge darker, as drawn; salt flat cream and cracked; fords light cyan; walls dark; Garage rust; depot tanks grey steel; black tyres; olive ribbed containers. Departures the record sanctions: navy sea (OQ16), Team-coloured towers (OQ5), neutral cover and posts (OQ16). Departures it does not: the cover is one rust box texture throughout, and the tank and Flag are smooth 64-segment cylinders (issue). Frames: topdown_map01_w330.png, f00000324.png, f00001003.png, f00000654.png.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Team colour ownership: Units, corner towers, tanks, dashed rectangles, Flags, HUD and choice edges, and nothing neutral", "value": "Each Unit is one Team colour plus dark and bone neutrals; the Buggy's pennant takes its own Team colour (k4/frames/sheet_types.png, units_team_cam0-2.png). Towers, tanks, markings and Flags are Team-coloured (f00000123.png, topdown_baseA.png). HUD and choice edges are 3 px in Team colour (k5/frames/final_choice.png). Dressing colours: the container tint (0.55,1,0.9) on the scrap texture renders olive; rubber 0.07; posts use tower steel; boulders use rock. Nothing neutral is in Orange or Teal.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Fuel amber told apart from Orange in a frame from each viewport", "value": "The amber bar (0.96,0.70,0.18) sits beside the orange edge (0.90,0.45,0.14) and in front of the orange tank, and reads yellower in the left view (f00000189.png, f00000123.png). The teal view shows the same bar for comparison.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Fuel Can red unmistakable, wears no Team colour", "value": "Color(0.78,0.08,0.10), cap and handle dark. Reads pure red, never orange, on sand, salt, road and ford (f00000361.png, f00000480.png, f00000540.png), and as a red tick at 40 m. Seen edge-on at the depot the Cans are thin red sticks, but still red (k6/frames/after_depot.png).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Flag look and the Motorbike's cream cue while carrying", "value": "Team body r 0.28, steel bands r 0.30, 0.94 m tall with lid and stand. Reads as a small echo of the tower's tank and unlike any prop. The cream tank-top cue stays visible above a carried Flag: 38-60 px per frame from frame 1860 on (count_movie_showcase_cream.log; k4/frames/cue_flag_crop.png).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Water tower as the Base landmark at the Flag's seat", "value": "Tank r 4.0 x 5.0 m at y 8.3-13.3, platform bottom y 8.0, braces at y 3.33 or higher. Reads as a classic water tower over the Flag (f00000189.png), and as the Base's landmark from the salt flat (f00000324.png, k3/frames2/tower_far_corner.png, f00000588.png).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "A Flag, a Fuel Can and a Unit of either Team colour told apart at 40 m over sand, salt flat, canyon road and ford", "value": "Not shown. Every staged 40 m Unit carries the viewer's Flag (movie_legibility f00000361/420/480/542); see issue.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Gyrocopter of either Team colour over salt water", "value": "movie_legibility f00000060.png: the Teal Gyrocopter over the navy channel and the Orange one over the channel and ford, at about 38 m, both readable.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Gyrocopter visible over the canyon walls and ridge; no Unit hidden at a Garage, under a tower or on the road's bends (frames only)", "value": "Both Gyrocopters hover visibly above the rock (f00001560.png, f00001620.png, f00001705.png). The Unit is clear in the Garage (f00000123.png), between the tower legs below the braces (f00000189.png) and on the bend (f00001003.png). The visual and runtime lenses own the tick-level ray checks.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11/AC-12", "what": "Unit silhouettes distinct by type from the chase camera", "value": "From behind at 13 m (k4/frames/sheet_types.png): single-track bike with cream patch; open-cage Buggy with pennant; boxy Truck with launcher; Gyrocopter rotor line with tail. All four are distinct in both colours.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "Frame rate and draw calls", "value": "Not in this lens (no Godot run)", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-15", "what": "Coherence judgement", "value": "The author's call; notes are in checked", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Art-direction lens. I worked read-only and ran no Godot.\n\n**What I read**\n- The drawings: design/source/map01_colored.png and assets/art/vehicles/vehicle-design.png.\n- Visual lens frames: topdown_map01_w330, topdown_baseA, topdown_depot and units_team_cam0/1/2.\n- movie_showcase: f123 (garage_spawn held), f126, f189 (under_towers held), f192, f258, f324 (north-west corner to Base A), f588, f654, f720, f1003 (bend), f1560, f1620, f1705 (Gyrocopters over rock and ridge), f1880 and f1939 (Flags carried).\n- movie_legibility: f60 (Gyrocopters over the channel), f71, f90, f120, and the surface frames f361, f420, f480, f540, f542. Also the showcase, legibility and cream-count logs.\n- Implementer frames: k4 main_spawn, cue_flag_crop, sheet_types; k5 final_choice; k6 after_inside, after_depot; k3 frames2/tower_far_corner.\n- Files: the map_01 material and texture references (grep), map_01_dressing.tscn, compound_base.tscn meshes, water_canister.tscn, fuel_can.tscn colours, both Team materials, both HUD edge styleboxes, and the map_01.tscn environment.\n\n**Verdict**\nIt is one coherent palette that follows the illustrated drawing, and the Units follow the concept sheet with one Team colour per model. The Team colours own exactly the Units, the corner towers, the tanks, the dashed rectangles, the Flags and the HUD and choice edges, and nothing else. The Fuel Can red is unmistakable everywhere. Nothing reads as a Unit or a Flag that is not one: the wrecks are plain boxes, and the dark depot posts are drums that never wear a Team colour. The four Unit types are distinct from 13 m behind.\n\n**AC-15 notes for the author (not decided here)**\n1. A Motorbike carrying the enemy Flag is almost all Flag from its own camera. Only the cream cue and the handlebar show above the 0.94 m drum (cue_flag_crop.png, f1939), so the player's own Unit reads in the enemy's colour. The letter of the ACs is met: AC-11 excludes a carried Flag, and AC-12's cue shows (38-60 px). A shorter Flag, or a lower or side carry point (data outside this workflow), would show the bike.\n2. Orange Units appear on the rust Garage floor with clearly less contrast than Teal ones (f123, main_spawn). The floor's cellular tile pattern is not in the drawing, which shows a corrugated rust roof.\n3. The biggest departures from the drawing, largest first:\n   - The navy sea (OQ16, deliberate).\n   - The cover. Wrecks, long containers and scrap walls all wear one scrap texture on plain boxes (rust.tres, container.tres and scrap.tres are identical). They no longer read as wrecks, containers and scrap walls, and at distance they blend into the rust rock (f480, f720).\n   - Team-coloured water towers (OQ5).\n   - Olive Base containers instead of the drawing's slate grey.\n   - Dark depot posts instead of orange (OQ16).\n4. At chase-camera range the salt flat's cracks read as wide, soft brown smudges rather than thin cracks (f71, f1560). This comes from the one non-tiling 2048 px texture over 190 m that the DESIGN chose.\n5. The fords' saturated pool-cyan with white caustics is the brightest neutral surface and pulls the eye. It is faithful to the drawing's light ford.\n6. Off-lane, Units visibly drive through no-collision dressing: the 2.5 m containers, the depot tanks and the boulders. OQ18 accepts this.\n7. The depot's north posts stand at (\u00b19.76, -8.94), outside the set-back tanks, rather than at about (\u00b17, -6). It reads fine.\n8. From the gate axis the depot Cans are seen edge-on as thin red sticks. They are still clearly red.\n9. The 6 m solid Team-coloured corner towers dominate each Base's silhouette. That is a strong ownership signal and matches the drawing's coloured corners.\n10. Where the orange tank sits behind P1's band, the band's orange edge disappears against it (final_choice). This is minor.\n\n**For the orchestrator**\n- The PNG two frames after a showcase frame= value already shows the next staging: f126 comes after garage_spawn (124) and f192 after under_towers (190). f123 and f189 are the held views, so pick the PNG at frame= or one before it, and read it.\n- Not measured here: AC-14 draw calls and fps, and the tick-level occlusion rays."}
