{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"StandardMaterial3D\" id=\"StandardMaterial3D_container\"]\nalbedo_color = Color(0.55, 1, 0.9, 1)   (also StandardMaterial3D_container_rib albedo_color = Color(0.38, 0.7, 0.62, 1) and StandardMaterial3D_rubber albedo_color = Color(0.07, 0.07, 0.075, 1))", "problem": "These are three inline materials with colour literals in a Map scene. Eight dressing nodes use them and none references a file under maps/map_01/materials/: Dressing/West and Dressing/East, each with ContainerNorth, ContainerSouth, ContainerRibs (MultiMesh) and TyreStacks (MultiMesh). The headless probe walked every GeometryInstance3D of the main scene's Map and found 8 violations ('MATVIOL total=8'). These are the only ones. Grepping albedo_color across the Map scenes finds only this file. This breaks the rule that every Map 01 mesh, dressing included, references a materials/ file or a Team material, and the 'data not literals' rule. materials/container.tres exists, but it is the cover containers' material, untinted, so the dressing could not reuse it as is.", "fix": "Move the three sub_resources unchanged into material files under src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/, for example dressing_container.tres, dressing_container_rib.tres and rubber.tres, with readable ids and no uid line. Reference them as ext_resources from BoxMesh_container_7m/8m, BoxMesh_rib and TorusMesh_tyre, then delete the sub_resources. Change no values. Re-run regress and the five map scenarios."}, {"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "quote": "color_meshes = [NodePath(\"Walls/TowerGateLeft/Mesh\"), NodePath(\"Walls/TowerGateRight/Mesh\"), NodePath(\"Walls/TowerBackLeft/Mesh\"), NodePath(\"Walls/TowerBackRight/Mesh\"), NodePath(\"Garage/Marking/Dash01\") ... NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\")]", "problem": "DESIGN 3 says compound_base.tscn lists only its four corner-tower meshes and the marking in the new color_meshes export. DESIGN 4 names only the tank (the beacon) as Team-coloured, with a dark steel ring or frame. The list also holds WaterTower/Roof, the SphereMesh_roof dome on tower.tres, so the roof is painted the Team colour too. Probe: color_meshes has 19 entries, which is 4 towers + 14 dashes + Roof. 22 Team-painted meshes per Base: Pad, Canister/Body, Tank, 4 towers, 14 dashes and Roof.", "fix": "Remove NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\") from color_meshes so the roof keeps tower.tres. Alternatively, the orchestrator records the roof as part of the tank under AC-12 ('each [water tower] takes its Base's Team colour') and keeps it."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn", "quote": "model_scale = 0.735   (no offset export set)", "problem": "Measured in the parent (Unit) space of the instanced model, the truck's hull runs z -2.330..2.073 and x -0.919..0.919, against a collider of x \u00b11.20 and z \u00b12.20. Its length of 4.403 m fits, but the hull sits 0.128 m forward: the nose overhangs the collider by 0.130 m and the rear stops 0.127 m short. At a wall contact the Truck's nose is drawn 0.13 m inside the wall, so the hull is not within the collider footprint. The other models: the Motorbike's tail overhangs by 0.060 m (the tail at z 1.36 that the DESIGN anticipated) and its front sits 0.058 m inside. The Buggy fits (x exactly \u00b10.900, z +0.001). The Gyrocopter's body is inside (x \u00b10.70, z -1.19..1.15); its accent rotor overhangs x by 1.419 m per side and the front by 0.228 m, as a rotor must.", "fix": "Orchestrator decides. Either record the Truck's 0.13 m nose overhang as accepted in the evidence doc, or set offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.128) in truck_kit_model.tscn. That is the existing export the Gyrocopter uses to centre its hull; it is data only."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"MultiMesh\" id=\"MultiMesh_depot_posts\"] ... buffer = PackedFloat32Array(1, 0, 0, -9.76, 0, 1, 0, 0.6, 0, 0, 1, -8.94, 1, 0, 0, 9.76, ...", "problem": "DESIGN 7 puts two depot posts at about (\u00b17, -6). They are built at (\u00b19.76, -8.94), 4.0 m away. The DESIGN's spot lies inside the layout's depot fuel tanks FuelTankNorthWest and FuelTankNorthEast (centre (\u22136.8, -6.6), radius 2.5), so the move is necessary. It is not recorded anywhere I could find. The other four posts are where the DESIGN puts them ((\u00b16.4, 3.9), (\u00b15, 5.9)). The nearest Fuel Can is 2.49 m from any post.", "fix": "Record the deviation (the DESIGN's (\u00b17, -6) collides with the fuel tanks; built at (\u00b19.76, -8.94)) in production/qa/evidence/story-007-the-map-evidence.md beside the positions table. No code change."}, {"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/textures/ford.tres", "quote": "materials/ford.tres: albedo_texture = textures/ford.tres, albedo white, transparency 0", "problem": "The ford's albedo is the closest neutral colour to a Team colour in the Map. Its texture ramp gives (0.46,0.68,0.73) / (0.49,0.70,0.74) / (0.56,0.74,0.77) at 0.2 / 0.5 / 0.8, which is CIE76 dE 18 to 24 from Team Teal (0.18,0.60,0.58). The sea and channels measure 45 to 60, and every other neutral is at least 32 from either Team colour. The look preflight named Teal over the pale ford the second-weakest legibility pair: 0.48 sRGB distance and 1.43 luminance ratio, against its 0.47 / 1.4 floor. AC-11 (open question 16: 'the water is a blue told apart from Teal') and AC-13's ford check depend on the rendered frames, which a headless run cannot judge.", "fix": "Check map_legibility's ford moments in both views from the windowed run. Change nothing if a Teal Unit and a Teal Flag read clearly over the ford. Otherwise the orchestrator decides on a ramp change to textures/ford.tres."}, {"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"BoxMesh\" id=\"BoxMesh_garage_back\"]\nmaterial = ExtResource(\"3_wall\")   (BoxMesh_garage_side likewise)", "problem": "The Garage's back and side walls use wall.tres, the scrap texture at 0.55 grey tint (albedo about (0.20,0.09,0.03)), the same as the compound walls. Only the Garage floor (garage_floor.tres) uses the rust-coloured garage texture (about (0.48,0.25,0.12)). AC-11's 'its walls stay dark and its Garage rust, as drawn' therefore rests on the floor alone. Headless cannot show whether the Garage reads as rust from the chase camera.", "fix": "Check the 'Unit appearing in a Garage' frame against design/source/map01_colored.png. If the Garage does not read as rust, the orchestrator decides whether the three Garage wall meshes may reference a rust material. That is a material reference only, with colliders untouched; K1 says 'the Garage rust (the garage texture)'."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-1..AC-9 (layout holds)", "what": "dev07 new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover (headless, own run-out copy)", "value": "all 5 RESULT ok, 0 failed checks (map_layout 2/2, map_edges 2/2, map_ford 1/1, map_bases 2/2, map_cover 1/1)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "REGRESSION", "what": "dev07 regress (24 baselines)", "value": "ALL_OK=True: the strict 20 byte-identical with rc 0; the soft 4 RESULT ok, and they are also byte-identical", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-15 frames (headless premise)", "what": "dev07 new map_showcase map_legibility", "value": "map_showcase RESULT ok moments=15, spawns p1_motorbike,p2_buggy, road_done true,true, rock_ticks 61,90, flag_ticks 167; map_legibility RESULT ok moments=6, worst_miss_m 2.02. No premise CHECK printed (it prints only on failure).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "FROZEN", "what": "dev07 frozen (shasum -c)", "value": "9 of 9 OK", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 kit untouched", "what": "dev07 assets", "value": "ASSETS UNCHANGED", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "launch", "what": "dev07 launch (main scene 120 frames, driving_toy 60 frames)", "value": "rc 0, no ERROR or WARNING lines", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "parse", "what": "dev07 parse", "value": "24 of 24 changed or new .gd files ok", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 materials", "what": "Every GeometryInstance3D of the main scene's Map (CSG and dressing included) references a materials/ file or a Team material; Fuel Can and Flag scenes exempt", "value": "8 violations, all in map_01_dressing.tscn (inline container, container_rib and rubber materials); all other nodes comply", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-10 textures", "what": "The nine textures against the preflight recipes (normalised text), uid lines, ids, loaded fields", "value": "9 of 9 identical to preflight-look/a/gl/recipes, no uid line, readable ids. All load as NoiseTexture2D: eight at 512x512 seamless, salt_span at 2048x388 not seamless; mipmaps and normalize on.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 material params", "what": "albedo texture, tint, roughness, filter, mapping", "value": "The anisotropic-filter enum value is 5, and every textured material uses filter 5 with roughness 1.0. Untinted except wall.tres, which has the 0.55 grey tint. sand, road, ford, rock and ridge are world triplanar at 1/32; sea and channel at 1/64, with channel equal to sea; garage_floor, wall, scrap, rust and container at 1/16. The salt flat uses its own UVs at scale 1 with no triplanar. marking (0.782,0.773,0.739), tower (0.30,0.31,0.33) and fuel_tank (0.64,0.65,0.64) are untextured. Every material is opaque, the ford included.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Team materials", "what": "team_orange/teal_material.tres", "value": "albedo (0.9,0.45,0.14) and (0.18,0.6,0.58); roughness 0.7, metallic 0.05; vertex colour as albedo and sRGB both on", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 who wears them", "what": "Base1/Base2.color_material, painted meshes, neutral nodes", "value": "Base1 Orange, Base2 Teal. 22 painted meshes per Base (Pad, Flag Body, Tank (beacon), 4 corner towers, 14 dashes, plus the Roof the DESIGN does not name), and no Base mixes colours. No node outside a Base wears a Team colour (TEAMUSE '-' n=0). Fuel Cans 9 of 9 with tank (0.78,0.08,0.1).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Units, main scene", "what": "split_screen.tscn team_material and real Unit.spawn() paint, 4 types x 2 Players", "value": "Player1Unit Orange, Player2Unit Teal; 8 of 8 paint Accent only; Neutral has no override; no other Team mesh", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 greybox composition", "what": "Probe after the harness's restore (--scenario=bases)", "value": "team_material = player_1/2_body_material.tres; Model = motorbike_model.tscn; the 4 UnitStats.model are the greybox models; World holds GreyboxField, TerrainStandIns and FuelCans", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 UnitStats", "what": "The four *_stats.tres model paths", "value": "motorbike, buggy, truck and gyrocopter all point at their _kit_model.tscn", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 UI edges", "what": "edge_style per instance; default when unset", "value": "P1 Hud and UnitChoice: team_orange_edge (border (0.9,0.45,0.14), 3 px, no fill). P2: team_teal_edge (0.18,0.6,0.58). The export defaults to null and draws nothing when null. player_hud.tscn is unchanged; unit_choice.tscn only gains unique_name_in_owner on Panel. Amber against Orange: CIE76 albedo dE 33.2.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10/AC-12 kit models", "what": "Accent and Neutral groups, surfaces, scale, hover, fallback material", "value": "All 4: Accent is in team_colour with 1 surface and a fallback vertex-colour material (0.66,0.67,0.68); Neutral is in no group and has 3 surfaces, 4 in total. Scales 0.98 / 0.72 / 0.735 / 0.66. Hover 0 / 0 / 0 / 0.8, and the Gyrocopter sits at (0, 0.8, -0.28). Only the Gyrocopter runs physics processing (the rise).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 kit hull within the collider", "what": "Model AABB in Unit space against the collider", "value": "Motorbike tail +0.060 m; Buggy +0.001 m; Truck nose +0.130 m (rear 0.127 m short); Gyrocopter body inside, rotor x +1.419 m", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-12 Motorbike cue", "what": "Build with the patch remap against a build without it", "value": "24 vertices (the 0.36 x 0.02 x 0.28 box at (0, 1.015, 0.03)) move from Accent to the lamp surface (122 -> 146). parts_remapped=1. The main neutral surface and the skull are identical. Nothing else changed.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 kit remaps", "what": "Buggy pennant and Truck drum against unremapped builds", "value": "Buggy: 24 vertices of colour (0.918,0.420,0.098) move from Neutral to Accent. Truck: 106 vertices change from (0.698,0.357,0.149) to steel_dark (0.298,0.310,0.329), with Accent unchanged.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 colliders", "what": "Collision before and after the look", "value": "Sections identical: compound_base 34/34 (k2 original against now), map_01 2/2, depot 0/0, water_canister and fuel_can as at HEAD; terrain, cliffs, water, cover and ford.tscn are untouched (modified before the look began). At run time: 5 CSG on layer 32; floor 1; shore 32; water 2 on layer 32; compound 32; cover 12; Areas: 2 ford, 2 zones, 2 Flags, 9 Fuel Cans. The dressing has none.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 dressing placement", "what": "Distance of each prop to the Base lanes (|x|<=5.5, z -30..7.2), seats, Fuel Cans and road; MultiMesh read from the .tscn buffers", "value": "Minimum distances: lane 3.44 m (ribs; containers 3.50), seat 9.54 m, Fuel Can 1.64 m (the layout's depot tank band; K6 posts 2.49 m), road 9.95 m. Boulders are all on sand, top at most 0.85 m, in rock.tres. Base B mirrors Base A.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12 water tower", "what": "Tank lowest point, braces, beacon", "value": "Tank CylinderMesh y 8.300 to 13.300 in both Bases; beacon is the Tank (true); lowest brace point y 3.352", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12 Flag", "what": "Body radius, height, PickupZone", "value": "Body r 0.28, h 0.72; widest part 0.300 (bands); total height 0.94 m. PickupZone sphere r 1.0 at y 0.6, layer 8, mask 2, identical to HEAD.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Fuel Can", "what": "fuel_can.tscn compared with HEAD", "value": "One line changed: albedo (0.95,0.62,0.12) -> (0.78,0.08,0.1); zones and nodes identical", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "base.tscn", "what": "git diff HEAD", "value": "unchanged", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11/16 neutral colours", "what": "Approximate albedo (tint x texture ramp), CIE76 against the Team colours and Fuel red", "value": "ford against Teal 18 to 24 (the closest pair); sea 45 to 60; every other neutral at least 32 from either Team colour and at least 40 from Fuel red", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "draw-call budget", "what": "MeshInstance3D count per scene", "value": "compound_base 44 per Base (52 of 88 with shadows off); depot 32 (20 with shadows off); dressing 4 MeshInstance3D + 7 MultiMeshInstance3D (94 instances); cover 12; water 3; ford 1 each; terrain 1 + 2 CSG; cliffs 5 CSG; Flag 5; Fuel Can 3; kit model 2", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13/AC-14/AC-15", "what": "Legibility, visibility of the Gyrocopter's rise, frame rate and draw calls, coherence judgement", "value": "Need windowed rendering; outside this headless role", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "I ran everything headless and read-only: one Godot process at a time, each with a timeout, using a private dev07 copy whose output goes to look/lens-ac-headless/run-out.\n\n- **Suite** (run_suite.py): frozen 9 of 9 OK, assets unchanged, parse 24 of 24 ok, the five map scenarios pass, map_showcase and map_legibility end RESULT ok, regress ALL_OK=True, and the launch is clean.\n- **probe_main.gd**: checked the texture-filter enum value, loaded the nine textures and the material files, the Team materials and the four UnitStats.\n  - Built the kit models next to unremapped builds and compared vertex counts and colours, to confirm the Motorbike patch, the Buggy pennant and the Truck drum.\n  - Measured each model's surfaces, groups, scale, hover and overhang against its collider.\n  - Loaded the main scene and walked the whole Map: materials, Team-colour use, collider census, tank and brace heights, the Flag and its PickupZone, the Fuel Cans, the UI edges.\n  - Painted all 4 types on both Players through the real Unit.spawn().\n- **probe_greybox.gd**: read the state after the harness's greybox restore.\n- **analyse.py**:\n  - texture text against the preflight recipes;\n  - collision sections before and after, using the look/k2 and k6 originals and HEAD;\n  - dressing distances to lanes, seats, Fuel Cans and the road. I read the MultiMesh positions from the .tscn buffers because the headless RenderingServer returns identity instance transforms.\n  - approximate albedo dE.\n\nSix findings:\n1. The dressing's three inline materials (STANDARD).\n2. The Roof is in color_meshes (SCOPE).\n3. The Truck's nose overhangs its collider by 0.13 m (DESIGN).\n4. The depot posts moved because the DESIGN's spot lies inside the fuel tanks (DESIGN).\n5. The ford is the closest neutral to Teal, to confirm in frames (UNVERIFIED).\n6. The Garage walls are dark and only the floor is rust (UNVERIFIED).\n\nNot covered here because they need rendering: AC-13 visibility and legibility, AC-14 fps and draw calls, AC-15.\n\nScripts and outputs are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-ac-headless/ (probe_main.gd/.out, probe_greybox.gd/.out, analyse.py, suite-*.txt)."}
