driving toy 60 frames, both rc=0 with no ERROR or WARNING. The main scene builds all four kit models at warm-up, so the new checks ran there and stayed silent.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty outputs are byte-identical; the soft four end RESULT ok and are also identical.", "dev07.py new: all five Map 01 scenarios pass with failed=0 \u2014 map_layout (checks=2), map_edges (checks=2), map_ford (checks=1), map_bases (checks=2), map_cover (checks=1).", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED. No Godot process is left running.", "lint007.py all on the four edited files: 0 declarations without a ## line and 0 ## lines over 100 columns. It still flags KitMerge._commit as 47 lines LONG, the same count as on the pre-fix copy. That count is a lint artefact: it adds the two inner classes that follow _commit to the end of the file, and _commit's own body is 16 lines. It also flags base.gd _ready and first_spawn_problem at about 11 complexity, which Slice K2 already reported. None of these is from this pass.", "No windowed frame was taken. None of the five issues changes anything visible: four are doc or error-message changes, and the query cap was shown above to change nothing on Map 01. No scene, mesh or material changed, so the draw calls are unchanged."], "deviations": ["Issue 2 (architecture, map_field.gd doc) is NOT applied. src/gameplay/maps/map_field.gd is not on this workflow's list of files I may write, and the run makes everything else read-only. I checked the lens's text against the files, and it is accurate. (a) map_01.tscn gives Base1 team_orange_material.tres and Base2 team_teal_material.tres. split_screen.tscn gives Player1Unit Orange and Player2Unit Teal as team_material, and the edge styles team_orange_edge.tres to Player 1's HUD and choice panel and team_teal_edge.tres to Player 2's. (b) KitUnitModel._rise_target() only rises for a hit whose collider is a GeometryInstance3D. (c) Map 01's channel water (ChannelWest and ChannelEast) is a bare StaticBody3D on layer 32 with a flat Surface mesh as its child. (d) terrain_stand_ins.tscn's Cliff is a StaticBody3D on layer 32 with a Mesh child. To apply the fix, add the lens's paragraph to MapField's class doc after the paragraph that starts '## The contract.', wrapped at 100 columns. The orchestrator needs to do this or allow the file.", "Issue 5: water_canister.gd is re-flowed slightly differently from the lens's wording. The lens wrote '... and nothing' / 'else.', which leaves a one-word line. A 100-column fill gives '... a touch zone.' (exactly 100 columns) / '## It holds where it is (at home, carried, dropped) and the Unit carrying it, and nothing else.'. Same words, two lines instead of three.", "Issue 1: besides the three items the lens asked for, the doc comments of _build() and _palette_of() each gained one sentence describing the new error, so each function's doc matches what it does. I also briefly extended the Built.parts_remapped doc, then reverted it to the original line to keep the edits minimal. The kit_merge.gd class-doc paragraph about the two remaps was re-flowed at 100 columns to fit the added sentence, with no other change to its words.", "Issue 4: the RISE_MAX_RESULTS comment uses the measured figures from this pass: up to 11 results for the real Gyrocopter box, and the lens's 30 for a 400 x 20 x 120 m box."], "blockers": ["Issue 2 cannot be applied in this pass: the doc fix belongs in src/gameplay/maps/map_field.gd, which this workflow does not allow me to write. The checked replacement text is in deviations, ready for the orchestrator."], "summary": "I applied four of the five fixes in this pass. Issue 2 is not applied because map_field.gd is outside the files I may write. All checks pass: regress ALL_OK, all five Map 01 scenarios ok, clean launch, frozen files and assets/ unchanged.\n\n1. **kit_merge.gd (part remap and palette errors).**\n   - `_build()` now raises an error just before `_commit()` when `parts_remapped` does not equal `part_remap.size()`. The message names the kit scene and the remap entries and says an unmatched part keeps its kit key.\n   - `_palette_of()` used to return early on a valid palette. It now returns early on a missing or empty one. It then raises one error, naming the kit scene and the key, for each of teal, orange, rim, teal_dark and orange_dark that the palette lacks.\n   - The class doc gained one sentence: the part remap is keyed on the kit part's geometry and reports an error when a kit edit moves it.\n   - All four kits match today, so neither error fires (Motorbike 1 of 1 matched, the other three 0 of 0). A probe with a deliberately wrong remap and a fake palette made both errors fire.\n\n2. **map_field.gd doc: not applied.** The file is not on my write list. I checked the lens's text against map_01.tscn, split_screen.tscn, kit_unit_model.gd, map_01_water.tscn and terrain_stand_ins.tscn, and it is accurate. It is ready for the orchestrator.\n\n3. **base.gd line 96.** 'the Lid keeps its cream' -> 'its steel parts stay steel'. The line is 98 columns, so nothing else moved.\n\n4. **kit_unit_model.gd, `RISE_MAX_RESULTS`.** 8 -> 64. Its comment now says that a CSG collider is reported once per overlapping piece, so the cap must be larger than the duplicates. The lens's claim holds on 4.7.2:\n   - The real Gyrocopter box gets up to 11 results from one cliff.\n   - 203 queries went over the old cap of 8.\n   - Across 89,040 queries, no second cliff was ever hidden at 8 and the top height never changed, so Map 01 behaves the same.\n   - No query came near 64.\n\n5. **water_canister.gd class doc.** The stray two-word line '## zone. It' is gone; the paragraph is re-flowed to fit 100 columns.\n\nNo windowed frame was taken, because none of these changes anything on screen. The probe and its outputs are in look/fix1/, along with copies of all four files from before the edits.", "complete": false}
