{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/base.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/canister/water_canister.gd"], "verification": ["All checks below ran on the final state of the tree, after this continuation's one doc edit and with the map_field.gd paragraph already on disk.", "dev07.py import: rc=0. It found 235 classes, none new or gone, and copied no .uid sidecars. .godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg is byte-identical before and after (cmp). The ERROR lines it lists come from the scratch copy, which has no assets/ folder, so the four kit scenes cannot load there. This is expected.", "dev07.py parse: rc=0, 24 files ok. They include kit_merge.gd, kit_unit_model.gd, base.gd, water_canister.gd and map_field.gd.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, both rc=0, noisy=[] (no ERROR or WARNING). The main scene's warm-up builds all four kit models, so the new KitMerge checks ran and stayed silent.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are byte-identical, and the soft four end RESULT ok and are also identical.", "dev07.py new: all five pass with failed=0 (8 CHECK lines in total, none failed) \u2014 map_layout checks=2; map_edges checks=2 (shore_lanes=20, cliff_lanes=18); map_ford checks=1 (runs=8, problems=0); map_bases checks=2 (exit_contacts=0); map_cover checks=1 (depot_takes=5).", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED. No Godot process was running before or after, and none of mine is left.", "lint007.py all on the five files: 0 declarations without a ## line and 0 ## lines over 100 columns. It flags KitMerge._commit as 47 lines LONG, which is a lint artefact: _commit starts at line 297, the file ends at line 343, and the count includes the inner classes Built (line 316) and _Surface (line 329); _commit's own body is about 18 lines. It also flags base.gd _ready and first_spawn_problem at about 11 complexity, which Slice K2 already reported. None of these comes from this pass.", "I re-read the previous attempt's probe output (look/fix1/rise_probe.gd.out and .err). Part remap: the Motorbike matched 1 part for its 1 entry; the Buggy, Truck and Gyrocopter 0 for 0. A remap with its size off by 0.01 m makes the new part-remap error fire, naming the kit scene and the entry. A fake palette without rim, teal_dark and orange_dark gives one error per missing key. Rise query with the Gyrocopter's real box: 89,040 queries; at most 11 results per query (all from one cliff); 203 queries returned 8 or more; with a cap of 8, no second cliff was ever left out (hidden_at_8=0) and the top height never changed (top_differs_8_vs_64=0); no query reached 64 (saturated_at_64=0).", "No windowed frame was taken. None of the five changes is visible: four are doc or error-message changes, and the query cap is shown above to change nothing on Map 01. No scene, mesh or material changed, so the draw calls are unchanged."], "deviations": ["Issue 2 (map_field.gd doc) was not written by this fix pass: map_field.gd is not on its list of writable files (it is not frozen). In this continuation I found the change already on disk: map_field.gd was changed at 02:09:49, after the previous attempt's last edit (02:07:45) and before this pass began, and it now has a paragraph at lines 23 to 30 starting '## The look (Story 007) asks two more things of a Map.' I checked it and did not touch the file. It covers both of the lens's points: (1) player_1_base wears team_orange_material.tres and player_2_base team_teal_material.tres, matching split_screen.tscn; (2) cliffs on the cliffs_water layer are CSG shapes with use_collision, water there is a bare StaticBody3D, and a StaticBody3D cliff with a mesh child (terrain_stand_ins.tscn) would hide the Gyrocopter. It parses, its widest line is 98 columns, and it is worded differently from the lens's text. The orchestrator should confirm it made this edit, since otherwise another agent is writing to the repo. The patch I had prepared for this paragraph was tested with a dry run only and never applied. I renamed it in scratch to look/fix1b/map_field.issue2.patch.OBSOLETE-already-applied-do-not-apply so it cannot be applied twice.", "Issue 5: water_canister.gd is re-flowed slightly differently from the lens's wording. The lens's version leaves 'else.' alone on its own line. A 100-column fill gives '... a touch zone.' (99 columns) followed by '## It holds where it is (at home, carried, dropped) and the Unit carrying it, and nothing else.' Same words, two lines instead of three.", "Issue 1 has three small extras: (a) the _build() and _palette_of() doc comments each gained one sentence describing the new error, so each doc matches what its function does; (b) the class-doc paragraph about the two remaps was re-flowed at 100 columns to fit the added sentence; (c) in this continuation I dropped the word 'then' from that sentence ('the build then reports' -> 'the build reports'), so the paragraph no longer ends on a one-word '## key.' line. The meaning is the same.", "Issue 4: the RISE_MAX_RESULTS comment uses measured figures: up to 11 results for the Gyrocopter's real box over Map 01 (this pass's probe) and 30 for one 400 x 20 x 120 m box (the lens's measurement)."], "blockers": [], "summary": "All five fixes are now on disk and every check passes. This pass applied four of them. The fifth, issue 2, was already in map_field.gd when I checked; I did not write it.\n\n- **Regression checks:** regress ALL_OK, all five Map 01 scenarios pass with failed=0, and the launch is clean with no ERROR or WARNING.\n- **Other checks:** the frozen files and assets/ are unchanged, the class cache is unchanged, and no Godot process is left running.\n\nChanges, before -> after:\n\n1. **`kit_merge.gd`** (part-remap and palette errors):\n   - `_build()`: nothing -> a `push_error` just before `_commit()` when `built.parts_remapped != part_remap.size()`. The message names the kit scene and the remap entries and says an unmatched part keeps its kit key.\n   - `_palette_of()`: returned early on a non-empty palette -> errors and returns `{}` on a missing or empty one, then raises one error for each key of `ACCENT_KEYS` and `ACCENT_DARK_KEYS` that the palette lacks, naming the kit scene and the key.\n   - Class doc: one sentence added saying the part remap is keyed on the kit part's geometry and reports an error when a kit edit moves it.\n   - All four kits match today (Motorbike 1 of 1, the others 0 of 0), so both errors stay silent. A probe made them fire on a deliberately wrong remap and on a palette missing three keys.\n\n2. **`map_field.gd`:** not written by this pass. The paragraph appeared on disk at 02:09:49 (lines 23 to 30), in wording that differs from the lens's text. I checked that it covers both of the lens's points, parses, and stays under 100 columns. The orchestrator should confirm it made this edit; if it did not, another agent is writing to the repo.\n\n3. **`base.gd` line 96:** 'the Lid keeps its cream' -> 'its steel parts stay steel'.\n\n4. **`kit_unit_model.gd`:** `RISE_MAX_RESULTS` 8 -> 64. Its comment now says a CSG collider is reported once per overlapping piece, so the cap must exceed the duplicates. On Map 01 the old cap never hid a second cliff and never changed the top height, so nothing changes there.\n\n5. **`water_canister.gd` class doc:** the stray line '## zone. It' is gone; the paragraph is re-flowed to two lines within 100 columns.\n\nThe only edit in this continuation was to the issue 1 sentence in `kit_merge.gd`: I dropped the word 'then' so the paragraph no longer ends on a one-word '## key.' line.\n\nNo windowed frame was taken, because none of these changes is visible. This pass's scratch files are in look/fix1b/; the previous attempt's probe and the pre-edit copies of the four files are in look/fix1/.", "complete": true}
