{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/motorbike_kit_model.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/buggy_kit_model.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/split_screen/split_screen.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd"], "verification": ["Probe on Godot 4.7.2 before editing (scratch look/fix1/probe_typed.gd; the engine wrote only to a scratch .tscn, never in the repo). The engine writes a typed export as `remap = Dictionary[String, String]({` then one entry per line, then `})`. A typed const `Dictionary[String, float]` compiles, and so do `Dictionary[String, Built]` and `Dictionary[String, _Surface]` (inner-class values). A Variant key assigns into `Dictionary[Material, String]` (25 of 25). The kit's `_m` is an untyped Dictionary of String to StandardMaterial3D (25 entries). Assigning an untyped Dictionary to a typed variable is a SCRIPT ERROR ('Trying to assign a dictionary of type \"Dictionary\" to a variable of type \"Dictionary[String, Material]\"'), so `palette` stays bare. Typed and untyped dictionaries format the same with %s, so KitMerge's cache key is unchanged.", "Probe after editing (scratch look/fix1/probe_remap.gd, headless). All four kit model scenes load material_remap as typed String/String with both entries. The Buggy's Accent mesh has 4434 vertices with the remap and 4410 without; the 24 extra are one BoxMesh, the pennant, so flag -> orange still reaches the build. The Motorbike builds with no KitMerge part-remap error, so its single entry still matches one part. Stderr empty.", "dev07.py import: rc=0, class cache 235 classes, none new or gone, no sidecars copied. The 'Cannot open file res://assets/...' lines come from the helper's scratch copy, which has no assets/.", "dev07.py parse: PARSE rc=0, 24 of 24 files ok.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames rc=0 noisy=[]; driving toy 60 frames rc=0 noisy=[].", "dev07.py frozen: every frozen file OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True (the strict twenty byte-identical with exit 0, the soft four RESULT ok).", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five pass. map_layout ok checks=2, map_edges ok checks=2, map_ford ok checks=1 (problems=0), map_bases ok checks=2 (exit_contacts=0), map_cover ok checks=1. Log: scratch look/fix1/verify.log.", "lint007.py all on kit_merge.gd, kit_unit_model.gd, split_screen.gd and map_showcase.gd: 0 declarations without a ## line, 0 ## lines over 100 columns. fns names only kit_merge.gd _commit 'lines=45 cc~10'. That flag predates this pass (47 lines before): the counter runs from `static func _commit` to the end of the file, through the inner classes Built and _Surface, while the function itself is 16 lines. _build is 36 lines and under cc 10.", "grep of the four edited scripts: no 'preflight' left; every 'measured on 4.7.2' carries the evidence-doc pointer; the only bare Dictionary declarations left are the `palette` ones (by design) and the part_remap entries (mixed Vector3 and String values).", "No windowed frame was taken: none of the five issues is visual. The only change that could alter a frame, the typed material_remap in the four scenes, is proved by the remap probe above.", "Only one Godot process of mine ran at a time, each with a timeout; none is left running. Pre-fix copies of every edited file are kept in scratch look/fix1/before/. The edit script is look/fix1/apply_fix1.py."], "deviations": ["Issue 5 (SCOPE, Built.parts_remapped): the proposed fix was wrong as written. The lens says the field is read nowhere, but _build() read it (old lines 161-162) for the error raised when the part remap does not match exactly one part per entry. That error is described in the class doc and is what would flag a lost cream heading cue (AC-12) if the kit changed. Deleting only what the lens listed would leave a reference to a deleted field and fail to compile. What I did: removed the field and its doc, the increment, the `built: Built` parameter of _key_of_part() and the doc sentence 'Counts the part remaps in built.parts_remapped.', as asked. The mismatch error stays, counted by a local in _build(): `remapped += int(not by_part.is_empty())`. To match each part only once, _build() now calls _part_remap_key() and passes the result to _key_of_part() as `by_part`. So _key_of_part's signature changed from (part, part_transform, key_of, key_remap, part_remap, built) to (part, by_part, key_of, key_remap), more than just dropping `built`. I wrote the count with int() rather than an `if` to keep _build under the lint's cc 10. One edge case changed: a part that matches a remap entry by size and position but whose material is not in the palette now counts as a match. It is still left out, with its own error.", "Issue 4 (unretained measurements): I fixed one more instance the lens did not list, in the same file. RISE_MAX_RESULTS' doc in kit_unit_model.gd: 'up to 11 for the Gyrocopter's box over Map 01, and 30 for one 400 x 20 x 120 m box (measured on 4.7.2)' -> figures dropped, '(measured on 4.7.2; the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run)'. Under issue 3, kit_merge.gd's KIT_POSE doc had the same kind of pointer as the listed _collect() line: 'the pose the model fit was measured in' -> 'the pose KitUnitModel's model_scale and offset fit.' The lens's line numbers in kit_merge.gd were 2 to 10 lines off (44/46 are 46/48, 173 is 183); I matched every edit by its text.", "For the orchestrator: these doc lines now say 'the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run', so that doc must keep these measurements. (a) PrimitiveMesh.get_mesh_arrays() reads back from the GPU and is too slow to repeat, which is why builds are cached (kit_merge.gd class doc). (b) DARK_TONE 0.68 gives ORANGE_DARK and TEAL_DARK within 0.01 (kit_merge.gd). (c) intersect_shape returns a Map CSG cliff as its CSGPolygon3D node (kit_unit_model.gd class doc). (d) a CSG collider is reported once per overlapping piece of its shape (kit_unit_model.gd RISE_MAX_RESULTS). (e) a model's first build costs enough that a spawn would show it (split_screen.gd _warm_up_models())."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 1 (gameplay): all five issues are fixed, in order, with no change to behaviour or output: regress ALL_OK and the five map scenarios pass. Changes, file and before -> after:\n\n(1) src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd, typed dictionaries:\n- `static var _cache: Dictionary` -> `Dictionary[String, Built]`\n- `const KIT_POSE: Dictionary` -> `Dictionary[String, float]`\n- `key_remap: Dictionary` -> `Dictionary[String, String]` in get_or_build(), _build() and _key_of_part()\n- `var key_of: Dictionary` -> `Dictionary[Material, String]`, and the same for the key_of parameter\n- `var surfaces: Dictionary` and the surfaces parameters of _surface_for() and _commit() -> `Dictionary[String, _Surface]` (_surface_for's signature now wraps onto two lines)\n- `palette` stays bare: the kit's `_m` is an untyped Dictionary and does not assign to a typed one (tested on 4.7.2). _palette_of()'s doc now says so.\n\n(2) kit_unit_model.gd: `@export var material_remap: Dictionary = {}` -> `Dictionary[String, String] = {}`. In motorbike, buggy, truck and gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn: `material_remap = {...}` -> `material_remap = Dictionary[String, String]({...})`, the format the engine itself writes (tested). A probe shows all four load typed and the remap still reaches the build.\n\n(3) kit_merge.gd docs:\n- The figures 26 to 53 ms, 37 and 29 draw calls, and 2.0 to 2.05 m are deleted.\n- Every 'look preflight' pointer is gone. The class-doc paragraph now ends 'That is four surfaces a Unit.'\n- NEUTRAL_ROUGHNESS and NEUTRAL_METALLIC now read '...of the neutral fold's material, which every folded neutral part shares.'\n- DARK_TONE and the GPU read-back sentence keep their fact with '(measured on 4.7.2; the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run)'.\n- _collect(): 'as the model fit was measured' -> 'KitUnitModel places the model'.\n\n(4) Unretained measurements in other files:\n- kit_unit_model.gd class doc: the CSG collider fact now carries the evidence-doc pointer.\n- kit_unit_model.gd model_scale: '(the look preflight)' dropped.\n- kit_unit_model.gd RISE_MAX_RESULTS: figures dropped, pointer added. The lens missed this one.\n- split_screen.gd _warm_up_models(): 'about a quarter of a second ... under a millisecond a spawn after' -> 'at a cost a spawn would show', plus the pointer.\n- map_showcase.gd _over_rock(): '(measured on 4.7.2: kit_unit_model.gd)' deleted.\n\n(5) Built.parts_remapped, its increment, the `built` parameter and the doc sentence are removed. The lens's literal fix would not compile, because _build() read the field for its part-remap mismatch error. That error is kept, counted by a local in _build(); see deviations.\n\nVerification: probes on 4.7.2; import (class cache unchanged); parse 24 of 24 ok; launch with no ERROR or WARNING; frozen OK; assets unchanged; regress ALL_OK=True; map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases and map_cover all pass. Lint names only kit_merge.gd's _commit (45 lines, 47 before this pass), a counter artifact that predates this pass: the counter runs through the two inner classes at the end of the file, and the function is 16 lines. I took no windowed frame: no issue is visual, and the one change that could alter a frame was proved headless. Nothing under assets/, tests/ or the frozen files was touched. No git write was run.", "complete": true}
