{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn"], "verification": ["python3 dev07.py import: rc 0. The class cache is unchanged at 235 classes (none new, none gone) and no .uid sidecars were copied. The only noise is the scratch copy lacking assets/ (the kit scenes cannot open there), which is expected.", "python3 dev07.py parse: ok on every .gd, including kit_unit_model.gd and kit_merge.gd after the final edit.", "python3 dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True on the finished tree (strict twenty byte-identical, soft four RESULT ok).", "python3 dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok, after the final edit.", "python3 dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, rc 0, noisy=[] (after the final edit).", "python3 dev07.py frozen: all OK. python3 dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "lint007.py all on kit_unit_model.gd and kit_merge.gd: 0 declarations without ##, 0 ## lines over 100 columns. It names one long function, KitMerge._commit (45 lines, cc~10). That function is untouched by this pass and no issue names it.", "Hull fit (scratch look/fix1-gameplay/probe_hull.gd, Unit frame, 5 decimals). Truck before: z[-2.32995..2.07270], centre -0.12863. Truck after offset 0.1286: z[-2.20135..2.20130] against collider +-2.20. The residual 0.0013 m per end comes from the design's scale 0.735, which gives a length of 4.40265 m; no offset can remove it. Motorbike z[-1.24204..1.35982], unchanged. Buggy z[-1.48680..1.50120]. Gyrocopter body z[-1.19080..1.20500].", "Rise, the lens's probes rerun headless at --fixed-fps 60 with the fix (outputs in scratch look/fix1-gameplay/*.out). probe_turn_wide.gd turns in at top speed 16.4 m/s from lateral 0.3/0.8/1.5/2.0/2.5/3.0/3.5/4.0/5.0 m: every run has inside_rock_ticks(sample)=0, slab_ticks=0 and min_clear 0.250. The turn-away control at 2.5 m never rises. The turn-away controls at 0.3 and 0.8 m now rise while flying within 2 m of the face, then settle to y 0.800.", "probe_stand_settled.gd (the lens's stand probe with a 24-tick settle, so the model has reached its at-rest state): gaps 0.00/0.10/0.25/0.50/1.00/1.50/2.50/4.00, both channel-to-ridge starts and the road run all show 0 inside ticks and 0 slab ticks, min_clear 0.250.", "probe_rise.gd: every crossing is clean (canyon road W-E, canyon S-N, ridge at x -70/0/70, oblique canyon). Both channels and open sand end at rise 0.000 / model y 0.800. collider_same=true on every run; Unit y max 0.001.", "The lens's original probe_stand.gd, which settles only 4 ticks after a teleport, still shows 8 inside ticks at gap 0.00, 2 at gap 0.10 and 8 on each channel-to-ridge start (hull already touching the ridge); gaps of 0.25 m and more are clean. Before the fix those figures were 12/6/4/2 ticks at gaps 0.00/0.10/0.25/0.50. See the deviations for why this remains.", "Windowed capture (probe_cap_fixed.gd at 1280x720, after checking that no Godot window was open; it captures at the first tick the hull is over rock). Frames are in scratch look/fix1-gameplay/rise-frames/ and I read them. turn03 (turn-in at 0.3 m): the capture tick has rise 1.47 and model y 2.27; the run has inside 0, slab 0, cam_blocked 0. stand00: the same. Read: turn03_side_from_outside.png shows the wheels above the rock top with the shadow on the face. The lens's pre-fix side_from_outside.png, at the same tick, showed the lower body against the face at rise 0.50. turn03_chase.png shows the Gyrocopter in view on the canyon rock edge. stand00_side_from_outside.png is clear of the rock.", "No Godot process of mine is left running (checked by executable name)."], "deviations": ["Issue 3 (rise DEFECT): I applied the lens's fix, which adds ONE new export, rise_margin (default 2.0 m, set on gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn). It sits in the existing 'Rise over cliffs' group, beside the rise exports the slice already had. The DESIGN block names the rise's purpose ('early enough that no part of the model is ever inside rock'), its data-driven parameters and that the slice records the mechanism, but not this specific export. The orchestrator should note it as a data addition made to restore that DESIGN sentence. Its visible side effect, measured: a Gyrocopter flying alongside a cliff face within 2 m of it flies at the risen height (control runs at 0.3 and 0.8 m rise to 1.47, then settle to 0.800 after turning away; at 2.5 m it never rises).", "Issue 3 residual, NOT built (rule a): the lens's probe_stand.gd as written, which settles only 4 ticks after spawn() puts the Unit with its hull touching the rock (gap 0.00 to 0.10 m), still clips for 2 to 8 ticks. No rate-limited rise can be up in 4 ticks (the full rise takes about 15 ticks at rise_rate 6 m/s). A Gyrocopter that has actually come to rest there has already risen through the margin, and that case (24-tick settle) is clean at every gap. In a Round a Unit appears only in its Garage, so the residual is reachable only by a tool's spawn() or place(). The class doc now says so. If the orchestrator wants that case clean too, the fix would be one the DESIGN does not name: the model takes its target at once on a jump (a fresh model, or a tick's move longer than rise_lead_max). I did not build it.", "Issue 2 (water_canister.gd doc wrap): no edit. The quoted orphan line '## zone. It' no longer exists. Lines 3-6 already read as the requested single paragraph ('...a small water tank in its owner's colour and a touch zone. / It holds where it is (at home, carried, dropped) and the Unit carrying it, and nothing else.'), so the orchestrator's earlier correction already fixed it.", "Issues 4/5 (model footprint): I set offset on the Truck only, Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286), using the export the Gyrocopter already uses (data only). 0.1286 is the measured hull centre, not the lenses' 0.129 or 0.128: 0.129 would leave 0.0017 m at the rear. The overshoot reads 0.0013 m per end, not 0.000, because the design's model_scale 0.735 makes the hull 4.40265 m long against a 4.40 m collider. The Motorbike is left unchanged at its 0.060 m tail overhang. The DESIGN explicitly accepts that tail tip (z 1.36, cleared by the Flag at z 1.40), and the lens called its change optional. If the orchestrator wants it, offset Vector3(0, 0, -0.0589) centres it to z[-1.3009..1.3009].", "The base.gd 'the Lid keeps its cream' clause from late finding 2 is not touched: no lens in this pass named it."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 1 (gameplay) for Story 007's look: three of the four issues needed edits, and all checks pass. Changes, file and before -> after:\n\n(1) VOCABULARY.\n- kit_unit_model.gd line 3: \"concept-kit vehicles\" -> \"concept-kit models\".\n- kit_unit_model.gd, the kit_scene doc: \"The kit vehicle this model is built from\" -> \"The kit model this Unit model is built from\".\n- kit_merge.gd line 3: \"concept-kit vehicles\" -> \"concept-kit models\".\n- kit_merge.gd lines 12-13: \"each vehicle script builds its 90 to\" -> \"each kit model's script builds its / 90 to 200 parts\".\n- res://assets/art/vehicles/... paths are left as they are.\n\n(2) WATER CANISTER DOC: already fixed by the orchestrator. The orphan '## zone. It' line is gone and lines 3-6 form the requested paragraph, so no edit.\n\n(3) RISE DEFECT, src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd.\n- _rise_target(): the query box was the hull footprint plus only the last tick's motion lead. It is now that footprint widened by the new export rise_margin on every side (x and z), plus the lead.\n- New export in the Rise over cliffs group: rise_margin: float = 2.0, documented.\n- gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn gains 'rise_margin = 2.0'.\n- Docs updated: the class doc's rise paragraph (re-wrapped to 100 columns, with the one exception stated), the rise_lead_seconds doc and the _rise_target doc. The class doc's old claim that the lead alone covers the whole rise was false.\n- Measured on the real Map 01:\n  - turn-ins at 16.4 m/s from 0.3 to 5.0 m lateral: 0 inside and 0 slab ticks;\n  - standing starts at every gap from 0.00 to 4.00 m, once the model has settled at rest: clean;\n  - every straight crossing: clean;\n  - channels and open sand still end at rise 0.000 / y 0.800;\n  - collider, layer and mask unchanged.\n- Windowed frames read: at the first rock tick the model is fully up, where the lens's frame showed the lower body in the face.\n- Residual: the lens's 4-tick-settle probe still clips at gaps of 0.10 m and below. That is a tool teleport against rock, unreachable in a Round; reported as a deviation, and I did not build the snap that would remove it.\n\n(4/5) TRUCK FOOTPRINT, truck_kit_model.tscn: no offset -> offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286).\n- Hull z[-2.330..2.073] -> z[-2.20135..2.20130].\n- The 1.3 mm left per end comes from the design's scale.\n- The Motorbike's design-accepted 0.06 m tail is left unchanged.\n\nVerification: import (no new classes or sidecars), parse ok, regress ALL_OK, the five map scenarios ok, launch clean, frozen OK, assets unchanged, lint clean on my lines. Probes, outputs and frames are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-gameplay/ for the evidence doc.", "complete": true}
