{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn"], "verification": ["Issue 3, re-emit: K6's original generator reproduced the repo's map_01_dressing.tscn byte for byte. The edited generator changes one line, line 103: the first two instances of the MultiMesh_depot_posts buffer go from (-9.76, 0.6, -8.94) and (9.76, 0.6, -8.94) to (-7.8, 0.6, -3.36) and (7.8, 0.6, -3.36). The generator of record is /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art/gen_dressing.py. I copied it over look/k6/gen_k6.py, and it re-emits the repo file byte for byte. Scene count is unchanged: 4 MeshInstance3D and 7 MultiMeshInstance3D holding 94 instances, with 6 posts.", "Geometry: (+-7, -6) is 0.65 m from the north tank's centre (+-6.8115, -6.6222). The tank's radius is 2.5 and its band's 2.56, so a post of radius 0.75 placed there would sit wholly inside the tank. The new spot (+-7.8, -3.36) is 3.409 m from the tank's centre, which leaves 0.099 m between the post and the band. It is 2.76 m from the drawn spot (K6's was 4.03 m) and 8.49 m from the depot's centre (K6's was 13.24 m). It is 4.81 m from the Fuel Can at (+-3, -3), whose pick-up radius is 1.6.", "K6's windowed clearance check (check_k6.gd), run again on the new file: DepotPosts[0] and [1] at (+-7.80, -3.36) give lane=94.24, seat=103.50, can=2.46, road=19.88, ok. SUMMARY props=110 under_1m=0 min_lane=3.74 min_seat=8.54 min_can=1.08 (the north tanks' band, unchanged) min_road=10.57. All 110 props ok, and none of the dressing nodes has collision.", "I took a windowed top-down of the depot (cx 0, cz 0, width 64) and READ it: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art/top_depot_after.png. The north posts now stand on the depot ring beside the north tanks, and all six posts are on or inside the ring. I compared it with a crop of design/source/map01_colored.png (look/fix1-art/depot_n3x.png), where the drawing's orange posts also sit on the dotted ring beside the tanks.", "dev07.py import: rc=0, 235 classes, new [], gone [], no uid sidecars copied. The four 'Cannot open res://assets/...' lines come from the scratch copy, which has no assets/; they are expected and were there before this pass.", "dev07.py parse: every file ok.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames rc=0 noisy=[]; driving toy 60 frames rc=0 noisy=[].", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "dev07.py regress: all 20 STRICT identical=True; all 4 SOFT result_ok=True identical=True; ALL_OK=True.", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: 8 CHECK PASS, 0 FAIL. RESULT ok for map_layout (checks=2, mirror items=116 worst=0.0000 m), map_edges (checks=2), map_ford (checks=1), map_bases (checks=2, exit_contacts=0) and map_cover (checks=1, depot_takes=5).", "lint007.py all on map_01_dressing.tscn: 0 functions over limits, 0 declarations without ##, 0 ## lines over 100 columns. The file holds no GDScript.", "Draw calls: the posts' MultiMesh still holds 6 instances and no mesh, material or node was added or removed, so this pass changes nothing the draw-call count could see. I did not measure it again.", "Issue 4: I READ the lens frame legibility_channel_gyrocopters_f68.png, both the full frame and a 4x crop (look/fix1-art/chan_crop4x.png). At 38 m over the navy channel, P2's Teal Gyrocopter reads as a teal vehicle: teal skids and rotor tips and a grey hull against the navy.", "No Godot process of mine is left running. I had none to wait on: ps showed no other Godot before either windowed run."], "deviations": ["Issue 3 (SCOPE, depot posts): the proposed fix (+-7, 0.6, -6) is wrong, and I did not apply it. That spot is 0.65 m from the north fuel tank's centre, so a post of radius 0.75 there would be hidden entirely inside the tank. It was also inside the tank at the layout's original tank position, 1.33 m from that centre. Neither of the issue's keep-conditions holds: the nearest lane is 94 m away and the nearest Fuel Can is 5 m away, centre to centre. The right fix was the nearest visible spot to DESIGN 7's (+-7, -6): (+-7.8, -3.36), on the line from the tank's centre through the drawn spot and 0.1 m clear of the band. That is 2.76 m from the drawn spot instead of 4.03 m, and it stands on the depot ring, where the drawing draws its posts. The post partly covers the flat ring dash next to it (Dash19, and Dash12 in the west), much as the drawing's posts overlap the dotted ring. For the evidence doc: DESIGN 7's (+-7, -6) lies inside the depot's north tanks.", "Issues 1 and 2 (SCOPE, the water tower's Roof in color_meshes): not applied. The orchestrator's ruling says the roof dome is part of the Team-coloured tank and keeps it in color_meshes. The three phrases in base.gd's docs that the lenses quote describe that ruled behaviour, so they stay. Late finding 2: the 'the Lid keeps its cream' clause is already gone from base.gd (grep finds no Lid or cream). The orphan wrapped line in water_canister.gd was not named by any lens in this pass, so I left it alone.", "Issue 4 (AC_UNMET, sea ramp): not applied; the orchestrator decides. The proposed darker ramp departs from DESIGN 2's binding navy recipe, and the lens itself hands that call to the orchestrator. AC-13 asks for 'told apart' and sets no dE bar. In the lens frame I READ, the Teal Gyrocopter at 38 m over the channel can be told apart; the lit teal pixels' p90 is dE 47. For the evidence doc and the author's AC-15 judgement: the shaded-side median is dE 23.7 and the lit p90 is dE 47, a marginal pair. If the orchestrator wants the change, it is the four colours of Gradient_sea in src/gameplay/maps/map_01/textures/sea.tres (channel.tres uses the same texture), followed by a new map_legibility measurement. Unverified: I did not measure a darker ramp. In the chase view the channel renders as sRGB (51, 74, 103), lighter than the recipe's (18, 51, 89). Light that a darker albedo does not reduce probably adds to it, likely sky reflection at grazing angles, so the gain could be smaller than the lens predicts.", "Issue 5 (DESIGN, a carried Flag hides the carrier's own Team colour): no code change, as the issue's own fix says. Recording it in the evidence doc is the orchestrator's job, because production/ is outside my write list. Evidence: look/lens-visual/showcase_flag_carried_own_colour_hidden_f1887.png and showcase_flags_taken_f1938.png. The cream cue stays at 60 px on every frame from 1878 to 1939, so AC-12 holds."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 1, art: I changed one repo file and handled the other four issues without code changes.\n\nIssue 3 (the depot's north posts) is the only edit. The lens proposed (+-7, -6), but that spot is inside the north fuel tanks, so the posts would have been hidden. I moved them instead to (+-7.8, -3.36), the nearest spot where a post shows: 2.76 m from the design's spot rather than 4.03 m, on the depot ring where the drawing puts its posts. I made the change in the scratch generator and re-emitted /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn; only the posts' buffer line (line 103) changed.\n\nThe other four issues:\n- **Issues 1 and 2 (the Roof):** not applied, because of the orchestrator's ruling that keeps the roof in color_meshes.\n- **Issue 4 (the sea):** not applied. It would depart from the binding navy recipe, and the lens leaves that call to the orchestrator. I read the frame and the Teal Gyrocopter can be told apart; the shaded median of dE 23.7 and the lit p90 of dE 47 should go to the evidence doc.\n- **Issue 5 (a carried Flag hides its carrier's colour):** a note for the evidence doc, which only the orchestrator can write.\n\nAll checks pass after the edit: import, parse, launch, frozen, assets, regress ALL_OK, the five map scenarios, lint, and K6's windowed clearance check (110 props ok). I read a windowed top-down of the depot and compared it with the drawing.", "complete": true}
