{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/canister/water_canister.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_depot.tscn", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn (changed by this fix pass's first, interrupted run; kept and re-verified in this run, not edited again)", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg (rewritten by dev07.py import only: 235 classes, none new, none gone)"], "verification": ["dev07.py import: rc 0, class cache 235 classes, none new or gone, no .uid sidecars copied. The only ERRORs are the expected missing assets/ kit scenes in the scratch copy.", "dev07.py parse: rc 0, all 24 files ok.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, rc 0, no ERROR or WARNING.", "dev07.py frozen: every frozen file OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are byte-identical to the baseline and the soft four end RESULT ok (the Flag's new segment counts do not reach any text output).", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok (map_positions, map_mirror_data, edge_shore, edge_cliffs, ford_speed, base_exits, base_flag_run, cover_stops all PASS; depot_takes=5).", "Headless bounds probe (look/fix1-art-r2/aabb_probe.gd): every changed CylinderMesh keeps its bounds exactly (tank 8x5x8, platform 8.6, band 8.12, Flag body 0.56x0.72, Flag band 0.60, stand 0.56, depot tank 5.0, depot band 5.12). The three domes now reach their full radius because rings=3 keeps an equator ring: lid 0.2797 -> 0.28 m, roof 3.9955 -> 4.0 m, depot dome 2.462 -> 2.5 m. The Flag's outer edge is still its 0.30 m band, so the carried near edge stays at z 1.40.", "Windowed close-ups before and after, READ (look/fix1-art-r2/shots/*_before.png and *_after.png). The water tower, its Flag and the depot tanks now have 12-sided outlines with low faceted domes, matching the 12-sided depot posts. The tank still reads as one Orange object on dark legs from the salt flat (tower_far_after.png).", "Render totals in identical views, before -> after: draw calls 58/47/67/76 unchanged. Primitives: tower view 43,808 -> 15,248; Flag view 22,892 -> 14,444; tower from the salt flat 31,074 -> 12,210; depot 19,504 -> 10,024. No MeshInstance3D added or removed.", "Windowed map_fps (both views together): RESULT ok, fps_avg_steady 120.0, fps_min_steady 120.0 (120 Hz display), draw_calls_max 257 (earlier runs 257-258; budget 1,000), primitives_max 118,796 (earlier runs 173,084-176,168).", "Windowed --write-movie run of map_legibility after the edits: RESULT ok, 6 moments. Ford moment frame=542 (PNG f00000541) cropped, zoomed and READ (look/fix1-art-r2/ford_left_3x.png, ford_right_3x.png). Left view: the carried Teal Flag, median sRGB (26,103,110), against the ford water (145,206,223) measures CIE76 dE 40.1, luminance ratio 3.77. Right view: the Teal Motorbike, partly hidden behind the Orange Flag it carries, median (47,146,149) against (147,208,226) measures dE 27.8, ratio 2.18. Both read clearly.", "lint007.py all on the three edited .tscn files: 0 long functions, 0 missing ## lines, 0 over-long ## lines.", "No Godot process of mine left running. The only repo files touched in this run are the three .tscn files plus the class cache rewritten by dev07 import."], "deviations": ["ISSUE 2 (STANDARD, inline dressing materials): NOT FIXED, a decision for the orchestrator. The proposed fix needs three NEW files under src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/ (dressing_container.tres, dressing_container_rib.tres, rubber.tres). This pass may only edit existing materials/*.tres, and FIX-PASS RULE (a) forbids files the DESIGN does not name. Re-pointing the dressing at existing files would change the look the visual lens reviewed: container.tres, rust.tres and scrap.tres are three byte-identical untinted scrap materials (none carries the olive tint), and tower.tres is metallic steel (0.30, 0.31, 0.33), not black rubber. I found no written rule in story-007 or the layout and look design text that every Map mesh must reference a materials/ file, and the DESIGN itself puts inline colours in water_canister.tscn and fuel_can.tscn. If the three paths are allowed, the change is mechanical: in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art/gen_dressing.py, write the three sub_resources out unchanged as files and emit ext_resources in their place, then re-emit map_01_dressing.tscn.", "ISSUE 4 (depot posts): the issue quotes stale positions. This fix pass's first run, stopped when the workflow restarted for the TD-009 ruling, already regenerated map_01_dressing.tscn (generator look/fix1-art/gen_dressing.py). MultiMesh_depot_posts north pair: (+-9.76, -8.94) -> (+-7.8, -3.36). That is the nearest visible spot on the line from the north tank's centre (+-6.8115, -6.6222) through the drawn spot (+-7, -6), 0.1 m clear of the tank band (radius 2.56), on the depot ring as the drawing draws its posts. It is 2.76 m from the drawn spot; K6's spot was 4.0 m away. I kept it because it is closer to DESIGN 7, and it passed both that run's verification and this run's. The other four posts are unchanged at (+-6.4, 3.9) and (+-5, 5.9); the nearest Fuel Can is 2.46 m from a moved post. I cannot write the evidence doc (production/ is read-only for me), so the orchestrator should record: DESIGN (+-7, -6) lies inside FuelTankNorthWest/NorthEast; built at (+-7.8, -3.36).", "ISSUE 1 scope note: SphereMesh_fuel_tank_dome in map_01_depot.tscn was not at the default (32 segments, 8 rings) but was changed too, to 12/3. Otherwise its 32-sided rim (radius 2.5) would overhang the now 12-sided tank's flats (2.415 m) by up to 0.085 m. The 16-segment hatch (radius 0.5) was left alone.", "ISSUE 3 (WaterTower/Roof in color_meshes): no change, per the orchestrator's ruling that the roof dome is part of the Team-coloured tank.", "ISSUE 5 (ford vs Teal): verified in a windowed run, no change to textures/ford.tres. The rendered pairs (dE 40.1 and 27.8, luminance ratios 3.77 and 2.18) are well above the lens's albedo-based estimate of 18-24. The weaker right-view figure comes from the carried Orange Flag hiding most of the Teal Motorbike from behind, not from the water colour.", "Observations only, not changed because no lens in this pass names them: in the earlier run's top-down frame the pale depot ring marking reads weakly on the cream salt flat (late finding 1 would allow darkening it), and the stale 'the Lid keeps its cream' clause in base.gd and the orphan doc line in water_canister.gd remain."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 1 (art), run 2, Story 007 look. I fixed issue 1, held issue 2 back for an orchestrator decision, made no change for issues 3 and 4, and checked issue 5 in a windowed run with no change needed. Every regression check passes.\n\nIssue 1 (fixed): the water tower, the Flag and the depot tanks now use 12 radial segments, like the 12-sided depot posts beside them. Cylinders get rings 0 and domes rings 3, because an odd ring count keeps a ring on the equator.\n- src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn: CylinderMesh_tank, _platform and _band go from default 64 segments and 4 rings to 12/0; SphereMesh_roof goes from 64/32 to 12/3.\n- src/gameplay/canister/water_canister.tscn: CylinderMesh_body, _stand and _band go from default to 12/0; SphereMesh_lid goes from default to 12/3.\n- src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_depot.tscn: CylinderMesh_fuel_tank goes from default to 12/0; _fuel_tank_band from 64 to 12 segments (its rings were already 0); SphereMesh_fuel_tank_dome from 32/8 to 12/3, so its rim does not overhang the faceted tank.\n\nResults of issue 1:\n- Every cylinder keeps its bounds exactly. The domes now reach their full radius, and the Flag's carried near edge is unchanged.\n- Draw calls are unchanged in identical views. Primitives per frame fall by 35\u201365%.\n- map_fps across both views: 257 draw calls at most (budget 1,000), a steady 120 fps, and 118,796 primitives at most (before: about 175,000).\n\nIssue 2 (not fixed): moving the three inline dressing materials out needs three new files under materials/. This pass may only edit existing material files, and the fix rules forbid new files the DESIGN does not name. No existing material matches the olive tint or the rubber black. This is reported as a deviation, with the mechanical generator change described.\n\nIssue 3 (no change): the roof stays Team-coloured, per the orchestrator's ruling.\n\nIssue 4 (no code change in this run): this pass's first, interrupted run had already moved the two north depot posts from (\u00b19.76, -8.94) to (\u00b17.8, -3.36). That spot is closer to the DESIGN's (\u00b17, -6), which lies inside the north fuel tanks. I kept the move. The orchestrator needs to record those positions in the evidence doc, which I cannot write.\n\nIssue 5 (verified, no change): in a fresh windowed map_legibility movie, Teal reads clearly over the ford in both views. The left view measures dE 40.1 with a luminance ratio of 3.77; the right view measures dE 27.8 with a ratio of 2.18.\n\nChecks, all passing: dev07 import, parse, launch (no ERROR or WARNING), frozen, assets unchanged, regress ALL_OK, the five map scenarios, and lint on the three edited files.\n\nScratch tools, before/after shots, crops, movie frames and logs are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art-r2/.", "complete": true}
