{"files_created": [], "files_modified": [], "verification": ["Issue (ac-headless, UNVERIFIED, compound_base.tscn Garage walls): I verified it by looking at a fresh windowed frame. This verdict is mine and needs no code change. compound_base.tscn: before -> after unchanged.", "Windowed map_showcase on the current tree (1280x720, --write-movie, --quit-after 130, one Godot of mine, no other window open). Staged lines printed: frame=63 p1_appears_as_motorbike / p2_appears_as_buggy at (-125,0) and (125,0), and frame=124 garage_spawn. I READ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art-r3/movie_showcase/f00000066.png. In both views the Unit appears on the rust Garage floor (garage texture plates), which fills the Garage between its dark side walls. The tops of the Garage back wall and the compound back wall stay dark and quiet across the lower part of each view, as DESIGN 2 requires.", "I compared it with the drawing. I READ design/source/map01_colored.png and a 2x crop of Base A (look/fix1-art-r3/drawing_baseA_2x.png). The drawn Garage is a ribbed rust box inside dark scrap walls.", "Colours measured on the frame (patch medians, sRGB 0-255, CIE76; look/fix1-art-r3/measure.py). Garage floor: P1 (139,79,50), P2 (138,79,49). Against the drawn Garage roof (154,73,34) that is dE 13.5 and 13.6. Floor against the Garage side walls (55,37,30): dE 34.1. Against the compound back wall (50,32,26): dE 35.9. Against the sand (196,159,110): dE 31.7. For comparison, the drawing's own Garage-to-wall contrast is dE 29.8. Built walls against the drawn scrap wall (92,59,38): dE 16.5, darker than drawn, which matches 'its walls stay dark'.", "Fresh top-down of Base A (tools/topdown.gd, 52 m wide), READ at look/fix1-art-r3/topdown_baseA.png. The Garage is a rust-plate rectangle framed by the dark walls, where the drawing has its rust roof. The corner towers, the dashed rectangle and the tank are Orange; the walls are dark.", "What-if for the orchestrator, applied at run time with no repo change (look/fix1-art-r3/whatif.gd). The three Garage wall meshes of both Bases were given material_override = garage_floor.tres on the main scene's opening chase views, with the choice panels hidden. I READ look/fix1-art-r3/whatif_sheet_p1.png. The rust walls carry the floor's crack plates onto vertical walls and onto the Garage back wall's top, a strip just under each spawn's floor. The rust-coloured share of the lower P1 view goes from 0.130 to 0.248. The rust walls measure (115,65,42), which is dE 20.4 from the drawn roof (the floor is 13.5).", "dev07.py frozen: every frozen file OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED. dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames rc=0 noisy=[]; driving toy 60 frames rc=0 noisy=[].", "Not re-run, because nothing in the repo changed: import, parse, regress, and the five map scenarios. find shows no file under src/, tools/ or the class cache newer than the last full verification (look/fix1-art-r2: regress ALL_OK=True; map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases and map_cover all RESULT ok). Those results still describe the current tree.", "Observation: the showcase run was stopped mid-scenario by --quit-after 130. Its exit printed 'WARNING: 31 ObjectDB instances were leaked' and 'ERROR: 12 resources still in use at exit'. These come from the forced quit; the normal-exit launch check is clean.", "Repo writes during my runs: only production/session-logs/session-cost.md, written by the session hook (gitignored), not by me. assets/ is untouched; I ran no godot --import and opened no editor."], "deviations": [], "blockers": [], "summary": "The Garage reads as rust in the \"Unit appearing in a Garage\" frame, so I changed no files. AC-11 (\"its walls stay dark and its Garage rust, as drawn\") is met, and the walls stay on wall.tres.\n\n**What the frame shows.** I ran a fresh windowed capture of map_showcase on the current tree and looked at frame 66, where both Units appear. Each Unit appears on the rust Garage floor, which fills the Garage between its dark walls in both views. Measured colours:\n- The floor is (139,79,50), dE 13.5 from the drawing's rust Garage roof (154,73,34).\n- It stands apart from its surroundings: dE 34.1 from the Garage walls, 35.9 from the compound wall and 31.7 from the sand. The drawing's own Garage-to-wall contrast is dE 29.8.\n- The walls are darker than the drawn scrap wall (dE 16.5), as \"its walls stay dark\" asks.\n\nA fresh top-down of Base A shows the Garage as a rust rectangle framed by dark walls, where the drawing has its rust roof. The issue's premise is right: the rust comes from the floor alone. That is how DESIGN 2's \"the Garage rust (the garage texture)\" was built, and it reads as intended.\n\n**Why I kept the walls dark.** I also tried the alternative at run time, without touching the repo: the three Garage wall meshes of both Bases set to garage_floor.tres. It works against the design in three ways:\n- It puts the floor's crack plates on the Garage back wall's top in the lower part of every spawn view. DESIGN 2 explicitly says to keep that wall top dark and quiet.\n- It puts the same cracks on vertical walls, where the drawing shows ribbed metal.\n- It moves the walls further from the drawn rust (dE 20.4) and almost doubles the rust share of the lower view (0.130 to 0.248).\n\nIf the orchestrator still wants more rust, the smallest form is to point only BoxMesh_garage_side (the two side walls) at garage_floor.tres in compound_base.tscn. That is a material reference with no collider change, and it leaves the back wall's top dark. I have not built it.\n\n**Checks.** The frozen files are unchanged, assets/ is unchanged, and the launch is clean (main scene and driving toy, no errors or warnings). I did not re-run import, parse, regress or the five map scenarios because nothing changed. No repo file is newer than the previous fix pass's verification (regress ALL_OK, all five map scenarios pass), so its results still apply. The capture run was stopped at frame 130 on purpose, and its exit printed leak warnings from that forced quit; the normal launch check exits cleanly.\n\n**Late finding (2).** No issue in this pass names it, so I left it alone. A grep shows base.gd no longer contains \"Lid keeps\" or \"cream\".\n\nAll captures, the drawing crop and the probe scripts are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-art-r3/.", "complete": true}
