{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/ui/hud/player_hud.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg (rewritten by 'dev07.py import' only; the set of classes is unchanged: 235 classes, none added or removed, no .uid sidecars copied)"], "verification": ["API probe, headless (look/fix1-ui/probe_api.gd). get_children() of player_hud.tscn returns HitPointsBar, HitPointsLabel, FuelBar, FuelLabel and CanisterStatusLabel: all Controls, in the same order as the old hard-coded list, with no internal children (5 with internal, 5 without). Rect2().merge(Rect2(16,16,10,10)) gives (0,0,26,26), which is why _band_rect() keeps seeding from the hit-point bar.", "Windowed capture before and after the edit (look/fix1-ui/capture_ui.gd, adapted from K5's capture_k5.gd; split_screen.tscn at 1280x720; choice, main and destroyed frames). For both Players and all three frames, before and after: band (16,16) size (608,60); edge (8,8) to (632,84), inside the 640x720 view; band elements in identical order.", "Pixel comparison of after against before, inside Godot. In every frame and both views, 0 of the 64,000 band pixels (640x100) differ, and 0 of the 4,008 border pixels of the Team edge differ (max channel difference 0.0000).", "Edge colours: P1 edge pixel is dE 0.4 from Orange, P2 edge pixel is dE 0.1 from Teal; the Fuel amber is dE 32.6 from the Orange edge. Draw calls are unchanged: 299 in the choice frame, 313 in the main frame (both views), 303 in the destroyed frame.", "Read look/fix1-ui/frames/after_main.png: Player 1's band has an Orange rounded edge and Player 2's a Teal one. The edge encloses both bars and the status line. Green hit-point bar, amber Fuel bar, white text, nothing clipped.", "lint007.py all src/ui/hud/player_hud.gd: 0 functions over 40 lines or complexity 10, 0 declarations without ##, 0 ## lines over 100 columns.", "dev07.py import: rc 0, class cache 235 classes, none new or gone, no uid sidecars. Its ERROR lines are the kit scenes under assets/, which the scratch copy leaves out by design.", "dev07.py parse: 24 of 24 ok, including res://src/ui/hud/player_hud.gd.", "dev07.py launch: main scene for 120 frames and driving toy for 60 frames, both rc 0, no ERROR or WARNING.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are byte-identical; the soft four (canister_run, hud, round_over, canister_showcase) end RESULT ok and are also identical.", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all RESULT ok, 0 failed checks.", "dev07.py frozen: all frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "ps after the run: no Godot process left running. I started only my own children, one at a time, each with a timeout."], "deviations": ["Issue 1 (architecture): applied as proposed, plus three doc-only edits the change needed. (a) _band_elements()' doc said 'The five elements of the band'; it now says 'The elements of the band, in tree order: every Control child of this HUD...; today the hit-point bar and its line, the Fuel bar and its line, and the status line'. (b) _band_rect()' doc said 'holds its five elements'; it now says 'holds every element of the band. It starts from the hit-point bar, one of them, because merging an empty Rect2 would add the origin' (measured). The code of _band_rect() is unchanged. (c) The class doc's Team edge paragraph ends with a new sentence: 'A Control a later story adds under this HUD in player_hud.tscn joins the band, and the redraw when it changes size, with no change to this script.' It names player_hud.tscn because _ready() connects resized only for children present at _ready(), so Story 008's Token count must be a child in the scene. The paragraph was re-wrapped at 100 columns.", "Issue 2 (engine, informational): no code change. The orchestrator's ruling already accepts the band edge drawn in PlayerHud._draw() because the scene has no framing panel. The lens noted it had not rendered or measured the edge; this pass measured it for the evidence doc: edge (8,8) to (632,84) inside each 640x720 view, edge pixel dE 0.4 from Orange (P1) and 0.1 from Teal (P2), Fuel amber dE 32.6 from the Orange edge."], "blockers": [], "summary": "I fixed issue 1 in /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/ui/hud/player_hud.gd. Issue 2 needed no code change: the orchestrator's ruling already accepts the edge drawn in `_draw()`.\n\nIssue 1, before and after:\n- **`_band_elements()`:** it built a hard-coded list, `var elements: Array[Control] = [_bar, _hit_points_label, _fuel_bar, _fuel_label, _status_label]`. It now starts from an empty `Array[Control]` and appends each child of `get_children()` that is a Control. So Story 008's Token count, added to player_hud.tscn, joins the edge and its redraw on resize without editing this function.\n- **Class doc, Team edge paragraph:** \"the smallest rectangle that holds the two bars, their lines and the status line\" became \"the smallest rectangle that holds every element of the band (each Control child of this HUD)\". I also added one closing sentence saying a Control a later story adds in player_hud.tscn joins the band.\n- **Docs of `_band_elements()` and `_band_rect()`:** both said \"five\"; now they don't. The code of `_band_rect()` is unchanged. It still starts from the hit-point bar, because merging an empty `Rect2` widens it to the origin (measured: (0,0,26,26)).\n\nI confirmed the fix before applying it. A headless probe shows `get_children()` returns the same five Controls in the same order as the old list. A windowed before/after capture of the real main scene (choice, main and destroyed frames) shows the change is invisible:\n- band and edge rectangles are identical, with the edge at (8,8) to (632,84) inside each 640x720 view;\n- 0 of 64,000 band pixels and 0 of 4,008 edge pixels differ in either view;\n- draw calls are unchanged (313 in the main frame).\n\nI read the after frame: Orange edge on Player 1's band, Teal on Player 2's, hit-point green and Fuel amber kept.\n\nAll checks passed:\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| import | rc 0; class cache unchanged at 235 classes |\n| parse | 24 of 24 ok |\n| launch | clean |\n| regress | ALL_OK (`hud` identical) |\n| map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases, map_cover | all RESULT ok |\n| frozen | OK |\n| assets | unchanged |\n| lint | 0 findings |\n\nNo Godot process is left running.\n\nScratch files are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-ui/: the original file in orig/, the probes, the runner and the frames in frames/ (before_*.png and after_*.png).", "complete": true}
