{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_fps.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd"], "verification": ["Facts checked before rewriting: the story's positions table puts the canyon rock's south face at Z -20 and gives the road centreline (-102,-26) to (102,-26). The built RidgeEast CSG polygon in src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_cliffs.tscn has its north face at world Z 22 for x 46..95, which matches the table. GYRO_SPOTS is (-14,-4, 70,6), so the starts are 16 m from the canyon wall and 16 m from the ridge.", "Exact-once replacement guard: each old text matched exactly once. Diffs against the scratch copies of the originals show only the rewritten doc lines (map_fps.gd lines 30-31, 35, 39-41; map_showcase.gd lines 53-54, 64). Line counts unchanged: map_fps.gd 166, map_showcase.gd 295.", "grep for map_bases, map_edges and canyon_south in both scenarios: nothing left.", "dev07.py import: rc=0, class cache 235 classes, none new or gone, no .uid sidecars copied. Its ERROR lines are the kit vehicle scenes failing to load in the scratch copy, which leaves out assets/ by design.", "dev07.py parse: ok on all 14 changed scripts, including map_fps.gd and map_showcase.gd.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames rc=0 and driving toy 60 frames rc=0, no ERROR or WARNING.", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "lint007.py all on the two files: 0 functions over 40 lines or cc 10, 0 declarations without ## above, 0 ## lines over 100 columns.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True (strict twenty byte-identical, soft four RESULT ok), 34 s.", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok, failed=0.", "Headless smoke run of the edited scenarios: map_showcase RESULT ok (moments=15), map_fps RESULT ok (both legs ok; headless numbers are meaningless, as expected), map_legibility RESULT ok (moments=6).", "No windowed frame: nothing visual changed (comments only). ps shows no Godot left running; every run went through a timeout wrapper that could stop only its own process group."], "deviations": ["Issue 5, beyond the named fix: the line I rewrote in map_showcase.gd line 64 said Player 2's Gyrocopter starts 14 m north of the east ridge. The built RidgeEast face is at Z 22 and the start is at z 6, which is 16 m, so I corrected the number in the same edit.", "Issue 5, kept on purpose: map_fps.gd still names fps.gd on lines 11, 13 and 149. DESIGN 8 itself sets the rule as 'exactly as fps.gd does', and the issue's fix lists only the map_bases.gd, map_edges.gd and canyon_south mentions. The orchestrator can decide whether those three should go as well. map_legibility.gd names no other scenario, only its helper kits."], "blockers": [], "summary": "I fixed issue 5, the only one that needed a code change. The other four are settled by the rulings, so I changed nothing for them.\n\n**Issue 5 (scenario names in the scenarios' docs).** Five doc pointers to other scenarios are now replaced by coordinates or by the story's positions table. Doc comments only, no code changed:\n- **map_fps.gd lines 30-31.** Before: \"onto the lane z -15.5 map_bases.gd drives home (between the north wrecks and the canyon's south face, through both fords)\". After: \"onto the lane along z -15.5 (between the north wrecks and the canyon rock's south face at Z -20, through both fords)\".\n- **map_fps.gd line 35.** Before: \"14 m past its west mouth (map_edges.gd's road run on the positions table's centreline).\" After: \"14 m past its west mouth, on the road centreline of the story file's positions table.\"\n- **map_fps.gd lines 39-41.** Before: \"(x 70, map_bases.gd's raid start, 35 m out of the gate at x 105, clear of the long container)\". After: \"(x 70, 35 m out of the gate at x 105, clear of the long container)\". Rewrapped, still three lines.\n- **map_showcase.gd lines 53-54.** Before: \"from 14 m past the west mouth (map_edges.gd's road run), due east, through the table's four bends to 8 m past the last one.\" After: \"from 14 m past the west mouth, due east, through the four bends of the story file's road centreline to 8 m past the last one.\"\n- **map_showcase.gd line 64.** Before: \"canyon wall at x -14 (map_edges.gd's canyon_south run), and 14 m north of the east ridge.\" After: \"canyon wall (its face at Z -20) at x -14, and 16 m north of the east ridge (its face at Z 22).\" The 14 to 16 change is a correction: the built ridge face is at Z 22 and the start is at z 6.\n\n**Issues with no change:**\n- **Issue 1 (TD-009 in the runner).** Not reverted, per the ruling. Regress is ALL_OK, which confirms it doesn't change any baseline's text. Closing TD-009 in the register is the orchestrator's job, because docs/ is read-only to me.\n- **Issues 2 and 4 (map_showcase.gd at 295 lines).** Accepted by the ruling; the file stays at 295 lines.\n- **Issue 3 (drive_to_flags() in map_kit.gd).** Accepted by the ruling; map_kit.gd is untouched at 347 lines.\n- **Late findings.** No issue in my list named the depot ring's paint, the \"Lid keeps its cream\" clause in base.gd, or the orphan doc line in water_canister.gd, so I left them as they are.\n\n**Checks after the edits.** Every check passed:\n- import is clean.\n- parse is ok on every changed script.\n- launch has no ERROR or WARNING.\n- regress is ALL_OK.\n- All five Map 01 scenarios (map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases, map_cover) end RESULT ok.\n- frozen and assets are unchanged.\n- lint shows zeros on both files.\n- A headless smoke run of map_showcase, map_fps and map_legibility ends RESULT ok.\n\nThere was no windowed frame because nothing visual changed. My scratch files (the replacement script, the timeout wrapper and copies of the two originals) are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-tools/.", "complete": true}
