{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_legibility.gd"], "verification": ["python3 dev07.py import: rc 0; the class cache is unchanged (235 classes, none new or gone) and no .uid sidecars were copied. The ERROR lines it printed are the scratch copy having no assets/, which is expected.", "python3 dev07.py parse: ok on every changed .gd, including map_legibility.gd and map_showcase.gd.", "python3 lint007.py all on both files: 0 functions over 40 lines or complexity 10, 0 declarations without a ## line, 0 ## lines over 100 columns. One 101-column doc line was found and shortened. map_showcase.gd is 298 lines (was 295), map_legibility.gd 203 (was 197).", "python3 dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True (the strict twenty identical, the soft four RESULT ok).", "python3 dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok, failed=0.", "python3 dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, rc 0, no ERROR or WARNING. frozen: all OK. assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "Windowed --write-movie run of map_legibility (scratch look/fix1-tools-r2/movie_leg1, log legibility1.log): RESULT ok checks=0 failed=0 moments=6 worst_miss_m=0.80 destroyed=0; flag1 and flag2 AT_HOME at every moment. For all six moment lines PNG F matches F-1 (the hold) and F+1 differs. The frames are channel_p1_gyrocopter f68, channel_p2_gyrocopter f134, sand f200, salt_flat f266, canyon_road f332 and ford f398, copied to look/fix1-tools-r2/leg1/.", "I read all six legibility PNGs. In f68 the right view shows P1's Orange Gyrocopter 40 m from cam2 against the dark channel with the sea beyond. In f134 the left view shows P2's Teal Gyrocopter 40 m from cam1 against the same water. On sand, salt flat, canyon road and ford, each view shows at about 40 m the viewer's own Flag standing, the other Team's Motorbike unladen and a red Fuel Can, as three separate objects. Every camera-to-object distance is 40.6 to 40.8 m.", "Windowed --write-movie run of map_showcase (scratch look/fix1-tools-r2/movie_show1): RESULT ok moments=15 spawns=p1_motorbike,p2_buggy road_done=true,true rock_ticks=61,90 flag_ticks=167 destroyed=0.", "map_showcase frame checksums: for the nine STILLS moments PNG F matches F-1 and F+1 differs. Every frame= is now one below the verifier's (under_towers 189, gates 255, depot 651, fords 717). garage_spawn: frames 122 and 123 match and 124 differs, so it now names 123.", "map_showcase frames read: f00000123.png shows both Units in their Garages, and f00000651.png shows the depot staging (Motorbike at x -20, Truck at x 20).", "Draw calls: not re-measured. This pass changed two evidence scripts that are not in the main scene and no scene, material or src file, so the windowed main-scene draw-call figure cannot change."], "deviations": ["Issue 2: map_legibility now has two channel moments instead of one re-staged channel_gyrocopters moment. They are channel_p1_gyrocopter, Vector4(-40, 36, -40, 9.6), and channel_p2_gyrocopter, Vector4(-40, 9.6, -40, 36). One staging cannot show both Team colours against salt water. The channel is 28 m long (z 20 to 48) and opens into the sea, so the camera looking north up it would sit 13 m behind a Unit at z 54 or more, past the shore boundary. In each moment the camera in the ford looks south down the channel at the other Team's Gyrocopter 40.0 m away. The old moment name channel_gyrocopters no longer exists.", "Issue 3: I removed the drive onto the Flags from map_legibility (RAID_SPOTS, RAID_FACINGS, RAID_CRUISE, STOP_SPEED, LIMIT_TICKS, _flag_ticks, the drive_to_flags() call), the flags_taken moment, the canister_picked_up event line and the 'carries no Flag' premise. The DESIGN does not name them for this scenario, and map_showcase's flags_taken still stages the carried Flags. map_kit.gd drive_to_flags() now has one user, map_showcase, so the TD-006 ruling text ('for the two frame scenarios') is stale.", "Issue 3: map_legibility.gd added no new data table. At each surface it moves the viewer's own Flag as a staging step, the way the Cans are moved: to the Can's spot mirrored through the other Unit, 4 m away (3 m on the road and in the ford). The Flags go back with the Cans at the end, and their state stays AT_HOME throughout. Small additions: a _face_off() staging helper, a 'Flag picked up' premise item, a cam%d_to_flag span field, and MOMENT_FRAME_LAG.", "Issue 3: the salt_flat row of SURFACES moved 1 m south, from [(-84,12,-57,12), (-57,16,-84,16)] to [(-84,13,-57,13), (-57,17,-84,17)]. This keeps the new Flag beside Player 1 1.8 m clear of cam2's line of sight past the wreck at (-80, 5).", "Cosmetic artefact: because the staged Flags keep state AT_HOME, the HUD band in the four surface frames reads 'Your Water Canister is at home' while the Flag stands in the field. This is outside the 40 m check, and nothing else changed.", "Not fixed: the art lens's side note that a carried Flag hides almost all of a Motorbike from its own chase camera (k4/frames/cue_flag_crop.png) is about the Flag and Motorbike look (AC-12) in map_showcase's flags_taken. It is not tooling and not part of the asked fix."], "blockers": [], "summary": "I fixed all three issues by editing only the two evidence scenarios; all checks passed.\n\n**Issue 1 (DEFECT, frame= named the next staging's PNG): fixed in both files.** The cause was that a moment's line prints on the same main-loop iteration in which the next staging moves the Units, before that frame is drawn. Both files now have `const MOMENT_FRAME_LAG: int = 1`, and moment lines print `Engine.get_process_frames() - MOMENT_FRAME_LAG`, which is the hold's last PNG.\n- In map_showcase.gd, `_line(label)` became `_line(label, lag: int = 0)` and only `_moment()` passes the lag, so event= lines still name the PNG drawn after the event.\n- Both class docs now say frame= is \"the number of the PNG that shows the moment\" (previously \"the number of the next PNG\").\n- Checked by PNG checksums from two windowed `--write-movie` runs: every map_legibility moment, and the nine still showcase moments, name a frame identical to the one before it (the hold), and the frame after differs. I read showcase frames 123 (Garage spawn) and 651 (depot); both show their own staging.\n\n**Issue 2 (no Orange Gyrocopter over salt water): now shown, as two moments.**\n- One staging can't show both colours, because the camera looking north up the channel would sit past the Map's edge.\n- `channel_p1_gyrocopter` (f68) and `channel_p2_gyrocopter` (f134) each put one Gyrocopter in the west channel and the other in the west ford. The ford Unit's camera looks south at the channel's Gyrocopter 40.0 m away, with salt water behind it.\n- Both frames read: Orange (cam2) and Teal (cam1) each stand against the dark channel and sea. The Orange-over-salt-water pair can now be recorded as observed, not computed.\n\n**Issue 3 (Flags rode on the Units): restaged.**\n- At each of sand (f200), salt flat (f266), canyon road (f332) and ford (f398), the far scene in each view is the viewer's own Flag standing on the ground, the other Team's unladen Motorbike and a red Fuel Can, as three separate objects at 40.6 to 40.8 m. I read all four frames.\n- The Flags are moved as a staging step, like the Cans, and put back home at the end.\n- The drive onto the Flags and the `flags_taken` moment are gone from map_legibility.\n- The salt-flat row moved 1 m south to keep the Flag clear of the wreck at (-80, 5).\n\nRun result: `RESULT map_legibility ok moments=6 worst_miss_m=0.80`.\n\n**Checks run after the edits:** import (class cache unchanged), parse ok, lint 0 findings, regress ALL_OK=True, the five Map 01 scenarios all RESULT ok, launch clean, frozen OK, assets unchanged.\n\n**Frames for the retained set** are in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix1-tools-r2/`:\n- Legibility copies in `leg1/`.\n- The full showcase movie in `movie_show1/`.\n- showcase1.log keeps only the tail of the output (the run helper keeps the last 6,000 characters). The first SPLIT lines are lost, but the frame numbers are deterministic: each is one below the verifier's run, so garage_spawn is 123.\n\n**For you to decide:**\n- The moment name `channel_gyrocopters` no longer exists; the retained set needs the two new names.\n- `map_kit.gd` `drive_to_flags()` now has only map_showcase as a user, so the TD-006 wording (\"for the two frame scenarios\") is stale.\n- In the four surface frames the HUD still says the Water Canister \"is at home\" while the Flag stands in the field, because the staged Flags keep their AT_HOME state. It is cosmetic and outside the 40 m check.\n- I did not act on the art lens's side note that a carried Flag hides almost all of a Motorbike from its own camera. That is about the Flag's look (AC-12), not tooling.", "complete": true}
