{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "design/rules.md", "quote": "Today's build paints Player 1 blue and Player 2 red; the recolour is data and belongs to the story that next touches the Bases and the HUD (story 007, Map 01).", "problem": "This sentence in the rules of record is now false: Story 007 did the recolour. It also leaves out where the Team colours now live. Each Team colour is stored twice as the same literal value, Color(0.9, 0.45, 0.14) and Color(0.18, 0.6, 0.58). One copy is albedo_color in src/gameplay/split_screen/data/team_<team>_material.tres, which paints the Units (team_material) and the Bases, towers, dashes, tank, roof and Flag (Base.color_material). The other is border_color in src/ui/hud/data/team_<team>_edge.tres, which draws the HUD band edge and the choice panel edge. Nothing links the two files. The only mention is inside the class docs of player_hud.gd and unit_choice.gd. If the author retunes Orange in the material the inspector shows on the Units and Bases, the HUD and choice edges stay the old Orange. That one-file edit silently breaks AC-11 ('each Player's HUD and choice panel carry that Player's Team colour').", "fix": "Replace the sentence with: \"Story 007 made the Team colours data: each is the albedo_color of src/gameplay/split_screen/data/team_orange_material.tres / team_teal_material.tres (Units, Bases, Flags) and the border_color of src/ui/hud/data/team_orange_edge.tres / team_teal_edge.tres (each Player's HUD band and Unit choice panel); a Team colour is retuned in both of its files together.\" This is a doc change only, with no new resource or code."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "design/rules.md", "quote": "The style is low-poly: the models are built from Godot's built-in meshes and the textures are generated in code.", "problem": "The shipped Units are now built at run time from the author's kit under assets/art/. That contract is written down only in src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd and kit_unit_model.gd. A grep of design/, docs/, production/ and .claude/docs finds nothing. The game relies on these kit facts: (1) the private _m palette, read with get(); (2) the keys teal, orange, rim, teal_dark and orange_dark (accent), lamp, skull and screen (own surfaces), steel (fallback), and flag and rust_orange (remapped); (3) the rust_seed, steer_deg and pod_yaw_deg properties; (4) every part is a MeshInstance3D holding a PrimitiveMesh with a palette material_override, built synchronously in _ready(); (5) the Motorbike's tank-top _box(body, Vector3(0.36, 0.02, 0.28), Vector3(0, 1.015, 0.03), \"orange\") is the AC-12 heading cue. assets/ is the author's folder (story 007 note: 'ask before moving or editing anything in it'), so the author is the one who will edit the kit, and nothing they read tells them it feeds the game. Some edits break silently. A renamed steer_deg is skipped by KIT_POSE's 'if property in kit', so the front wheel is baked at the kit default of 14 degrees with no message. A moved tank top turns the cue into a Team-coloured patch, with only a console error.", "fix": "Add one bullet after that sentence: \"Since Story 007 the four Units' models are built when the main scene loads from the concept kit under assets/art/ by src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd (KitUnitModel), which relies on: each kit script's _m palette and its keys teal, orange, rim, teal_dark, orange_dark, lamp, skull, screen, steel, flag, rust_orange; the rust_seed, steer_deg and pod_yaw_deg properties; parts built in _ready() as MeshInstance3D of a built-in PrimitiveMesh with a palette material_override; and the Motorbike's 0.36 x 0.02 x 0.28 tank-top box at (0, 1.015, 0.03), its heading cue. An edit that changes these is reported as an error naming the kit scene, except a renamed pose property, which is skipped; change the model scenes (src/gameplay/units/models/*_kit_model.tscn) with it.\""}, {"kind": "DEFECT", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "quote": "built.hull = AABB(low, high - low)", "problem": "_build() does not report a kit that yields no foldable part. This happens if the kit builds its parts after _ready(), for example deferred, while _m is still set. In that case: no per-part error fires, because there are no parts; the part-remap count error fires only for the Motorbike, the one scene with a part_remap; and _palette_of() passes. _build() then returns an empty Built and get_or_build() caches it. The result is an invisible Unit for the whole process, with no message for the Buggy, Truck and Gyrocopter. For the Gyrocopter, low and high stay at Vector3.INF and -INF, so the hull becomes AABB(INF, -INF) and hull.end is NaN. _rise_target() then sizes a non-finite BoxShape3D and runs intersect_shape with it every physics tick. The DESIGN's rule is that a kit the build cannot read is a push_error naming the kit scene.", "fix": "In KitMerge._build(), right after the parts loop and before 'built.hull = AABB(low, high - low)', add: 'if surfaces.is_empty(): push_error(\"KitMerge: the kit scene '%s' built no part the palette can fold, so no model is built.\" % kit_path); return null'. get_or_build() then caches nothing, and KitUnitModel's existing null path ('if _built == null: return') applies."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Team colour values across the data files (material albedo_color against HUD/choice edge border_color)", "value": "Orange Color(0.9, 0.45, 0.14) and Teal Color(0.18, 0.6, 0.58) are identical in team_*_material.tres and team_*_edge.tres today. That makes 2 files per Team with no link between them (issue 1).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9", "what": "Map contract still holds with the look (SplitScreen field typed MapField, warm-up generic over match_controller.unit_types(), rise rule documented in MapField's contract)", "value": "split_screen.gd names no Map node and no KitMerge. unit_types() reads rules before begin(). map_field.gd documents that cliffs must be drawn colliders (CSG with use_collision) and water a bare StaticBody3D.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "MeshInstance3D / MultiMesh footprint per look sub-scene (static count from the .tscn files; draw calls not run by this lens)", "value": "compound_base: 44 MeshInstance3D per Base (88 for two). depot: 32 (20 ring dashes sharing one mesh and material, plus 12 fuel-tank parts) plus its Fuel Cans. dressing: 4 MeshInstance3D + 7 MultiMeshInstance3D (94 instances). cover: 12. terrain: 1 + 2 CSG. water: 3. cliffs: 5 CSG. fords: 2. Each Flag: 5. Each Fuel Can: 3. Each kit Unit: 2 (Accent 1 surface, Neutral 1 to 4 surfaces).", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "TD-006", "what": "Line counts of the three new look scenarios (limit: 'at most about 280 lines')", "value": "map_showcase.gd 298, map_legibility.gd 203, map_fps.gd 166. Runner split_screen_harness.gd grew from 542 to 698 lines across Story 007.", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "The concept-kit contract that src/ relies on is documented where the author of assets/art would find it", "value": "Documented only in kit_merge.gd and kit_unit_model.gd. A grep of design/, docs/, production/ and .claude/docs for KitMerge, kit_merge or _m returns nothing.", "verdict": "FAIL"}], "checked": "Architecture review only: I read the code, scenes and data and did not run Godot, as the role says. Files read: kit_merge.gd, kit_unit_model.gd, the four *_kit_model.tscn, the diffs of base.gd, unit.gd, split_screen.gd/.tscn, player_hud.gd, unit_choice.gd/.tscn, water_canister.gd, fuel_can.gd/.tscn, greybox_field.gd, the four UnitStats .tres, design/rules.md and the runner. Also read: map_field.gd, map_01.tscn, compound_base.tscn, map_01_dressing.tscn, map_01_depot.tscn, the 16 Map 01 materials and the sand and scrap textures, the Team materials and edges, the kit's wasteland_motorbike.gd and wasteland_palette.gd, story 008, the EPIC, and the frozen list (by name only; no sha256 check run).\n\nStory 008 needs no rewrite of this story's files:\n- MapField.token_stock is untouched.\n- SplitScreen._warm_up_models() is generic: it instances each model scene of match_controller.unit_types(), which reads rules before begin(). A Garage spawn mid-Round therefore hits KitMerge's cache.\n- PlayerHud's edge wraps every Control child, so story 008's Motorbike count joins the band (its 90 px rule) with no script change.\n- UnitChoice's edge follows the panel's draw signal as the choice rows grow with counts.\n- For the Flag rename, no src/ code of the look names the canister by string. map_showcase.gd (2 mentions) and map_legibility.gd (4) join 008's rename and re-run set.\n\nLater Maps:\n- Map materials are world-triplanar and position-independent. The exception is salt_flat.tres: its UVs run 0..1 over the 190 x 36 m plane, so a differently sized salt flat stretches it. The shared folder is named map_01/materials.\n- compound_base.tscn is reusable, with color_material set per instance.\n- The kit models are Map-independent. The rise rule ('a GeometryInstance3D collider on layer 32 is rock, a bare body is water') is stated in MapField's Map contract, so a Map author finds it.\n\nLower-priority remarks (not filed as issues):\n- The dressing props sit at absolute world coordinates under West and East, which have identity transforms. If a Base moves, its containers and tyre stacks stay behind; giving each group the Base's origin would keep them together.\n- The dressing's container and rib materials are inline sub_resources: an olive tint on scrap, computed at about (0.32, 0.37, 0.18) at the top of the ramp, so not Teal. Meanwhile materials/container.tres serves the cover, so the two container looks will drift on a retune.\n- Base.color_meshes as an explicit Array[MeshInstance3D] is sound and keeps Unit.TEAM_COLOUR_GROUP separate. The type excludes MultiMeshInstance3D (material_override lives on GeometryInstance3D), but engine instancing of a shared mesh plus material makes that moot today.\n- base.gd's class doc summarises AC-11 as 'and on the water tower's roof', but AC-11 names the tank (per AC-12). Painting the Roof is beyond the DESIGN's K2 list: a question for the scope lens.\n- truck_kit_model.tscn sets offset Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286), which the DESIGN does not name (it names only the Gyrocopter's z -0.28): for the scope and fidelity lens.\n- The part remap is keyed by geometry, reports a miss loudly, and is documented in both classes. The cache key covers path, seed and both remaps.\n- _m is read with get() as the DESIGN binds. The palette's public static materials(seed) would survive a rename of _m.\n- KitUnitModel is not @tool, so a model scene opened in the editor is empty and model_scale or offset retunes are blind until the main scene runs.\n- map_showcase.gd is 18 lines over 'about 280'.\n\nExit leaks: of the run logs checked, only fix1-art-r3/movie_showcase.log (a --write-movie run) reports exit leaks ('12 resources still in use at exit', '31 ObjectDB instances were leaked'). The other main-scene logs checked (k7 window_map_fps_17, headless_map_fps_1/2, headless_map_showcase_2, headless_map_legibility_2, fix1-tools-r2 showcase1 and legibility1) show none, so I do not attribute the leak to KitMerge's static cache.\n\nNot run, left to the other lenses: regress, the five map scenarios, frozen, draw calls, and frames."}
