{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "tools/evidence/split_screen_harness.gd", "quote": "if _held.get(key, false) == pressed and Input.is_physical_key_pressed(key) == pressed:  ...  func _reassert_held_keys() -> void:  (called from advance_ticks() after every physics_frame)  ...  func _send_key(key: Key, pressed: bool) -> void:", "problem": "The TD-009 held-key re-assertion is not named by the look DESIGN, which lets the runner grow only for registering map_showcase, map_legibility and map_fps and for the greybox restores (GREYBOX_MODELS, _apply_greybox_models(), the body-material put-back). It adds set_key()'s second clause, _send_key(), _reassert_held_keys(), a call after every physics_frame in advance_ticks() and two doc paragraphs, about 45 of the runner's growth from 542 lines at HEAD to 698. It changes the per-tick path of every scenario, the 24 baselines included, so only regress proves it invisible. TD-009 is registered debt that is still Open in docs/tech-debt-register.md. Raised in the round-1 engine lens and unchanged.", "fix": "Revert the TD-009 additions: the 'and Input.is_physical_key_pressed(key) == pressed' clause in set_key(), _send_key() (back inline in set_key()), _reassert_held_keys() and its call in advance_ticks(), the class-doc paragraph that starts 'A window that loses focus makes the engine release every pressed key' and the TD-009 sentence in the _held doc. Leave TD-009 Open. Or the orchestrator names it in the DESIGN, regress shows ALL_OK, and TD-009 is marked Resolved in the register."}, {"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn (and the class doc and color_meshes doc of src/gameplay/maps/base.gd)", "quote": "NodePath(\"Garage/Marking/Dash14\"), NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\")]   and in base.gd: \"## the dashed rectangle in front of the Garage and on the water tower's roof, its walls dark and its\"", "problem": "DESIGN 3 names the four corner towers and the dashed rectangle as the further Team-coloured meshes, plus the tank as the beacon. WaterTower/Roof (SphereMesh_roof, radius 4, y 13.3, up to 14.7) is a fifth, unnamed Team-coloured part, so each Base paints 19 color_meshes entries (4 towers, 14 dashes, the Roof) where the design lists 18. base.gd states it in three places: the AC-11 sentence ('and on the water tower's roof'), the WaterTower paragraph ('its Roof (one of color_meshes)') and the color_meshes doc ('and its water tower's roof'). Raised in round 1 and unchanged.", "fix": "Remove NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\") from color_meshes so the Roof keeps its tower.tres dark steel. In base.gd delete 'and on the water tower's roof' (AC-11 sentence), change 'its Roof (one of color_meshes)' to 'its Roof' and delete ', and its water tower's roof' from the color_meshes doc. If the author wants the dome in the Team colour, the orchestrator records that in the DESIGN instead."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "quote": "@export var rise_rate: float = 6.0   (same pattern: rise_clearance = 0.25, settle_rate = 2.0, rise_lead_seconds = 0.4, rise_lead_max = 8.0, rise_margin = 2.0, rise_mask = 32, rust_seed = 11)", "problem": "The standard is no rate or tuning number as a literal in a .gd under src/. Eight tuning exports carry real values as their script defaults, and gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn (and all four scenes for rust_seed) store the same numbers again, so two places hold each value. Every other tuning export in src/ defaults to an inert 0.0 with the value in data (unit_stats.gd max_speed = 0.0, chase_camera_settings.gd follow_sharpness = 0.0, ford_settings.gd speed_fraction = 0.0, fuel_can_settings.gd refill_amount = 0.0), and the HUD docs say 'Required, with no default'.", "fix": "Set rust_seed, rise_mask, rise_clearance, rise_rate, settle_rate, rise_lead_seconds, rise_lead_max and rise_margin to 0 / 0.0 in kit_unit_model.gd and say 'Required, with no default' in their docs. Nothing changes at run time: gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn stores every rise_* value and all four model scenes store rust_seed = 11; the other three types never enable the rise."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "quote": "static func _palette_of(kit: Node3D, kit_path: String) -> Dictionary:  (also 'var palette: Dictionary = _palette_of(kit, kit_path)' and 'palette: Dictionary' in _surface_for, _material_of, _tone_of, _colour_of; doc: 'The palette stays an untyped Dictionary in every function that reads it ... an untyped Dictionary does not assign to a typed one.')", "problem": "The lens requires no bare Dictionary where a type is known, and the palette's is known: kit key (String) to Material. The doc's reason holds for assigning the kit's untyped _m directly to a typed variable, not for copying it once. Five signatures and one local stay untyped because of it.", "fix": "In _palette_of() copy the kit's entries once into a Dictionary[String, Material] (loop the keys, String(key) and 'as Material', skipping values that are not a Material) and return that. Type the local in _build() and the four parameters Dictionary[String, Material], and delete the doc sentence about staying untyped. The mesh arrays (Array from get_mesh_arrays()) and the part-remap entries (mixed Vector3 and String values) legitimately stay untyped. No behaviour change."}, {"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn", "quote": "offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286)", "problem": "DESIGN 5 names exactly one offset, the Gyrocopter's z -0.28. The Truck's z 0.1286 is an unnamed data value. A round-1 fix probe produced it (hull centre z -0.00003 once applied) to centre the hull on the 2.4 x 4.4 collider. The DESIGN and the reports I read do not record it, and the Motorbike and Buggy have none.", "fix": "The orchestrator adds 'the Truck offset z 0.1286 (centres its hull on the collider)' to the DESIGN and the evidence doc, or the line is removed."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "tools/evide