cision. Preferred: add the roof dome to the design block as part of the Team-coloured tank, so the block and the code agree. Otherwise delete NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\") from color_meshes in compound_base.tscn and the phrase 'and its water tower's roof' from the color_meshes doc in base.gd; the dome then keeps tower.tres dark steel."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "quote": "## Roughness of the neutral fold's material, which every folded neutral part shares.\nconst NEUTRAL_ROUGHNESS: float = 0.8\n## Metallic of the neutral fold's material, which every folded neutral part shares.\nconst NEUTRAL_METALLIC: float = 0.1", "problem": "LOW. DESIGN K4 asks for 'the neutral material's roughness and metallic as named constants with their source'. DARK_TONE's doc states its source ('measured on 4.7.2; the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run'); these two docs say what the constants are and give no source. The values themselves match the look preflight's tested reference (ref/kit_merge.gd lines 78-79: roughness 0.8, metallic 0.1), so the code is right and only the provenance is missing.", "fix": "Append the source to both doc comments, wrapped at 100 columns, for example: '(0.8, the value of the look preflight's tested variant C, measured on 4.7.2; the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run)', and the same for 0.1. No value changes."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-10 (textures)", "what": "The nine NoiseTexture2D files under maps/map_01/textures/ against the look preflight's tested recipes, then generated in 4.7.2", "value": "All nine byte-identical to preflight-look/a/gl/recipes (diff). Every one produced a non-null image after 1 frame. Sizes: 512x512 seamless, salt_span 2048x388 non-seamless. Mean colours: sand (0.669,0.534,0.347), road (0.610,0.448,0.279), sea (0.052,0.154,0.262), salt_span (0.738,0.711,0.642). No salt.tres or salt_big.tres. No uid lines, readable ids. No get_image() anywhere in src/ or tools/.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 (materials)", "what": "Every material under maps/map_01/materials/, loaded and read back", "value": "BaseMaterial3D.TEXTURE_FILTER_LINEAR_WITH_MIPMAPS_ANISOTROPIC = 5 and every textured material has texture_filter 5, roughness 1.0 and white albedo, except wall.tres (tint 0.55). Triplanar and world-triplanar are true with uv1_scale 1/32 for sand, road, ford, rock and ridge; 1/16 for scrap, rust, container, wall and garage_floor; 1/64 for sea and channel (identical parameters). salt_flat.tres has no triplanar, scale 1. marking, tower and fuel_tank have no texture. No transparency anywhere (ford.tres is opaque).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 (loads)", "what": "54 new or changed .tscn and .tres, loaded with ResourceLoader (CACHE_MODE_IGNORE) in a headless script and every PackedScene instantiated; static scan of the headers", "value": "0 ERROR and 0 WARNING lines across the whole 253-line probe output. All 54 loaded and every scene instantiated. No uid= lines in any new or changed file. No opaque 'N_xxxxx' ids in new files (the one hit, motorbike_stats.tres 1_g7j1u, pre-exists at HEAD). No unique_id in new files. New .gd files carry .uid sidecars. Class cache lists KitMerge and KitUnitModel.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "Layout AC-1..9 and DEPENDENCY", "what": "dev07.py parse, launch, regress (full), new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover, frozen, assets", "value": "Parse ok on 24 files. Launch (main scene 120 frames and driving_toy) has no ERROR or WARNING. Regress ALL_OK: strict twenty identical, soft four RESULT ok. The five Map 01 scenarios: map_layout ok, map_edges ok, map_ford ok, map_bases ok, map_cover ok, all failed=0. Frozen files all OK. assets/ UNCHANGED. lint007: 0 declarations without ##, 0 doc lines over 100 columns.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11, AC-14 (KitMerge build)", "what": "The four kit models built through KitMerge in the tree (headless), plus the cache", "value": "Accent has 1 surface (motorbike 1594 verts, buggy 4434, truck 2484, gyro 1958) with 2 distinct vertex colours (white and the 0.68 tone). Neutral has 3 surfaces (fold, lamp or screen, skull). Faces consistently oriented with the stored normals (faces_pos=0 in all four; the inverse-transpose bake is right), 0 non-unit normals. Accent is in group team_colour; Neutral is in none. Fallback material: steel (0.66,0.67,0.68), vertex colour sRGB, no override. Kit freed: node and orphan counts unchanged (1->1, 0->0) after each model. A second instance costs 0.02-0.03 ms and shares the same ArrayMesh. First build 2.9-5.3 ms headless.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11, AC-12 (remaps)", "what": "Whether each remap hits exactly the intended parts: inspected the four kit scenes directly and read the KitMerge cache", "value": "The tank-top patch rule (BoxMesh 0.36x0.02x0.28 at (0,1.015,0.03)) matches exactly 1 part in the Motorbike kit (key orange, remapped to lamp) and 0 in the other three. Key 'flag' is 1 part (buggy) and 'rust_orange' 1 part (truck), mapped to the orange accent and steel_dark. No kit part is left out (odd_parts=[] for all four). The keys of the neutral fold are rust_dark, leather, rubber, tread, gunmetal, steel, steel_dark, hole, glass; none is a Team colour or red.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 (Unit painting)", "what": "The real Unit.spawn() for all four stats, with and without team_material (unchanged _swap_model and _paint_team_colour)", "value": "With Team Teal: Accent.material_override is the Team material and Neutral's is null, for 4 of 4 types, and the model scale is as designed (0.98, 0.72, 0.735, 0.66). Without a team_material: no override and the fallback steel shows.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 (Base paint, base.gd)", "what": "compound_base.tscn instanced with team_orange_material; base.tscn instanced", "value": "painted=22: Pad, Tank (beacon), Canister/Body and 19 color_meshes (4 corner towers, Dash01..14, WaterTower/Roof). The walls stay unpainted. The greybox base.tscn has color_meshes size 0 (empty by default). _paint_color_meshes() runs in _ready() and skips an unassigned entry with a warning. The export is documented.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13 (rise over rock, engine facts)", "what": "What intersect_shape returns for Map 01's layer-32 bodies, and a real Gyrocopter spawned through Unit.spawn() and driven across RidgeCentre (southbound) and the canyon walls (northbound) with the rise code, checked each tick against a physics oracle of the hull footprint", "value": "The five cliff polygons come back as the CSGPolygon3D node itself (a GeometryInstance3D, top y = 2.0, up to 5 duplicate results, cap 64). The two channels come back as StaticBody3D and are ignored by the rule. Ridge crossing: 255 overlap ticks, 0 with the model's lowest point below the rock top, worst clearance 0.250 m (= rise_clearance), max rise 1.47 m, rise began at tick 48 against first overlap at tick 75. Canyon crossing: 316 overlap ticks, 0 violations, clearance 0.250 m, rise began at tick 37 against overlap at tick 64. The code reads physics only from _physics_process and never touches the collider.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 (KitMerge error paths)", "what": "Defensive reads, driven on purpose", "value": "Null kit scene, a kit with no _m, a host outside the tree and a part whose material is not in the palette each give one push_error naming the kit scene (and the part, for the last); the first three return null with nothing cached. A part remap matching 0 parts gives an error naming the kit scene and the entries. The host is left with 0 children in every case.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "Runner greybox restores", "what": "Code reading of split_screen_harness.gd _ready() plus regress", "value": "_apply_greybox_models() runs on the shared UnitStats before SPLIT_SCENE.instantiate(). _apply_greybox_composition(split) (Map freed, field re-pointed, both Team materials put back) runs right after instantiate() and before add_child(split). All 24 baselines identical.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14 and windowed behaviour", "what": "Windowed draw calls and frame rate; the GPU-readback cost of get_mesh_arrays() in the warm-up; static _cache release at exit with a real renderer; how the PlayerHud and UnitChoice Team edges render; the camera-to-model sight line for the Gyrocopter", "value": "Not measured in this lens: headless uses the dummy renderer, and the windowed runs and frames belong to the other lenses and the orchestrator. The earlier windowed map_* runs left empty .err files, which is suggestive only.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Method: read-only. One headless Godot process at a time through python3 subprocess timeouts. No window opened, no import in the repo, no process of anyone else touched. Scratch is under look/lens-engine/ (probe_engine.gd, probe2.gd, driver.py and their outputs).\n\nRead in full: kit_merge.gd, kit_unit_model.gd, base.gd, the split_screen.gd, unit.gd, split_screen.tscn, HUD, choice, canister and fuel-can diffs, the harness diff, compound_base.tscn, map_01.tscn, all four kit model scenes, the Team materials and edge styles, all nine textures and every map material, the author's palette and motorbike kit, and the first 50 lines of map_showcase.gd.\n\nRan:\n- A headless probe that loads and instantiates all 54 changed or new .tscn/.tres, reads the material fields and generates the textures.\n- The kit builds, with leak counts and normal-orientation checks.\n- The real Unit.spawn() for all four types, with and without team_material.\n- Base painting.\n- intersect_shape against the real Map.\n- Two real Gyrocopter crossings.\n- KitMerge error paths.\n- dev07 parse, launch, frozen, assets and lint007.\n- The full 24-baseline regress and the five Map 01 scenarios.\n\nFinding: the engine and API surface the look uses all behaves as the code assumes on 4.7.2. Nothing in the engine lens fails. The three issues above are low-severity differences between the binding design block and what was built.\n\nNot issues, noted for the orchestrator:\n- lint007 flags KitMerge._commit as 45 lines LONG. It is lines 298-313; the lint counts through the inner classes that follow it.\n- map_showcase.gd is 298 lines against the design's 'about 280'. I did not flag it.\n- PlayerHud draws its Team edge in _draw() rather than applying a StyleBox to a band panel. This is justified: player_hud.tscn has no such panel, and the class doc says so.\n- Fix rounds 1 to 3 had already adjusted the models; everything above was measured on the files as they stand now.\n\nNot covered: windowed behaviour, the visual frames, the depot, cover and dressing scenes beyond load and instantiate, and the HUD edge appearance."}
