{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/channel.tres", "quote": "map_legibility channel_p2_gyrocopter, frame 134, view 1 at 40 m: teal_rotor_w obj (0.10,0.40,0.43) vs channel water (0.23,0.35,0.48) dE76 21.4 / 22.7; teal_gyro_body obj (0.14,0.46,0.48) vs (0.19,0.26,0.37) dE76 30.1 / 32.1 (Orange Gyrocopter over the same water: 66.9 to 69.9)", "problem": "The Teal Gyrocopter over the navy channel water is the weakest Unit-over-ground pair in the whole legibility set. Its body clears the bar at dE 30 to 32, but that is 14 points below the 44 to 46 the look preflight measured for Teal over the navy sea with flat proxies. The real model's accent carries the 0.68 dark tone and shading. Its thin west rotor blade measures 21 to 23 dE, under the 25 bar, and almost disappears against the water. PNGs: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/v2_leg_channel_p2_gyrocopter_f134.png and v2_leg_channel_p2_gyrocopter_band.png (2x zoom of the 40 m band). Every other pair measured 27.9 or more.", "fix": "No code change inside the binding design: DESIGN 2 fixes the navy recipe and DESIGN 5 fixes the 0.68 accent tone. Record it in the Story 007 evidence as the weakest pair (Teal Gyrocopter over the channels at 40 m: body dE 30 to 32, rotor blade 21 to 23, with the PNG paths above) so the author judges it at AC-15."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd", "quote": "wc -l: 298 tools/evidence/split_screen/map_showcase.gd (DESIGN 8: \"at most about 280 lines\")", "problem": "The showcase scenario is 18 lines (6 percent) over the cap DESIGN 8 sets. It is not a visual defect, and it runs correctly: RESULT map_showcase ok checks=0 failed=0 moments=15 rock_ticks=61,90 flag_ticks=167. It is flagged because the cap is part of the binding design. map_legibility.gd (203 lines) and map_fps.gd (166 lines) are within it.", "fix": "Bring map_showcase.gd to 280 lines or fewer by tightening doc comments or folding a helper, without changing anything it prints. Re-run it and confirm the same RESULT line and the same frame= values for the 15 moments."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-14", "what": "map_fps run 1, windowed 1280x720 (no movie, driven from python3 with a timeout), RESULT line", "value": "fps_avg_steady=120.0 fps_min_steady=120.0 fps_min=85.0 (first second, excluded) refresh_hz=120.0 draw_calls_max=257 primitives_max=118796 samples=17 legs=flat_and_road:ok,into_bases:ok", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "map_fps run 2, back to back", "value": "fps_avg_steady=120.0 fps_min_steady=120.0 fps_min=86.0 draw_calls_max=257 primitives_max=118796; draw calls per sample 146 to 257 for both views together (peak at t=1.03 with both Units at their Bases), against a 1,000 budget", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14 (cost detail)", "what": "MeshInstance3D count per sub-scene (from the .tscn text)", "value": "compound_base 44 (26 with shadows off; 2 instances); depot 32 (20 off); cover 12; dressing 4 MeshInstance3D + 7 MultiMeshInstance3D; terrain 1 + 2 CSG; water 3; cliffs 5 CSG; ford 1 (2 instances); Flag 5 (2 instances); Fuel Can 3. No sub-scene threatens the budget at 257 total.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over sand (map_legibility f200), dE76 from the object's Team-colour or red pixels to clean ground on both sides", "value": "Teal Unit 53.8/54.6; Orange Unit 38.0/37.8; Orange Flag 34.7 (the other sample landed in shadow); Teal Flag 56.2/56.8; Fuel Can 58.3/60.3 and 65.0/62.9", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over the salt flat (f266)", "value": "Teal Unit 46.5/46.6; Orange Unit 62.8/63.4; Orange Flag 62.7/60.1; Teal Flag 54.2/54.8; Fuel Can 85.3 and 82.4", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over the canyon road (f332)", "value": "Orange Unit 28.0/27.9/28.7 (weakest surface pair, above 25); Orange Flag 31.5/30.7; Teal Unit 56.3; Teal Flag 51.1/49.6; Fuel Can 51.8 and 48.5 on the road", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "40 m legibility over the ford (f398)", "value": "Teal Unit 35.3/38.9; Teal Flag 33.3/38.1; Orange Unit 91.9; Orange Flag 81.1; Fuel Can 94.8 and 105", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Gyrocopter over salt water (channel) at 40 m (f68, f134)", "value": "Orange Gyrocopter body 68.6/66.9, rotor 69.9; Teal Gyrocopter body 30.1/32.1, east rotor blade 29.2/32.6, west rotor blade 21.4/22.7 (under 25: see issue)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Motorbike cream heading cue: cream pixels in the bike's region from the chase camera", "value": "60 px while carrying the enemy Flag (flags_taken f1938, both views); 60 px without a Flag (depot f651, garage_spawn f123). The carried Flag hides the bike's rear but not the tank-top patch.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Flag geometry and colour (water_canister.tscn and sheet)", "value": "Team-coloured body cylinder radius 0.28 m, dark bands 0.30 m, total height 0.88 m. Reads as a Team-coloured banded tank in both colours (v2_units_flags_can_both_teams_sheet.png, v2_show_under_towers_f189.png). The only other cylinders near it are the black depot posts.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12/AC-13", "what": "Water tower: lowest point of the tank, and landmark visibility", "value": "Tank CylinderMesh height 5.0 at y 10.8, so its lowest point is 8.3 m (at least 8.0). Each Base's tower reads clearly in its own colour from the salt flat's centre (f585), a corner (f321) and the depot (f651). The other three corner frames were not read.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Units visible to their own camera: in a Garage, under a tower, on the road's bends, Gyrocopter over rock", "value": "Garage spawn f123: Orange bike against the garage floor, dE 39 to 52. Under towers f189: both Units visible between the legs. Bends p2_bend_3 f1002 and p1_bend_2 f1067: both visible. p1_over_rock f1553: Orange Gyrocopter over the canyon wall and Teal over the ridge, both visible with shadows on the rock.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Gyrocopter visible on every tick of each crossing and never inside rock", "value": "I saw single frames only. The scenario reports rock_ticks=61,90. The per-tick ray proof belongs to the K4 slice and was not re-run here.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "HUD and choice-panel Team edges, and amber vs Orange (f0, f123)", "value": "Rendered P1 edge (0.90,0.45,0.14), P2 edge (0.18,0.60,0.58). Fuel amber (0.96,0.70,0.18) is dE76 32.6 from the Orange edge in the frame. The HP bar stays green (0.40,0.82,0.38). Choice panels carry the same edges.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "One Team colour per Unit, Base, tower and marking; neutrals in neither colour and not Fuel Can red", "value": "Sheet: all 4 kit models in Orange and in Teal, none mixed; the Buggy pennant takes the Team accent and the Truck drum is grey. Frames and Base top-downs: corner towers, tank and dashed Garage marking in the Base colour. Walls are dark, the Garage floor rust, the depot tanks grey on rust, posts black, containers olive, tyres black, boulders rust. The cover pieces rust and the depot's flanking barriers are both rust (the drawing's teal east barrier was correctly not copied). The sea is navy.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Top-down at 330 m (2640x800) next to design/source/map01_colored.png, and the kit models next to vehicle-design.png", "value": "Same zoning and palette family: sand island, rust canyon with a pale road, darker ridge, cracked salt flat (no visible tile repeat), cyan fords, navy channels and sea (a deliberate DESIGN change from the drawing's teal-blue), Orange Base A west and Teal Base B east. Kit forms match the concept sheet, flat-shaded.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "First frame textured; no magenta; no shimmer or z-fight flicker on still holds", "value": "Showcase movie f0 is fully textured (f0 differs from f1, and f1 to f3 are identical). No magenta in any frame read. At all 6 legibility holds the md5 of frames F-2, F-1 and F are identical. No pad bleeds through the Garage floor in the Base top-downs.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-15 support", "what": "Staged scenarios run windowed with --write-movie", "value": "map_showcase RESULT ok checks=0 failed=0 moments=15 spawns=p1_motorbike,p2_buggy road_done=true,true rock_ticks=61,90 flag_ticks=167 (1941 PNGs). map_legibility RESULT ok moments=6 worst_miss_m=0.80 (401 PNGs).", "verdict": "PASS"}], "checked": "The rendered Map 01 meets AC-10 to AC-14 as far as I could measure it. I found two items to flag: the Teal Gyrocopter's rotor over the channel water reads weakly at 40 m, and map_showcase.gd is 298 lines against the design's cap of about 280.\n\nAll my files are under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/. I wrote nothing in the repo. Every Godot run was my own child process with a timeout, one at a time, after checking that no other Godot was running; none were left running.\n\nWhat I ran and read:\n1. map_showcase and map_legibility windowed at 1280x720 with --write-movie (v2work/movie_show, v2work/movie_leg; logs v2work/show.log and leg.log). Each staged moment is copied as v2_show_<moment>_f<N>.png and v2_leg_<moment>_f<N>.png, plus v2_leg_<moment>_band.png (2x zoom of the 40 m band) and v2_show_first_frames_f0/f1/f2/f30.png.\n2. Top-down snapshots with the scratch tools/topdown.gd: whole Map at 2640x800, --width=330 (v2_topdown_whole_map_330m.png), plus v2_topdown_baseA_50m.png, v2_topdown_baseB_50m.png and v2_topdown_depot_40m.png.\n3. A scratch probe (v2work/units_sheet.gd) showing the 4 kit models in both Team colours, both Flags and a Fuel Can, under the Map's own Sun and environment on sand (v2_units_flags_can_both_teams_sheet.png).\n4. map_fps windowed twice back to back (v2work/fps1.log, fps2.log).\n\nI read these images: map01_colored.png, vehicle-design.png, the whole top-down, Base A top-down, the units sheet, first frame f0, garage_spawn, under_towers, gates, towers_north_west, towers_centre, depot, fords, the p1_bend_2 and p2_bend_3 road bends, p1_over_rock, flags_taken, and the ford and channel_p2 legibility bands.\n\nColours were sampled with pure Python (sips to BMP, CIE76 dE against clean ground on both sides of each object): v2work/analyze.py, an2.py, an3.py. An earlier pass that averaged a ring around each object mixed in the Unit's own tyres and shadow; those figures are superseded by the clean-ground ones in the measurements.\n\nStatic checks: tank lowest point 8.3 m; Flag radius 0.28 (bands 0.30) and height 0.88 m; Fuel Can (0.78,0.08,0.10); Team materials as designed; map material and dressing colours. Two dressing tints in map_01_dressing.tscn are written as teal-ish values, (0.55,1,0.9) and (0.38,0.7,0.62). They multiply rust textures and render olive or brown, so nothing neutral renders in a Team colour.\n\nResults:\n- **AC-14:** both runs give fps_min_steady 120 (the display cap is 120 Hz) and at most 257 draw calls for both views, against 1,000.\n- **AC-13:** every Flag, Fuel Can and Unit pair over sand, salt flat, canyon road and ford is at dE 27.9 or more. The weakest is the Orange Unit on the canyon road at 28.\n- **Gyrocopter over water:** the Orange one is at 67 to 70. The Teal body is at 30 to 32, but its west rotor blade is 21 to 23, under the 25 bar (issue 1).\n- **Heading cue:** the Motorbike's cream patch shows 60 px whether or not it carries a Flag.\n- **Look:** the first frame is textured, there is no magenta, the still holds are frame-identical, and the water towers read as landmarks.\n\nNot covered by me:\n- regress, the five map scenarios, frozen, assets and lint belong to other verifiers; I only ran the three new scenarios.\n- The per-tick proof that the Gyrocopter stays visible and never enters rock.\n- Shimmer while moving (I checked still holds only).\n- The road-bend frames other than the two above (p1_bend_1, p1_bend_3, p1_bend_4, p2_bend_1, p2_bend_2, p2_bend_4) and the three other tower-corner frames.\n- The lowest point of the tower braces: I did not read the brace mesh size, though the frames show the braces above the Units.\n\nNotes for the art-direction lens, not raised as defects:\n- The Garage floor uses a cellular plate texture, while the drawing shows a ribbed roof. The design chose that recipe.\n- A carried enemy Flag covers most of the Motorbike's body from the chase camera, so its colour dominates that view. The cream cue stays visible.\n- The Flag's banded cylinder shape is close to the depot's black posts; colour is what tells them apart."}
