{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/garage_floor.tres", "quote": "albedo_texture = ExtResource(\"1_garage_texture\")", "problem": "Player 1's Unit is hard to see in its own Garage. The Garage floor uses the garage texture with no tint; its ramp tops out at (0.518, 0.272, 0.128) and renders as a light terracotta, close in hue to Team Orange (0.90, 0.45, 0.14). At every Player 1 spawn the orange Motorbike reads as a thin orange sliver on an orange-rust floor (left view of /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/v2_show_p1_appears_as_motorbike_f63.png and v2_show_garage_spawn_f123.png). Player 2's teal Buggy on the same floor stands out strongly (right view), because teal is the complementary hue. The same Map gives one Team a harder figure-ground read at the one place every spawn passes. The Unit is not hidden, so AC-13's sentence passes, but a player or the author will notice. The illustrated drawing paints the Garage a darker brick-rust that stays apart from the Team orange.", "fix": "In garage_floor.tres, add one tint line under the texture: albedo_color = Color(0.65, 0.65, 0.65, 1). This keeps the rust hue and the texture and only darkens the floor. Re-shoot the f63/f123 spawn poses. Keep the value at which the Orange Motorbike stands apart from the floor by brightness as clearly as the Teal Buggy does by hue, with the floor still lighter than the walls' 0.55 tint. The hidden Pad shares this material, but Base._ready() repaints it and it is invisible, so nothing else changes. No baseline is affected because compound_base.tscn is only in Map 01. The DESIGN's rule 'albedo_color white unless a tint is named' means the orchestrator must name this tint."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/marking.tres", "quote": "albedo_color = Color(0.782, 0.773, 0.739, 1)", "problem": "The depot ring is the only visible use of marking.tres: every Garage dash is listed in color_meshes and repainted with the Team material. Its pale paint sits on the cream salt flat and almost disappears from the chase camera. It shows as faint white strokes in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/lens-visual/v2_show_towers_centre_f585.png, is not readable in v2_show_depot_f651.png, and shows only as light grey dashes in v2_topdown_depot_40m.png. The illustrated drawing, the look of record for AC-10, draws the depot ring as a bold dark-brown dashed circle. The DESIGN block's 'pale neutral paint' differs from the drawing, and no open question covers it, so the orchestrator should decide. Low priority.", "fix": "Set marking.tres albedo_color to a dark neutral brown matching the drawing's ring, for example the scrap ramp's dark end Color(0.25, 0.16, 0.11, 1). Change nothing else: no texture, and roughness stays 1.0. This changes only the depot ring, which is neither a Team colour nor the Fuel Can red. If the orchestrator keeps the DESIGN's pale paint, record this as a known departure from the drawing in the evidence doc."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Palette against the illustrated drawing (topdown_map01_w330.png, v2_topdown_baseA/B_50m, v2_topdown_depot_40m, about 30 chase-camera frames)", "value": "Layout and hue families follow the drawing: warm tan sand, cream salt flat with cellular cracks, terracotta canyon rock, darker-brown ridge, light-aqua fords, dark Base walls, rust Garage floor, steel-grey depot tanks with a rust band, black tyre stacks, low rock boulders. The departures the story itself makes: navy sea (open question 16), Team-coloured water towers (open question 5), roofless Garage. Departures not covered by the story: no pale shallow-water rim at the shore, no tyre tracks (optional), all cover in one rust-box material, pale depot ring (issue 2).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10", "what": "Meshes and textures in the look's scenes and materials I read (water_canister.tscn, compound_base.tscn, map_01_dressing.tscn, map_01_depot.tscn, fuel_can.tscn, materials garage_floor/wall/marking/fuel_tank/rust/container/tower, textures garage/ford/scrap)", "value": "Only built-in meshes: CylinderMesh, SphereMesh, BoxMesh, PlaneMesh, TorusMesh, MultiMesh. Textures are NoiseTexture2D only. No imported mesh or texture.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Who wears the Team colours, judged in the frames (v2_units_flags_can_both_teams_sheet.png, f63, f189, f255, f321, f585, topdown_baseA/B)", "value": "Orange and Teal appear on: the Units (one Team colour each, the rest neutral; the Buggy's pennant takes its owner's accent), the four corner towers, the tank and its dome roof, the dashed rectangle, the Flags, and the HUD and choice-panel edges. Neither colour appears on the cover, the depot, the rock, the water, the containers, the tyres or the boulders. No model in the sheet mixes the two.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Fuel amber told apart from the Orange edge, both viewports", "value": "In v2_show_garage_spawn_f123.png and v2_show_towers_centre_f585.png the amber bar reads yellow inside the orange edge in the P1 view and inside the teal edge in the P2 view. The hit-point bar stays green.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11", "what": "Fuel Can red", "value": "fuel_can.tscn tank albedo is Color(0.78, 0.08, 0.1). It reads as an unmistakable red jerrican in every frame, including the 40 m bands. Nothing neutral is red: the depot tank bands are dark rust.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "The Flag as built (water_canister.tscn)", "value": "Team-coloured body r 0.28 m, h 0.72 m. Steel bands r 0.30 m, a steel dome lid, a steel base ring. Total height 0.94 m. Only the body is Team-coloured. It reads as a small version of the water tower's tank (cylinder, dark band, dome).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Cream heading cue while carrying (lens-visual count_movie_showcase_cream.log; v2_show_flags_taken_f1938.png; k4 cue_flag_crop.png)", "value": "38 to 60 cream pixels on every frame from 1860 to 1939 with the Flag carried. The patch stays visible above the drum.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12", "what": "Water tower (compound_base.tscn)", "value": "Tank spans y 8.3 to 13.3 (lowest point at least 8.0). Tank and dome are Team-coloured. Band, platform, legs and braces are dark steel. Lowest brace point is about 3.35 m (above 3.2). It reads as a classic water tower from the salt flat.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Each Base's water tower seen from the salt flat's corners and centre", "value": "v2_show_towers_north_west_f321, south_west_f387, north_east_f453, south_east_f519 and centre_f585: in both viewports the tank and Team-coloured corner towers are in view and not hidden, out to about 200 m.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "Flag, Fuel Can and Unit of each Team told apart at 40 m; Gyrocopter over salt water", "value": "In v2_leg_sand/salt_flat/canyon_road/ford bands, the orange and teal drums, the red Can and the Unit are all distinct. In v2_leg_channel_p1/p2_gyrocopter bands, both Gyrocopters read over the navy channel, the teal rotor clearly.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13", "what": "No Unit hidden from its own camera: Garage, under the tower, road bends, Gyrocopter over rock", "value": "f63/f123 (Garage), f189 (under the towers), f880, f1053 and f1198 (bends), f1553 and f1705 (Gyrocopter risen over canyon rock and ridge): the Unit is in view in every frame. In the Garage, P1's Orange Unit has low contrast against the floor (issue 1).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-13 (look review, not an AC sentence)", "what": "Figure-ground of the Orange Unit on the rust Garage floor at spawn", "value": "P1's Motorbike is a thin orange sliver on light rust (left view of f63/f123). P2's teal Buggy on the same floor stands out. One Team is disadvantaged at every spawn.", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-10/AC-13", "what": "Unit silhouettes by type from the 13 m chase camera", "value": "Motorbike: a thin upright sliver with the cream patch. Buggy: a roll cage on four big wheels. Truck: a wide block with a turret. Gyrocopter: a rotor line over a small body. All four are distinct, and the four kit models keep the concept sheet's silhouettes.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "Frame rate and draw calls", "value": "Not this lens. The frames I read do not measure it.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-15", "what": "Human coherence judgement", "value": "The author's call. My notes for it are in 'checked'.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Art-direction review only. I read frames and files and wrote nothing: the repo is read-only and so is my agent-memory folder under the repo.\n\nFRAMES READ, set beside design/source/map01_colored.png and assets/art/vehicles/vehicle-design.png:\n- lens-visual: topdown_map01_w330, topdown_baseA, v2_topdown_baseB_50m, v2_topdown_depot_40m, v2_units_flags_can_both_teams_sheet\n- lens-visual v2_show: panels_f59, p1_appears_as_motorbike_f63, garage_spawn_f123, under_towers_f189, gates_f255, the five tower views (f321, f387, f453, f519, f585), depot_f651, fords_f717, p2_bend_1_f880, p2_bend_4_f1053, p1_bend_3_f1198, p1/p2_over_rock_f1553, gyro_end_f1705, p1_takes_flag_of_p2_f1867, flags_taken_f1938\n- lens-visual other: showcase_flag_carried_own_colour_hidden_f1887, showcase_frame_eq_652..., v2_leg_sand_f200, v2_leg_canyon_road_f332, the ford/channel/salt/canyon 40 m bands, count_vis.log and count_movie_showcase_cream.log\n- implementers' frames: k5 noedge_main, k4 cue_flag_crop, k6 after_inside\n\nFILES READ: water_canister.tscn, compound_base.tscn, map_01_dressing.tscn, map_01_depot.tscn, fuel_can.tscn; materials garage_floor, wall, marking, fuel_tank, rust, container and tower; textures garage, ford and scrap; team_orange_material.tres, team_orange_edge.tres; the cover scene's material references.\n\nVERDICT ON COHERENCE: The Map is one coherent palette that follows the drawing. Warm tan sand, cream salt flat, terracotta canyon over a darker ridge, dark walls, rust, steel greys and a navy sea. The two Team colours, the red Cans and the aqua fords are the only saturated accents, which is the right hierarchy.\n- Strongest elements: the water towers as landmarks. They read from about 200 m and from every corner of the salt flat.\n- The Team-coloured corner towers announce each Base.\n- The four kit Units keep the concept sheet's silhouettes and skull decals in one Team colour each.\n- The red jerrican reads at a glance everywhere.\n\nTEAM COLOURS: They own exactly what they should: the Units, the corner towers, the tank and its dome, the dashed rectangle, the Flags, and the HUD and choice-panel edges. Nothing neutral wears them or the Fuel red. The rust band on the depot tanks is dark rust, not red. No prop has a Unit's silhouette: the cover is plain boxes. Nothing looks like a Flag that is not one. The depot posts are squat dark-steel cylinders 1.5 m wide, and the depot tanks are 5 m grey tanks; colour and scale separate both from the 0.56 m Team-coloured drum.\n\nBIGGEST DEPARTURES FROM THE DRAWING, most visible first (notes for AC-15; only the depot ring is filed as an issue):\n1. The shore. The navy sea is decided (open question 16), but the island now meets it with a hard polygon edge and no pale shallow-water rim. That glow is the drawing's signature (topdown_map01_w330, v2_leg_sand_f200 right view). Adding it needs a new mesh, which this DESIGN does not name: a follow-up.\n2. The Garage. It is a roofless dark pen with a cellular rust floor that reads like terracotta tiles. It rhymes with the salt-flat cracks instead of the drawing's corrugated rust shed (topdown_baseA, f63). The recipe was copied as the DESIGN required.\n3. The cover. Wrecks, long containers and scrap walls render as one identical rust box: container.tres equals rust.tres, and both use the scrap texture. The drawing has charcoal car-shaped wrecks and ribbed containers. A cheap option, if the orchestrator wants it: tint container.tres olive like the Base containers, so 'container' reads as one material.\n4. The salt flat. Its cracks are soft and wide rather than a crisp fine network, and there are no tyre tracks. The drawing's dotted tracks are optional in the DESIGN and would give the flat direction.\n5. The depot ring is pale (issue 2).\n6. The corner towers. They are untextured 6 m blocks of flat Team colour, the loudest masses in each Base and louder than the tank (f255, f321). They are correct in colour and a matter of taste.\n\nTASTE NOTES:\n- The Flag reads more as a banded oil drum than a water tank. The rhyme with the tower's tank carries the 'tank under the tank' idea. The tower's dome is Team-coloured while the Flag's lid is dark steel; painting the lid would tighten the rhyme, but apply_color reaches only body_mesh.\n- A carried Flag hides most of the carrier's own colour from its own camera: P1 sees a teal drum (f1887). AC-11's carve-out allows this, and the cream cue stays at 38 to 60 px.\n- The warm palette makes Orange the weaker Team for figure-ground: the Garage floor (issue 1) and the terracotta canyon under the Orange Gyrocopter (f1553 left). Teal's weakest ground is the light-aqua ford: the teal Motorbike reads mainly by its dark parts (f717 right). My estimate is about dE 30 between the ford and Teal, mostly by lightness.\n- The olive containers bring in a green that the drawing (slate containers) and the concept sheet lack. The DESIGN allows olive, and it sits well in the warm palette.\n- The depot tanks are glossy (metallic 0.3, roughness 0.5). This matches the drawing's shaded spheres.\n- The HUD status line sits over the Team tank at spawn (f59, f63). It has no backing, as before K5, and stays readable through its outline.\n\nAC-15 NOTES FOR THE AUTHOR (not decided here): coherent and recognisably the drawing's map. The things the author will most likely ask about are the missing shoreline glow, the Garage's look, the identical brown cover boxes, and whether the Flag should read more as 'water'.\n\nALSO OBSERVED, for the visual lens: the showcase's 'depot' frame= points at a frame of the fords staging (showcase_frame_eq_652...); f651 shows the depot.\n\nNOT COVERED: AC-14 numbers, the scenarios' mechanics, the code standards, the kit-merge internals, and the frozen-file and regression runs."}
