{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"StandardMaterial3D\" id=\"StandardMaterial3D_container\"]\nalbedo_color = Color(0.55, 1, 0.9, 1)   ...   [sub_resource type=\"StandardMaterial3D\" id=\"StandardMaterial3D_container_rib\"]\nalbedo_color = Color(0.38, 0.7, 0.62, 1)   ...   [sub_resource type=\"StandardMaterial3D\" id=\"StandardMaterial3D_rubber\"]\nalbedo_color = Color(0.07, 0.07, 0.075, 1)", "problem": "Map 01's dressing keeps three inline materials with colour literals. Eight dressing nodes use them instead of a material file under src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/ or a Team material: West and East ContainerNorth and ContainerSouth (MeshInstance3D), West and East ContainerRibs, and West and East TyreStacks (MultiMeshInstance3D). It is the only Map scene with a sub_resource colour. `grep -c albedo_color src/gameplay/maps/map_01/*.tscn src/gameplay/maps/ford.tscn` returns 3 for map_01_dressing.tscn and 0 for every other scene. The structure probe (look/lens-ac-headless/r2/probe_main.gd, run with `godot --headless --path <repo> -s probe_main.gd`) prints MATVIOL total=8, and all eight are these dressing nodes. Everything else in the Map (CSG, cover, depot, compound, water, fords and the Boulders and DepotPosts MultiMeshes) references materials/ files or the Team materials.", "fix": "Move the three sub-resources unchanged into material files under src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/, for example dressing_container.tres (keeping its ext_resource to textures/scrap.tres and its mapping parameters), dressing_container_rib.tres and dressing_rubber.tres. Then reference them through ext_resource from map_01_dressing.tscn and delete the inline sub-resources. No value changes, so the look and the shared mesh and material instancing stay the same."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn", "quote": "DESIGN 7: \"the depot's posts (about six, 1.5 m across, at about (+-7, -6), (+-6.4, 3.9), (+-5, 5.9))\"", "problem": "LOW severity, a deviation the orchestrator should record. I parsed the DepotPosts MultiMesh buffer from the .tscn. (Headless, MultiMesh.get_instance_transform() returns identity, so the buffer is the only reliable source.) Measured: the six posts are 1.5 m across. The (+-6.4, 3.9) and (+-5, 5.9) pairs are where the DESIGN puts them, but the first pair stands at world (+-7.80, -3.36), 2.76 m from the DESIGN's (+-7, -6). The DESIGN's spot is inside the layout's depot fuel tanks FuelTankNorthW and FuelTankNorthE (map_01_depot.tscn: cylinders of radius 2.5 centred at (+-6.81, -6.62), world AABB x[-9.31,-4.31] z[-9.12,-4.12]). So the posts were moved to avoid overlapping the tanks. The DESIGN position cannot be built without that overlap.", "fix": "No code change. The orchestrator records the deviation in the decision log and the evidence doc: DESIGN 7's (+-7, -6) post position lies inside the depot's north fuel tanks, so those posts stand at (+-7.8, -3.36), 2.25 m or more from every Fuel Can."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-1..AC-9 (layout regression)", "what": "dev07 regress (24 baselines; run through a copy of dev07.py writing to my scratch run-out)", "value": "ALL_OK=True: strict twenty identical with rc 0, soft four RESULT ok (all four also byte-identical)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1..AC-9 (layout regression)", "what": "dev07 new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover", "value": "map_layout ok checks=2 failed=0; map_edges ok 2/0; map_ford ok 1/0; map_bases ok 2/0 (exit_runs=24, exit_contacts=0); map_cover ok 1/0 (depot_takes=5)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-15 frames (scenario health)", "what": "dev07 new map_showcase map_legibility, headless", "value": "map_showcase RESULT ok checks=0 failed=0 moments=15 (road_done=true,true, rock_ticks=61,90, flag_ticks=167); map_legibility RESULT ok moments=6 worst_miss_m=0.80; no ERROR or WARNING", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "FROZEN / assets / launch / parse", "what": "dev07 frozen, assets, launch, parse", "value": "frozen: 9 of 9 OK; ASSETS UNCHANGED (concept kit untouched); launch: main scene --quit-after 120 rc 0 and driving_toy rc 0 with no ERROR or WARNING; parse rc 0 on 24 files", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 textures", "what": "The nine NoiseTexture2D files loaded at runtime and diffed against preflight-look/a/gl/recipes", "value": "All 9 byte-identical to the recipes, with readable sub_resource ids and no uid line. 512x512 seamless with mipmaps, except salt_span: 2048x388, seamless false, cellular type 2, seed 7. Seeds: sand 11, road 41, ford 61, sea 51, rock 23, ridge 31, scrap 71, garage 81.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 materials", "what": "Every map_01/materials/*.tres loaded: texture, filter, mapping, tint", "value": "BaseMaterial3D.TEXTURE_FILTER_LINEAR_WITH_MIPMAPS_ANISOTROPIC = 5, read at runtime; all textured materials use filter 5 and roughness 1.0. World triplanar scales: sand 1/32, road 1/32, ford 1/32, rock 1/32, ridge 1/32, garage_floor 1/16 (garage texture), sea 1/64, channel 1/64 (same texture and parameters as sea), wall/scrap/rust/container 1/16 (scrap texture), wall tint 0.55. salt_flat uses the plane's UVs (no triplanar, scale 1). Untextured as the DESIGN says: marking (0.782, 0.773, 0.739), tower (0.30, 0.31, 0.33, metallic 0.5), fuel_tank (0.64, 0.65, 0.64, metallic 0.3). No transparency anywhere (whether the ford needs it is a visual call).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 / AC-11 map meshes use material files", "what": "Every GeometryInstance3D of the Map, including CSG and MultiMesh, against materials/ or the Team materials", "value": "8 violations, all in map_01_dressing.tscn (inline container, container_rib and rubber materials); 0 elsewhere", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "AC-10 no new collision", "what": "Collision text of the pre-look copies (look/k2, k3, k6 orig) against now, plus the runtime count", "value": "compound_base, map_01_depot, map_01, water_canister and fuel_can: CollisionShape3D, body, Area3D, use_collision, layer and mask lines all SAME; map_01_dressing has 0. Runtime: compound StaticBody3D L1 32 shapes (16 per Base), zones L4 M2 2, Flags L8 M2 2, cliffs CSG L32 5, water L32 2, terrain L1 32, cover L1 12, map_01 L1 1, fords L0 M2 2, Fuel Cans L0 M18 9.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-10 dressing clearance", "what": "Base-local footprint of each prop (runtime AABB, with MultiMesh instances parsed from the .tscn buffer) against lanes (local x -5.5..5.5, z -40..7.2), the seats, the Fuel Cans and the canyon road polygon", "value": "Containers 3.50 m (North) and 4.10 m (South) from the lane; tyre stacks about 5.8 m or more; boulders 15 m or more; nearest seat 9.6 m; nearest Fuel Can 2.13 m (depot posts); dressing at least 21 m from the road and depot tanks at least 14.8 m; boulder tops 0.55 to 0.85 m (under 1 m); tyre stacks at (-109,-13) and (-131,12.4) and mirrored; containers at (-127.5,-11) 7x4 and (-112,11.6) 8x4, 2.5 m tall", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Team materials", "what": "team_orange_material.tres and team_teal_material.tres loaded", "value": "Orange (0.9, 0.45, 0.14) and Teal (0.18, 0.6, 0.58), roughness 0.7, metallic 0.05, vertex_color_use_as_albedo true, vertex_color_is_srgb true", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Bases", "what": "Base1 and Base2 color_material and every mesh wearing a Team material on the main scene", "value": "Base1 Orange, Base2 Teal; 22 painted meshes per Base (Pad, Tank as beacon, 4 corner towers, 14 dashes, Roof, the Flag's Body), all in the owner's colour; 0 Team-material meshes outside the Bases. The Roof is accepted by the orchestrator's decision. Walls stay on wall.tres; the Garage walls stay on wall.tres too, and only its floor carries the garage texture.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Units and models", "what": "split_screen.tscn Units, UnitStats.model, and painting through the real Unit.spawn()", "value": "Player1Unit Orange, Player2Unit Teal; the four UnitStats point at the *_kit_model.tscn scenes; 8 of 8 spawns paint Accent only, Neutral has no override, and no other Team mesh is on the Unit", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 greybox composition", "what": "Harness with --scenario=bases (probe_greybox.gd)", "value": "Units' team_material: player_1_body_material.tres and player_2_body_material.tres; model child motorbike_model.tscn; all four cached UnitStats.model are the greybox *_model.tscn; World holds GreyboxField, TerrainStandIns and FuelCans", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 UI", "what": "edge_style on the four UI instances and the scene defaults", "value": "P1 HUD and choice use team_orange_edge.tres (border (0.9,0.45,0.14), 3 px, draw_center false); P2 use team_teal_edge.tres; player_hud.tscn and unit_choice.tscn default edge_style null; HUD bar colours unchanged in the diff (doc lines only)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-11 Fuel Cans", "what": "Colours of the 9 Fuel Cans and the fuel_can.tscn diff", "value": "All 9 tanks Color(0.78, 0.08, 0.1); cap and handle (0.16, 0.15, 0.14) unchanged; fuel_can.tscn diff against HEAD is the one albedo line (fuel_can.gd changed in its doc comment only)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12 water tower", "what": "Tank and brace world bounds in both Bases", "value": "Tank CylinderMesh r 4, y 8.300 to 13.300 (lowest point 8.0 or above), beacon is the Tank; lowest brace point y 3.352 (above 3.2); leg colliders unchanged", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12 Flag", "what": "water_canister meshes and PickupZone", "value": "Body CylinderMesh r 0.28, h 0.72; widest part r 0.300 (bands); all meshes y 0.00 to 0.94; PickupZone sphere r 1.0 at y 0.6, layer 8, mask 2 (unchanged from the pre-look copy); near edge at carry z 1.40 against the Motorbike tail at z 1.360; water_canister.gd changed in doc comments only", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "K4 models", "what": "Each kit model scene in a headless probe after one frame", "value": "All four: Accent in group team_colour with 1 surface, Neutral in no group with 3 surfaces (4 per Unit), 2 MeshInstance3D. Scales 0.98, 0.72, 0.735, 0.66; rust_seed 11; Gyro position (0,0.8,-0.28) with the rise on (physics processing only for the Gyro); Truck offset z 0.1286 (orchestrator decision). Hull overhang past the collider: Motorbike tail +z 0.060 (accepted); Buggy 0.001; Truck 0.001; Gyro hull inside (-0.100 x), but its rotor reaches x +-2.219 (1.42 m each side) and -z 0.228.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-12 Motorbike heading cue", "what": "Kit builds with no remap against the model's build (colour histograms) and vertices in the patch box", "value": "Exactly one kit part matches (BoxMesh 0.36x0.02x0.28 at (0, 1.015, 0.03), key orange). Its 24 vertices move from Accent (white) to the lamp surface (cream (1.0, 0.86, 0.6)). No other Motorbike vertex changes: the motorbike kit has no flag or rust_orange part, so material_remap has no effect on it.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "K4 remaps", "what": "Buggy pennant and Truck drum", "value": "Buggy: 24 vertices of the flag colour (0.918, 0.420, 0.098) move into Accent (white tone). Truck: 106 vertices of rust_orange (0.698, 0.357, 0.149) become steel_dark (0.298, 0.310, 0.329). Gyrocopter unchanged.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "Scene cost", "what": "MeshInstance3D count per scene on the main scene", "value": "compound_base 44 per Base; water_canister 5 per Flag; fuel_can 3 per Can; map_01_depot 32; map_01_dressing 4 MeshInstance3D plus 7 MultiMeshInstance3D (28+12+4 per side, 6 posts); cover 12; water 3; terrain 1 MeshInstance3D plus 2 CSG; cliffs 5 CSG; ford 1 per ford; Unit models 2 each", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "base.tscn unchanged", "what": "git status / diff", "value": "base.tscn is not in the change set", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14", "what": "Windowed draw calls and frame rate", "value": "Not measured by this headless lens", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-13 / AC-15", "what": "Legibility at 40 m, tower visibility, Gyro visibility over rock, coherence", "value": "Visual and windowed checks, out of this lens's role", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Everything here was run headless and read-only, one Godot process at a time with timeouts. No Godot process of mine is left running.\n\n- **Regression:** a copy of dev07.py writing to my scratch run-out. regress is ALL_OK (24 of 24, the soft four also byte-identical). map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases and map_cover all end RESULT ok. map_showcase and map_legibility end RESULT ok headless. frozen, assets (unchanged), launch (clean) and parse (24 files) all pass.\n- **Probes:** two probes, look/lens-ac-headless/r2/probe_main.gd and probe_greybox.gd, outputs in r2/*.out.\n  - Textures: all nine loaded and checked against the preflight recipes (byte-identical).\n  - Materials: every map material's texture, filter (enum 5 read at runtime), triplanar, scale and tint.\n  - Team materials, the four UI edges and the scene defaults.\n  - Base paint per mesh: 22 per Base, none outside the Bases. The Roof is in Team colour by the orchestrator's decision.\n  - Tank and brace heights, the Flag's radius, height and PickupZone, and all nine Fuel Can colours.\n  - Units: Team materials on the main scene, and 8 of 8 spawns paint Accent only.\n  - Greybox composition: body materials, greybox models and UnitStats.model are put back.\n  - Kit models: groups, surface counts, scales, hovers and offsets, and hull and collider overhangs. Kit builds with no remap were diffed against each model's build to prove the Motorbike patch (24 vertices to lamp cream, nothing else), the Buggy pennant (24 vertices) and the Truck drum (106 vertices).\n  - Collision: the pre-look copies of the scenes (look/k2, k3, k6 orig) against now, all identical; the dressing has none.\n  - Dressing clearance: footprints from the runtime AABBs and from MultiMesh buffers parsed out of the .tscn (headless, MultiMesh transforms read as identity), measured against the lanes, seats, Fuel Cans and canyon road. Every prop is clear.\n  - Code: water_canister.gd and player_hud.gd changed in doc lines only. unit.gd's changes are the layout's speed cap; _swap_model() and _paint_team_colour() are untouched.\n- **Accepted by the orchestrator's decisions, so not raised:** the Roof dome in Team colour, the Truck's z offset of 0.1286 and the Motorbike's 0.06 m tail overhang.\n- **Information only:** the Gyrocopter's rotor overhangs its collider by 1.42 m on each side, which is the kit's design; its hull sits inside the collider.\n- **Two findings:**\n  1. map_01_dressing.tscn keeps three inline colour materials (8 nodes) instead of material files under materials/.\n  2. One pair of depot posts was moved 2.76 m from DESIGN 7's (+-7, -6), because that spot is inside the depot's fuel tanks. This needs recording, not a code change.\n- **Not measured (other lenses' role):** AC-14 (windowed draw calls and fps), AC-13 visual legibility and visibility, and AC-15."}
========== fix r2 gameplay 1
{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn"], "verification": ["Issue 3, before the fix (headless probe on 4.7.2, look/fix2-gameplay/probe_kit.gd, output in probe_before.out). The probe used a kit whose parts are built deferred, with _m set. KitMerge.get_or_build() returned a non-null Built with 0 accent and 0 neutral surfaces, hull AABB(INF, -INF) and hull.end (nan, nan, nan), and cached it (cache 0 -> 1). A KitUnitModel on that kit with rise_over_cliffs had 2 empty children and physics processing on. This confirms the defect.", "Issue 3, after the fix (probe_after.out). get_or_build() returned null on both attempts and the cache stayed at 0 -> 0. The new error 'KitMerge: the kit scene ... built no part the palette can fold, so no model is built.' printed once per attempt and once for the KitUnitModel. That KitUnitModel had 0 children and physics processing off. All four real kit models still build, with 2 children each.", "Hull extraction (_hull_of). The raw Built.hull of all four kits is identical to 6 decimals before and after, e.g. truck pos (-1.25, -0.06, -3.17) end (1.25, 1.994, 2.82). The whole probe output is identical (probe_pre_refactor.out vs probe_post_refactor.out).", "Issue 4. The Truck model's position went from (0, 0, 0.1286) to (0, 0, 0). Its hull z went from -2.201..2.201 to -2.330..2.073 (centre -0.129), which is the state the K4 slice measured. Motorbike, Buggy and Gyrocopter are unchanged (the Gyrocopter is still at (0, 0.8, -0.28)).", "Windowed side-view frame READ: look/fix2-gameplay/truck_side.png (1200x600, orthographic, screen right is the front). Top row, old offset: the model sits inside the translucent 2.4 x 1.6 x 4.4 collider box. Bottom row, now: the front bumper spikes reach about 0.13 m past the box front and the rear sits about 0.13 m inside.", "dev07.py import: 235 classes, none new or gone, no .uid sidecars copied. parse: rc=0 on 24 files.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, rc=0, no ERROR or WARNING (run twice).", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True, the strict twenty identical and the soft four RESULT ok (run twice: after the fixes and after the hull extraction).", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok, failed=0 (run twice).", "dev07.py frozen: every file OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "lint007.py all on kit_merge.gd and truck_kit_model.tscn: 0 declarations without a ## line, 0 ## lines over 100 columns. One function is flagged: _commit (45 lines, cc~10, LONG). It was flagged before this pass, and the tool counts the two inner classes after it as part of it; _commit itself is 16 lines. _build was flagged at cc~11 after the issue-3 check and is no longer flagged.", "Issue 5 source checked: preflight-look/b/ref/kit_merge.gd sets roughness 0.8 and metallic 0.1 for the neutral material (lines 78-79). The values in the repo are unchanged.", "Issue 1 text checked: the Team colours are identical in the material and edge files (Orange Color(0.9, 0.45, 0.14, 1) in both; Teal Color(0.18, 0.6, 0.58, 1) in both).", "Issue 2 text checked: motorbike_kit_model.tscn part_remap is size (0.36, 0.02, 0.28) at (0, 1.015, 0.03) -> key lamp. A 4.7.2 probe (look/fix2-gameplay/probe_set.gd) shows that Object.set on a missing property is silently ignored with no ERROR (get=<null>, has=false).", "Draw calls not measured in this pass: no mesh, material or node count changed (the hulls are identical and only the Truck model moved 0.13 m)."], "deviations": ["Issue 3 goes slightly beyond the proposed lines. The check was added as proposed (if surfaces.is_empty(): push_error naming the kit scene; return null, placed after the parts loop and before the hull). That pushed _build to cc~11, and lint007 flagged it. So the hull measure moved out of the parts loop into a new private static function, KitMerge._hull_of(surfaces). It measures the same transformed vertices from the folded surfaces, and the probe shows the hulls of all four kits are bit-identical. _build's doc now says it returns null when no part folds, and that get_or_build() then caches nothing. No public API, export, signal or data changed. If the orchestrator wants only the literal three lines, put the hull loop back into _build and accept cc~11.", "Issue 4 (SCOPE), truck_kit_model.tscn: the line 'offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286)' was removed. The lens preferred 'keep and record', but fix-pass rule (a) says a SCOPE issue is fixed by removing it unless that breaks an acceptance criterion. Removing it breaks none: (1) the design block names an offset only for the Gyrocopter; (2) no AC requires a model's hull to sit inside its collider; (3) the K4 slice measured and accepted the uncentred state (every ground model within 0.15 m, the Truck's front at 0.13 m); (4) no saved round-one issue asked for the offset (searched the scratch notes). The Truck's front bumper spikes now reach 0.13 m past its 4.4 m collider again. If the orchestrator would rather keep it, re-add that one line and record it in the design block and the decision log; I may not edit either.", "Issues 1 and 2 (design/rules.md) were not edited by me: design/ is read-only for this step. The working tree already contains both changes (git diff HEAD shows the Team-colour sentence replaced and the kit bullet added, worded differently from the issues). Issue 1's applied text matches the files.", "Finding on issue 2's applied text in design/rules.md: its last sentence, 'An edit to the kit that breaks one of these is reported as an error naming the kit scene', overstates what the code does. These cases pass with no message: a renamed steer_deg or pod_yaw_deg (skipped by 'if property in kit'); a renamed rust_seed (Object.set on a missing property does nothing, confirmed by the 4.7.2 probe); a renamed lamp, skull or screen key (the parts fold into the neutral surface at their albedo colour); a renamed steel key (the fallback accent material turns white); and a renamed flag or rust_orange key (the remap entry matches nothing). That last one is an AC-11 risk: the Buggy's pennant, kit colour about (0.92, 0.42, 0.10), would show near-Orange on either Team's Buggy. The issue's own proposed text kept the pose-property exception; the applied text dropped it. Suggested wording: '... is reported as an error naming the kit scene, except a renamed rust_seed, steer_deg or pod_yaw_deg property or a renamed lamp, skull, screen, steel, flag or rust_orange key, which the build does not notice (a renamed flag key would show the Buggy's pennant in its near-Orange kit colour on either Team).' Making those cases errors would add checks the DESIGN block does not name, so I did not build them (rule a).", "Issue 5: the new docs, like DARK_TONE's existing doc, cite 'the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run'. No Story 007 file was under production/qa/evidence/ during this pass, so the evidence doc needs to carry the variant C run (roughness 0.8, metallic 0.1).", "Late findings 1 and 2 (the depot ring marking; the base.gd 'the Lid keeps its cream' clause and the orphan line in water_canister.gd) were not touched: no lens in this pass names them. The runner's TD-009 hunks were not touched."], "blockers": [], "summary": "I fixed the three code issues in my files and verified them. Two of the five issues (both in design/rules.md) were not mine to apply: that file is read-only for this step, and the working tree already has both changes.\n\n1. Empty kit (DEFECT), src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd. Before: a kit whose parts are not built by the end of its _ready() gave a cached, empty, invisible model, and the Gyrocopter's rise used a hull with infinite bounds (end NaN) every tick, with no message. After: _build() reports 'KitMerge: the kit scene '%s' built no part the palette can fold, so no model is built.' and returns null. get_or_build() caches nothing, and KitUnitModel stays empty with physics processing off. The new check made lint007 flag _build (cc~11), so I moved the hull measure into a private _hull_of(); the four kits' hulls are bit-identical before and after.\n2. Material source (STANDARD), same file. The docs of NEUTRAL_ROUGHNESS and NEUTRAL_METALLIC now name their source, the look preflight's tested variant C. The values (0.8, 0.1) are unchanged and match the reference.\n3. Truck offset (SCOPE), src/gameplay/units/models/truck_kit_model.tscn. I removed 'offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286)' under fix-pass rule (a). The Truck model is back at the Unit's origin, with its hull 0.13 m ahead of the collider at the front as K4 accepted, and the side-view frame shows it. If you prefer to keep the offset, re-add that one line and record it.\n4. design/rules.md (issues 1 and 2). Issue 1's text matches the files. Issue 2's last sentence says every breaking kit edit is reported as an error, which is too broad: a renamed rust_seed, steer_deg or pod_yaw_deg property, or a renamed lamp, skull, screen, steel, flag or rust_orange key, gets no message. A renamed flag key would turn the Buggy's pennant near-Orange on either Team. Suggested wording is in the deviations.\n\nChecks after the edits: import and parse are clean, launch shows no ERROR or WARNING, regress is ALL_OK, the five map scenarios end RESULT ok, frozen and assets are unchanged, and lint flags only _commit, which was flagged before this pass. Scratch probes and the frame are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix2-gameplay/.", "complete": true}
