with its vertex, normal and colour checksums, every material, the positions (Gyrocopter (0, 0.8, -0.28)), scales, hulls, the Accent node in team_colour, and KitMerge's cache of 4.", "Typed palette check (after the edit): _palette_of() on a fake kit whose _m is {\"teal\": material, &\"orange\": material, \"not_a_material\": 5} returns keys [\"teal\", \"orange\"]. The StringName key is converted to String, the non-Material entry is skipped, and the dictionary is typed String (TYPE_STRING = 4) to Material.", "No windowed frame was taken: none of the four issues is visual, and the probe shows the drawn meshes, materials and transforms unchanged.", "No Godot process of mine is left running (checked with ps). Scratch artefacts are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix2b-gameplay/ (edit.py, probe_models.gd, run_probe.py, before.out, after.out, newmap.log, *.before copies)."], "deviations": ["Issue 3 (SCOPE, truck_kit_model.tscn 'offset = Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286)'): no edit in this pass, because the line is already gone. The previous fix pass removed it as its 'Issue 4 (SCOPE)' (scratch look/fix2-gameplay/edit.py, 05:21 local). The current file has no offset line (grep count 0), which matches the binding DESIGN 5: it names only the Gyrocopter's offset. Conflict for the orchestrator: production/session-logs/decision-log.md line 1335 (2026-10-03T02:15:26Z, 'Story 007: the Truck model's centring offset') still records 'Kept: truck_kit_model.tscn offset Vector3(0, 0, 0.1286)', which the file no longer matches. Effect of the removal, from the probe hull: the Truck's model spans z -2.330..2.073 in the Unit frame against the collider's -2.2..2.2. Its nose therefore overhangs the collider's front by about 0.13 m and is drawn that far inside a wall it stops against. No AC-10 to AC-15 names model clipping, so the removal breaks no acceptance criterion. The orchestrator either adds 'the Truck offset z 0.1286' to DESIGN 5 and the evidence doc and the one line is restored, or corrects the decision-log entry.", "Issue 2, minor: the copied key is converted with str(key) rather than the String(key) the issue named, so a StringName key (or any other key) converts safely. One untyped Dictionary local (kit_entries, with a comment) remains, holding the kit's own untyped _m as the source of the copy, as the kit declares it. Each value is tested with 'is Material' before 'as Material', because a cast of a non-object value to an object type is a runtime error. A kit whose _m has entries but no Material now gives the existing 'has no palette' error at once; before, such a palette passed the empty check. The author's four kits never reach that case."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 2 (gameplay) for Story 007's look: four issues handled in order. Issues 1, 2 and 4 are fixed. Issue 3's line was already removed by the previous pass, and the decision log still says it was kept. Nothing visible changed and no output changed: regress ALL_OK, the five Map 01 scenarios pass, launch is clean, frozen and assets are unchanged.\n\nISSUE 1 (STANDARD), src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd: the eight tuning exports now default to inert values.\n- rust_seed 11 -> 0\n- rise_mask 32 -> 0\n- rise_clearance 0.25 -> 0.0\n- rise_rate 6.0 -> 0.0\n- settle_rate 2.0 -> 0.0\n- rise_lead_seconds 0.4 -> 0.0\n- rise_lead_max 8.0 -> 0.0\n- rise_margin 2.0 -> 0.0\nDocs: rust_seed now says 'Required, with no default: each model scene stores it.' Each of the seven rise values now says 'Required, with no default, when rise_over_cliffs is set.' Before editing I confirmed that all four model scenes store rust_seed = 11, that gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn stores every rise value, and that nothing else creates a KitUnitModel.\n\nISSUE 2 (STANDARD), src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd: the palette is now typed.\n- _palette_of(): returned the kit's untyped _m as a bare Dictionary -> copies it once into a Dictionary[String, Material], skipping any value that is not a Material; an empty copy gives the existing 'has no palette' error.\n- _build(): the local 'palette: Dictionary' -> Dictionary[String, Material]; 'for key: Variant ... String(key)' -> 'for key: String ... key'.\n- _surface_for(), _material_of(), _tone_of(), _colour_of(): the 'palette: Dictionary' parameter -> Dictionary[String, Material]; in _material_of(), 'palette[group] as Material' -> 'palette[group]'.\n- Doc: the sentence 'The palette stays an untyped Dictionary in every function that reads it ... does not assign to a typed one.' is deleted, and the doc now says the palette is copied into a typed dictionary.\nThe mesh arrays and the part-remap entries stay untyped, as the issue allows.\n\nISSUE 3 (SCOPE), truck_kit_model.tscn: no change made. The offset line was already removed by the previous fix pass, so the file matches DESIGN 5. production/session-logs/decision-log.md:1335 still records the offset as 'Kept'. Without it the Truck's nose overhangs its collider by about 0.13 m. No AC is broken; this is listed as a deviation for the orchestrator to settle.\n\nISSUE 4 (STANDARD), kit_merge.gd class doc: '## 90 to 200 parts in its _ready() as MeshInstance3D ...' -> '## parts in its _ready() as MeshInstance3D ...'.\n\nNo change at run time: a before/after probe of the four model scenes shows identical built meshes (counts and checksums), materials, positions, scales, hulls and groups. The only differences are the unused rise values on the three types that never rise. A fake-kit check shows the typed copy converts a StringName key and skips a non-Material value. The lint reports nothing new.", "complete": true}
