{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/marking.tres"], "verification": ["dev07.py import: rc 0. Class cache 235 classes, none new, none gone; no .uid sidecars copied. The kit-scene load errors it prints come from the scratch copy, which has no assets/ folder.", "dev07.py parse: rc 0, 24 of 24 files ok.", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, no ERROR or WARNING lines.", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK. dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are byte-identical and the soft four end RESULT ok.", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: all five RESULT ok. Checks 2+2+1+2+1, 0 failed.", "Windowed top-down, 1200x1200, 40 m wide, centred on the depot, read: scratch fix2-art/top_depot_40m.png. The ring is now a bold dark dashed circle like the drawing's. Dash against salt: before (219,220,218), dE76 7 (lens-visual/v2_topdown_depot_40m.png); after (60,38,31), dE76 67.", "Windowed map_showcase movie at 1280x720, my own child, stopped after the depot moment (659 PNGs). Moments: garage_spawn 123, under_towers 189, towers_centre 585, depot 651. Read show_depot_f651.png and show_towers_centre_f585.png: the ring reads as dark painted dashes around the tanks in both views, apart from the Units and from the red Fuel Cans.", "Pixel diff against the lens frames. Depot f651, left view: 366 ring pixels went from (233,233,230) to (67,46,39), dE76 72. Garage spawn f123 and under towers f189: only 14 and 10 pixels per view changed, all of them the distant ring. So the Garage dashes, which also reference marking.tres but are repainted with the Team material through color_meshes, and the Garage floor are pixel-identical.", "lint007.py: not applicable. No .gd file changed in this pass.", "Draw calls: not re-measured (no map_fps run). One albedo value changed on an existing material, with no node, mesh, surface or material resource added.", "No Godot window was left open (ps). Only children I started were run or stopped."], "deviations": ["ISSUE 4 (art, garage_floor.tres tint): NOT applied; this needs an orchestrator decision. The DESIGN says 'albedo_color white unless a tint is named', the issue itself says the orchestrator must name the tint, and the rulings and late findings do not name it. Fix-pass rule (a) forbids adding undesigned data unless it restores an AC, and measurement shows it restores none. (1) The rendered floor in f63 and f123, both views, about 3,300 to 3,800 rust pixels each, is median (133,76,49) L* 38.6, 90th percentile (141,80,50) L* 40.7: a mid rust, not light terracotta. (2) The drawing's Garage (map01_colored.png, both Bases) is stripes (154,73,34) L* 40.8 and ribs (128,61,28) L* 34.0, at the same hue angle, about 50 degrees. The floor already sits inside the drawn range, so AC-10 and AC-11's 'Garage rust, as drawn' are met. (3) The Orange Motorbike against the floor is dE76 45.4 (42.1 against the 90th percentile), standing apart by brightness (delta L* about 30). The Teal Buggy is 60.6. Both are far above the 25 bar. (4) The proposed 0.65 tint gives (110,61,39) L* 31.3, darker than the drawing's darkest rib, and moves the floor from about dE 11 to about dE 20 from the drawing. The issue's premise is measurably wrong: the drawing's own Garage is dE 33.8 from the rendered Orange, nearer to it than our floor is. (5) The 'thin sliver' read is the kit Motorbike's narrow rear silhouette at 13 m, which a floor tint does not change. If the author still wants more separation, the orchestrator names the tint; 0.65 gives dE 53.7.", "ISSUE 5 (art, marking.tres), applied under late finding (1), with a different value from both examples. albedo_color changed from Color(0.782, 0.773, 0.739, 1) to Color(0.188, 0.085, 0.035, 1). Roughness 1.0 kept and no texture added. Source: the drawing's depot-ring ink (59,28,13), sampled from map01_colored.png, divided by 1.48 in linear space. That is DESIGN 2's own calibration rule for the nine ramps, so the lit render matches the drawing (predicted dE 1.2). The late finding's example (0.25,0.24,0.22) renders grey, dE 25 from the drawing's ink; the issue's (0.25,0.16,0.11) gives dE 10. The new value is neither Team colour (dE 71.6 from the rendered Orange) nor the Fuel Can red. Before copy: scratch fix2-art/marking.before.tres. The file sits in an untracked directory, so git diff HEAD cannot show it.", "ISSUES 1 and 2 (engine and standards SCOPE, WaterTower/Roof in color_meshes): no change, per the orchestrator's ruling ('keep it in color_meshes'). base.gd's three mentions already describe the ruled state: the AC-11 sentence, the WaterTower paragraph and the color_meshes doc. Only the binding design block still omits the roof, and the orchestrator's ruling covers updating it.", "ISSUE 3 (visual, channel.tres): no code change. DESIGN 2 binds the navy sea recipe; I confirmed channel.tres carries the sea texture and the sea's parameters (world triplanar, 1/64). DESIGN 5 binds the 0.68 accent tone. I cannot write production/, so the orchestrator should record in the Story 007 evidence doc that this is the weakest legibility pair: Teal Gyrocopter over the channel water at 40 m, body dE76 30.1 to 32.1, rotor blade 21.4 to 22.7 (below 25), against 66.9 to 69.9 for the Orange Gyrocopter. PNGs: scratch look/lens-visual/v2_leg_channel_p2_gyrocopter_f134.png and v2_leg_channel_p2_gyrocopter_band.png.", "Late finding (2): no 'cream' clause remains in base.gd (grep finds none). No lens in this pass names the water_canister.gd orphan line, so it is untouched (rule g). Late finding (3): the runner was not touched.", "Observation, not from this pass: in the f585 and f651 diffs against the 01:10 lens frames, Unit pixels also changed, because map_showcase's choreography was edited in later fix passes. f123 and f189 are pixel-identical apart from the ring, so Unit materials are unchanged. The retained frame set should be shot from the current build."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Of the five issues in fix pass 2, only the depot ring needed a change in the repo; the other four end with no edit, each for a stated reason, and nothing is blocked.\n\n**Applied**\n- **Issue 5, depot ring:** in `/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/marking.tres`, `albedo_color` went from `Color(0.782, 0.773, 0.739, 1)` to `Color(0.188, 0.085, 0.035, 1)`, under late finding (1).\n  - **Source:** the value is the drawing's ring ink, put through DESIGN 2's own \u00f71.48 linear calibration so it renders as drawn.\n  - **Result:** the ring now reads as the drawing's bold dark dashed circle. Against the salt it went from dE 7 to dE 67 top-down, and to dE 72 from the chase camera.\n  - **Nothing else changed:** the Garage dashes, which share this material, are still repainted in the Team colour, and the Garage frames are pixel-identical apart from the distant ring.\n\n**Not applied**\n- **Issue 4, Garage floor tint:** I measured it and did not add the 0.65 tint.\n  - **Floor already matches the drawing:** it renders (133,76,49), inside the drawing's own Garage range.\n  - **Motorbike already stands out:** the Orange Motorbike sits at dE 45 against the floor, well above the 25 bar.\n  - **Tint would move away from the drawing:** it would make the floor darker than the drawing's darkest stripe.\n  - **No design authority:** DESIGN 2 needs any tint to be named, and none was.\n\n  The orchestrator decides; 0.65 would give dE 54.\n- **Issues 1\u20132, water-tower roof:** unchanged, as your ruling says. `base.gd` already describes the roof as Team-coloured; only the design block still needs your update.\n- **Issue 3, Teal Gyrocopter over the channels:** no code change, since DESIGN 2 and 5 bind both the colour and the tone. You need to record it in the evidence doc as the weakest legibility pair: body dE 30\u201332, rotor blade 21\u201323. The PNGs are in `look/lens-visual/`.\n\n**Checks after the edit**\n- `import`, `parse`, `launch`, `frozen` and `assets` are clean.\n- `regress` is ALL_OK.\n- The five map scenarios all pass.\n- I read three windowed frames: top-down depot, depot moment, salt-flat centre.\n- Draw calls were not re-measured, but the edit adds no node, mesh or material.\n- Scratch work (the chain script, its log and the frames) is in `look/fix2-art/`.", "complete": true}
