{"files_created": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/dressing_container.tres", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/dressing_container_rib.tres", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/dressing_rubber.tres"], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn"], "verification": ["Issue 1 baseline before any edit: the fix1-art generator re-emitted map_01_dressing.tscn byte for byte (cmp: REGEN IDENTICAL), and the lens probe (look/lens-ac-headless/r2/probe_main.gd, headless) printed MATVIOL total=8, all eight from the three inline materials.", "After the edit the lens probe prints MATVIOL total=0. grep -c albedo_color on map_01_dressing.tscn: 3 -> 0, so every Map 01 scene is now 0.", "Values unchanged: the [resource] body of each new .tres matches the removed sub_resource body line for line (dressing_container, dressing_container_rib and dressing_rubber: SAME VALUES).", "Scene diff (look/fix2-art-r2/before/map_01_dressing.tscn -> the repo file) shows only the expected changes: the header ext_resources, three sub_resources removed, and four 'material =' lines. Mesh, MultiMesh and node lines are byte-identical.", "dev07 import rc=0: 235 classes, none new or gone, no .uid sidecars copied. Its noisy lines are the scratch copy's missing assets/, as designed.", "dev07 parse: 24 files ok.", "dev07 launch: main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames, noisy=[].", "dev07 frozen: all OK. dev07 assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED.", "dev07 regress: ALL_OK=True (strict twenty identical, soft four RESULT ok).", "dev07 new: map_layout ok checks=2 failed=0; map_edges ok 2/0; map_ford ok 1/0; map_bases ok 2/0; map_cover ok 1/0.", "Windowed main-scene draw calls at the spawn frame (both views, frames 60, 90 and 120): 299 -> 299. Objects 830 -> 830, primitives 51,370 -> 51,370.", "Pixel identity (headless compare.gd on the PNG data): two before renders were identical, so the render is deterministic. Before vs after was IDENTICAL for a 40 m top-down of Base A (1200x1200), Base B (1200x1200) and the main-scene frame (1280x720).", "Frames read: look/fix2-art-r2/after_top_west1.png (olive ribbed containers, black tyre stacks, Orange corner towers and water tower) and after_main.png (Orange and Teal views, containers and tyres visible in both).", "Scene object count is unchanged: 4 MeshInstance3D and 7 MultiMeshInstance3D (56 ribs, 24 tyres, 8 boulders, 6 posts).", "lint007 all on the four files: 0 functions flagged, 0 undocumented declarations, 0 long ## lines.", "Nothing in src/ or tools/ still references the removed ids StandardMaterial3D_container, StandardMaterial3D_rubber or 3_scrap_texture.", "Issue 2 measured from the files: the DESIGN's spot (+-7, -6) is 0.650 m from the FuelTankNorthWest and FuelTankNorthEast centres at (+-6.8115, -6.6222), inside their 2.5 m radius. The built posts at (+-7.8, -3.36) are 3.409 m from those centres and 0.099 m clear of the 2.56 m band. They stand 2.76 m from the DESIGN's spot and 8.49 m from the depot centre, on the 9 m ring. The closest any of the six posts comes to a Fuel Can spot is 3.52 m, centre to centre (the (+-5, 5.9) pair to (+-3, 3)).", "No Godot process of mine is left running (ps count 0)."], "deviations": ["Issue 1: I created three new files under src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/ (dressing_container.tres, dressing_container_rib.tres, dressing_rubber.tres), the names the lens gave. The FILES list names materials/*.tres only as edits to existing files, and fix-pass rule (a) bars files the DESIGN block does not name. Why I did it anyway: the layout design the look builds on (design.txt section 5.0) requires every Map 01 mesh to reference a shared .tres per surface kind under materials/, 'never a colour written into a node or a sub_resource of a scene; a slice creates the .tres it needs the first time'. So the fix restores that rule and adds no behaviour. No existing file could take these materials without changing the look: container.tres, rust.tres and scrap.tres are the untinted rust scrap that DESIGN 2 fixes for the cover, there is no rubber material, and tower.tres would make the tyres grey metal. If the orchestrator rejects the new files, the fallback is container.tres for the containers and wall.tres for the ribs (the containers turn rust instead of the drawing's grey-olive), and the tyres would still need a material file of their own.", "Issue 2 (no code change; for the orchestrator's decision log and evidence doc): DESIGN 7's depot posts at (+-7, -6) cannot be built, because that spot is 0.65 m from the centres of the north fuel tanks (FuelTankNorthWest and FuelTankNorthEast, radius 2.5, at (+-6.8115, -6.6222)), inside them. The north pair stands at (+-7.8, -3.36), 2.76 m from the DESIGN's spot, 0.1 m clear of the tank band, on the 9 m depot ring. The other four posts are where DESIGN 7 puts them. The closest any post comes to a Fuel Can spot is 3.52 m centre to centre. I could not reproduce the lens's figure of '2.25 m or more', so the record should state which distance it means.", "Observation only, nothing changed: the earlier fix2-art round (05:39) made materials/marking.tres a dark brown, Color(0.188, 0.085, 0.035). Late finding 1 gave Color(0.25, 0.24, 0.22) as its example. No lens in this pass named the marking. Late finding 2 (the stale clause in base.gd and the orphan line in water_canister.gd's class doc) was not named by a lens either, so I left both, per rule (g)."], "blockers": [], "summary": "I fixed both issues in order. The look did not change: frames and draw calls are identical before and after, and every check passes.\n\nIssue 1 (STANDARD, map_01_dressing.tscn), fixed. The scene's three inline StandardMaterial3D sub-resources now live in three shared material files. They are referenced through ext_resource, and no value changed.\n\n- **map_01_dressing.tscn, before:** an ext_resource to textures/scrap.tres plus inline StandardMaterial3D_container (scrap texture, tint Color(0.55, 1, 0.9)), StandardMaterial3D_container_rib (tint Color(0.38, 0.7, 0.62)) and StandardMaterial3D_rubber (Color(0.07, 0.07, 0.075), roughness 0.95). BoxMesh_container_7m, BoxMesh_container_8m, BoxMesh_rib and TorusMesh_tyre used them as SubResource. The file was 148 lines.\n- **After:** ext_resources 3_dressing_container, 4_dressing_container_rib and 5_dressing_rubber point at materials/dressing_container.tres, dressing_container_rib.tres and dressing_rubber.tres. The four meshes use ExtResource, the inline sub-resources are gone, and the scrap texture is now referenced only by the two container material files. The file is 128 lines; the multimeshes and nodes are unchanged.\n- **The new files** follow the format of wall.tres and tower.tres. I re-emitted the scene from an edited copy of the K6 generator at look/fix2-art-r2/gen_dressing.py, not by an engine re-save.\n- **Results:**\n  - The lens probe's MATVIOL count went from 8 to 0.\n  - Draw calls at the spawn frame were 299 before and after.\n  - Top-down frames of both Bases and the main-scene frame are pixel-identical before and after.\n  - regress ALL_OK; the five map scenarios pass; launch, frozen and assets are clean.\n\nCreating the three files departs from the FILES list (which allows only edits to existing material files) and from fix-pass rule (a), which bars files the DESIGN block does not name. I did it because the layout design's rule 5.0 says to create such files and no existing file fits without changing the look. It is recorded as a deviation for your decision.\n\nIssue 2 (DESIGN, depot posts), confirmed with no code change. The DESIGN's spot (+-7, -6) is inside the north fuel tanks. The posts stand at (+-7.8, -3.36), 2.76 m from that spot and 0.1 m clear of the tank band; the numbers are in the deviations for your decision log.\n\nScratch evidence is in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/look/fix2-art-r2/: chain.log, probe_before.log, probe_after.log, the before_*.png and after_*.png frames, and before/map_01_dressing.tscn.", "complete": true}
