dards and scope review of the look's change set against the DESIGN block, with no Godot run. A trailing /tech-debt skill block with no subcommand was also in the prompt. Its Phase 1 would end in 'FAIL - missing required subcommand' with no scan, so I ran no tech-debt mode and did the verification the workflow task asked for.\\n\\nRead in full: kit_merge.gd, kit_unit_model.gd, map_fps.gd, the diffs of base.gd, water_canister.gd, fuel_can.gd, unit.gd, greybox_field.gd, split_screen.gd/.tscn, player_hud.gd, unit_choice.gd/.tscn, fuel_can.tscn, the four UnitStats files and the runner, the four kit model scenes, the Team materials, the HUD edge styles, water_canister.tscn, compound_base.tscn (tower, color_meshes, dash, mesh sections), 4 textures, all 20 materials, and the heads and function lists of map_showcase and map_legibility.\\n\\nChecked: ## docs on every declaration, 100-column wrapping, static typing, declaration order, naming, literals, singleton and autoload, gameplay-to-UI and src-to-tools references, prints, vocabulary, function sizes, tool sizes, frozen files, must-not-change files, uid lines and ids, class cache, scenario registration. The only avoided-vocabulary hit is the existing 'Player colour' heading in split_screen.gd, which the look did not add.\\n\\nScope calls made from the orchestrator's records, not flagged:\\n- The Team-coloured Roof dome on the water tower, painted through color_meshes. Not in the DESIGN, but logged as a deliberate ruling in log-decisions-4.sh.\\n- The runner's TD-009 held-key hunks (_send_key, _reassert_held_keys, the set_key condition). Logged as kept: the layout half's design 3.4, verified there. The register's TD-009 entry was not updated in this change, which the orchestrator may want to resolve.\\n- The three dressing material files (dressing_container, dressing_container_rib, dressing_rubber). Not named in the DESIGN, but implied by DESIGN 7 and neutral.\\n- Doc-only edits to water_canister.gd and fuel_can.gd, which keep the docs true.\\n- Warm-up in SplitScreen._ready() and the KitUnitModel box-query rise: both consistent with DESIGN 5, which leaves the mechanism to the slice.\\n\\nNOT_VERIFIED, not run or not read: regress and the five map scenarios, windowed frames, draw calls and frame rate, MeshInstance3D counts, colour fidelity to the drawings (the visual lens's job), the bodies of map_showcase and map_legibility beyond their heads and function lists, map_kit.gd, the cover, cliffs, terrain, water and ford scenes (layout files), the MultiMesh transform data in map_01_dressing.tscn, and the road, rock, ridge and garage textures."}
