{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DEFECT", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_merge.gd", "quote": "## straight, the Gyrocopter's pod forward): the pose KitUnitModel's model_scale and offset fit.", "problem": "KIT_POSE sets steer_deg and pod_yaw_deg before the kit builds, but the doc names the wrong Unit. I loaded the four kit scenes. pod_yaw_deg is exported by the Truck kit (exports: pod_yaw_deg, pod_pitch_deg, steer_deg, rust_seed), and the Gyrocopter kit does not export it (exports: rotor_yaw_deg 25, rotor_tilt_deg 6, rust_seed). So the pose is not applied to the Gyrocopter at all: its rotor keeps the kit's authored yaw and tilt, and the Truck's pod keeps pod_pitch_deg 22. The comment is the only statement of the contract and it misleads whoever edits the kit.", "fix": "Correct the comment to say that steer_deg is zeroed on the Motorbike, Buggy and Truck kits and pod_yaw_deg on the Truck kit (the pod aimed forward), and that the Gyrocopter's rotor and the Truck's pod pitch keep the kit's authored pose. Change nothing in the code."}, {"kind": "STANDARD", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/units/models/kit_unit_model.gd", "quote": "@export_flags_3d_physics var rise_mask: int = 0", "problem": "The docs on rise_mask, rise_clearance, rise_rate, settle_rate, rise_lead_seconds, rise_lead_max and rise_margin say 'Required, with no default, when rise_over_cliffs is set', but _ready() validates none of them (it just creates the box and the query and enables physics). A gyrocopter_kit_model.tscn that sets rise_over_cliffs and omits rise_mask or rise_rate silently never rises (query mask 0, move_toward at rate 0), so the Gyrocopter model sinks into rock with no error. The project's pattern (Unit, PlayerHud, UnitChoice _first_problem()) is to push_error on a missing required export. The rust_seed doc has the same 'Required' claim with a silent default of 0.", "fix": "In _ready(), when rise_over_cliffs is set and rise_mask is 0 or rise_rate, settle_rate, rise_lead_seconds or rise_lead_max is not above 0 or rise_clearance or rise_margin is negative, push_error naming this node and the unset export, and leave physics processing off. No other behaviour changes."}, {"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "quote": "NodePath(\"Garage/Marking/Dash14\"), NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\")]", "problem": "The DESIGN (K2) names for base.gd's new export only 'its four corner-tower meshes and the marking'. The water tower's Tank is painted as the beacon. WaterTower/Roof (a 4 m radius hemisphere over the tank) is a nineteenth Team-painted mesh that the design does not name. Measured at run time on the loaded Map: each Base's color_meshes is 19 (4 towers + 14 dashes + Roof), and each Base paints 22 meshes in all (+ pad, beacon, Flag body). base.gd's class doc and the color_meshes doc were written around it ('and on the water tower's roof', 'its Roof (one of color_meshes)').", "fix": "Remove NodePath(\"WaterTower/Roof\") from color_meshes in compound_base.tscn (the roof then keeps its tower.tres steel) and drop the roof sentences from the base.gd class doc and the color_meshes doc. If the orchestrator wants the roof Team-coloured as a drawing detail, record that as a design decision instead."}, {"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/materials/marking.tres", "quote": "albedo_color = Color(0.188, 0.085, 0.035, 1)", "problem": "The DESIGN says 'The depot ring marking a pale neutral paint (no texture)'. marking.tres is a dark brown (0.188, 0.085, 0.035), and the depot's RingMarking dashes (Dash01 to Dash20 in map_01_depot.tscn) use it directly. The look of record (design/source/map01_colored.png, read at the depot) draws the ring as a dark-brown dotted ring on the pale salt flat, so the DESIGN text and the drawing disagree and the implementation followed the drawing without saying so (the file was last edited late, 05:39).", "fix": "The orchestrator decides. Either set a pale neutral albedo_color here (for example Color(0.85, 0.83, 0.78, 1)) to follow the DESIGN, or amend the DESIGN line to the drawing's dark brown and keep the file. Nothing else changes."}, {"kind": "FIDELITY", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_dressing.tscn", "quote": "buffer = PackedFloat32Array(1, 0, 0, -7.8, 0, 1, 0, 0.6, 0, 0, 1, -3.36, 1, 0, 0, 7.8", "problem": "The DESIGN puts the depot's posts at about (+-7, -6), (+-6.4, 3.9), (+-5, 5.9). The second and third pairs match exactly, but the first pair stands at (+-7.8, -3.36): 2.76 m from (+-7, -6) and about 1.6 m from the drawing's dot at roughly (+-6.5, -4.9). I could not tell whether a lane or Fuel Can clearance forced the move (not recorded). The headless run cannot read the MultiMesh back (the dummy renderer returns zeros), so the placement was read from the buffer text only.", "fix": "Set the first pair of instances to (-7, 0.6, -6) and (7, 0.6, -6), or record the clearance reason next to the buffer and in the evidence doc."}, {"kind": "SCOPE", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/design/rules.md", "quote": "- Since story 007 the four Units' models are the author's own concept kit under `assets/art/vehicles/`", "problem": "design/rules.md is the author's design record, and the DESIGN names no edit to it. The Team-colour bullet rewrite replaces text that said story 007 would make the recolour data, which is fine. The new kit-dependency bullet (the kit scripts' _m keys, rust_seed, steer_deg, pod_yaw_deg, the tank-top plate) is implementation documentation that the look design routes to the evidence doc ('note that dependency in the evidence doc').", "fix": "Move the kit-dependency bullet into the Story 007 evidence doc and remove it from design/rules.md, or have the orch